berfabric/cyberware-frontx/statuses/33a3f4ebb0ea48d949525b5e695119afb6fb9f39"}},"author_association":"NONE","auto_merge":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},"source_issue_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/comments/3935746811","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/174#issuecomment-3935746811","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/174","id":3935746811,"node_id":"IC_kwDOQBxSA87qlrr7","user":{"login":"qodo-code-review[bot]","id":151058649,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-20T16:00:44Z","updated_at":"2026-02-20T16:00:44Z","body":"<h3>Review Summary by Qodo</h3>\n\nReplace prek with husky for git hook management\n\n<code>✨ Enhancement</code>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<h3>Walkthroughs</h3>\n\n<details open>\n<summary>Description</summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n<pre>\n• Replace prek with husky and lint-staged for git hooks\n• Remove prek dependency, reducing dependency surface\n• Implement custom lint-staged checks script for validation\n• Add husky pre-commit hook with file size and architecture checks\n</pre>\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Diagram</summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n>\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  prek[\"prek dependency\"]\n  husky[\"husky + lint-staged\"]\n  checks[\"lint-staged-checks.mjs\"]\n  precommit[\".husky/pre-commit\"]\n  \n  prek -- \"replaced by\" --> husky\n  husky -- \"uses\" --> checks\n  husky -- \"uses\" --> precommit\n  checks -- \"validates\" --> files[\"files: trailing-whitespace, end-of-file, JSON, YAML\"]\n  precommit -- \"runs\" --> filesize[\"file size check\"]\n  precommit -- \"runs\" --> archcheck[\"architecture check\"]\n```\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<h3>File Changes</h3>\n\n<details>\n<summary>1. package.json\n <code> Dependencies </code> <code> +16/-5 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Update dependencies and scripts for husky\n><pre>\n>• Remove <b><i>@j178/prek</i></b> from devDependencies\n>• Add <b><i>husky</i></b> and <b><i>lint-staged</i></b> as devDependencies\n>• Replace <b><i>prek:install</i></b> and <b><i>prek:run</i></b> scripts with <b><i>prepare</i></b> script for husky\n>• Remove <b><i>postinstall</i></b> prek hook\n>• Add <b><i>lint-staged</i></b> configuration for file validation checks\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/174/files#diff-7ae45ad102eab3b6d7e7896acd08c427a9b25b346470d7bc6507b6481575d519'> package.json\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>2. .pre-commit-config.yaml\n <code>⚙️ Configuration changes</code> <code> +0/-26 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Remove prek configuration file\n><pre>\n>• Remove entire prek configuration file\n>• Migrate all prek hooks to husky-based approach\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/174/files#diff-63a9c44a44acf85fea213a857769990937107cf072831e1a26808cfde9d096b9'> .pre-commit-config.yaml\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>3. .husky/pre-commit\n <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +13/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Add husky pre-commit hook script\n><pre>\n>• Create new husky pre-commit hook script\n>• Add file size validation (&gt;500KB check, excluding package-lock.json)\n>• Run lint-staged for file quality checks\n>• Run architecture check via npm script\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/174/files#diff-d2bc4bbf14eadc292d84e0ef5f7a93115c23557f533809fc80b896934291529d'> .husky/pre-commit\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary><ins><strong>View more (2)</strong></ins></summary><br/>\n<details>\n<summary>4. scripts/lint-staged-checks.mjs\n <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +71/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Add custom lint-staged validation checks script\n><pre>\n>• Create new script to replace prek built-in hooks\n>• Implement trailing-whitespace check with line-by-line validation\n>• Implement end-of-file newline check\n>• Implement JSON validation using native JSON.parse\n>• Implement YAML validation using js-yaml library\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/174/files#diff-1063eb8e02345a7969b0ffe9e387b8d671c6bddef745f0502ee66d537d5689b1'> scripts/lint-staged-checks.mjs\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>5. eslint.config.js\n <code>⚙️ Configuration changes</code> <code> +1/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Exclude husky directory from linting\n><pre>\n>• Add <b><i>.husky/**</i></b> to eslint ignores list\n>• Prevent linting of husky hook files\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/174/files#diff-a32a0887ed9d1d707bbb3b845b7df7fd40e673c47e7b60a3ebd896b68d3b8839'> eslint.config.js\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n<a href=\"https://www.qodo.ai\"><img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/qodo-logo.svg\" width=\"80\" alt=\"Qodo Logo\"></a>","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/comments/3935746811/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":484649,"client_id":"Iv1.8b06d3cf5deea057","slug":"qodo-code-review","node_id":"A_kwHOCuzIt84AB2Up","owner":{"login":"qodo-ai","id":183290039,"node_id":"O_kgDOCuzItw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183290039?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai","html_url":"https://github.com/qodo-ai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Qodo Code Review","description":"### The AI Code Review Platform\r\n\r\n## Get Started\r\nSimply sign into Github and click the \"Configure\" button. Check out our documentation for more info: https://docs.qodo.ai/get-started.\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\nQodo automatically reviews every GitHub pull request, identifies logic bugs, edge cases, security issues, and code quality problems, and provides actionable suggestions your team can apply immediately.\r\n\r\nInstall in minutes. Integrates seamlessly into your existing workflows.\r\n\r\n## Qodo is designed for developers who:\r\n- Handle frequent pull requests and need reliable review coverage\r\n- Balance code quality with fast delivery\r\n- Work in complex, multi-repo systems\r\n- Use AI-generated code and need stronger guardrails\r\n- Build production software where reliability matters\r\n\r\n## Qodo Capabilities\r\n- ## Automated PR Analysis\r\n  - Reviews every pull request automatically\r\n  - No manual trigger required\r\n\r\n- ## Context-Aware Code Review\r\n  - Understands cross-file changes\r\n  - Detects architectural inconsistencies\r\n\r\n- ## Actionable Suggestions\r\n  - Concrete code fixes\r\n  - Clear explanations\r\n  - Prioritized feedback\r\n\r\n- ## Security & Reliability Checks\r\n  - Identifies risky patterns\r\n  - Reduces attack surface area","external_url":"https://www.qodo.ai/","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","created_at":"2023-11-16T16:18:38Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T15:53:40Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"read","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","discussion_comment","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review_comment","push"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/comments/3935765436","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/174#issuecomment-3935765436","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/174","id":3935765436,"node_id":"IC_kwDOQBxSA87qlwO8","user":{"login":"qodo-code-review[bot]","id":151058649,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-20T16:04:34Z","updated_at":"2026-02-20T16:20:09Z","body":"<h3>Code Review by Qodo</h3>\n\n<code>🐞 Bugs (4)</code>  <code>📘 Rule violations (1)</code>  <code>📎 Requirement gaps (0)</code>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<br/>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/action-required.png\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Action required\">\n\n<details>\n<summary>  ✅ 1.  <s>lint-staged failure masked</s> <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>✓ Correctness</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>The pre-commit script runs <b><i>npx lint-staged</i></b> and then <b><i>npm run arch:check</i></b> without stopping on\n>errors. If lint-staged fails but arch:check succeeds, the hook exits 0 and the commit incorrectly\n>passes.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[.husky/pre-commit[R12-13]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/174/files#diff-d2bc4bbf14eadc292d84e0ef5f7a93115c23557f533809fc80b896934291529dR12-R13)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+npx lint-staged\n>+npm run arch:check\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details >\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>The hook executes <b><i>npx lint-staged</i></b> followed by <b><i>npm run arch:check</i></b> with no <b><i>set -e</i></b> and no `||\n>exit 1`, so the final exit code can come from the second command rather than lint-staged.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[.husky/pre-commit[10-13]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/1f4f432d432538aec2f198353b8d6c5728c8dbea/.husky/pre-commit/#L10-L13)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>## Issue description\n>The pre-commit hook can succeed even when `lint-staged` fails, because its exit code is overwritten by the subsequent `npm run arch:check`.\n>### Issue Context\n>We want commits to be blocked when any pre-commit check fails.\n>### Fix Focus Areas\n>- .husky/pre-commit[12-13]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>  ✅ 2.  <s>Large-file check not staged</s> <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>✓ Correctness</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>The large-file guard checks the working tree file size, not the staged blob size, so it can be\n>bypassed (or falsely fail) when the index differs from the working tree (e.g., partial staging). It\n>also iterates filenames unsafely (breaks on spaces/backslashes).\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[.husky/pre-commit[R2-6]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/174/files#diff-d2bc4bbf14eadc292d84e0ef5f7a93115c23557f533809fc80b896934291529dR2-R6)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+git diff --cached --name-only | grep -v 'package-lock\\.json' | while read file; do\n>+  if [ -f \"$file\" ]; then\n>+    size=$(wc -c < \"$file\")\n>+    if [ \"$size\" -gt 512000 ]; then\n>+      echo \"ERROR: $file is too large ($(( size / 1024 ))KB > 500KB)\"\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details >\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>The loop lists staged paths via <b><i>git diff --cached --name-only</i></b> but then runs <b><i>wc -c &lt; &quot;$file&quot;</i></b>,\n>which reads from the filesystem (working tree). It also uses <b><i>while read file</i></b> without <b><i>IFS=</i></b>/<b><i>-r</i></b>\n>and without <b><i>-z</i></b> paths.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[.husky/pre-commit[2-6]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/1f4f432d432538aec2f198353b8d6c5728c8dbea/.husky/pre-commit/#L2-L6)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>## Issue description\n>The large-file check measures working tree size instead of staged blob size and uses unsafe filename iteration.\n>### Issue Context\n>Hook should enforce a maximum on what is actually being committed (the index), and must correctly handle paths with spaces/special characters.\n>### Fix Focus Areas\n>- .husky/pre-commit[2-6]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>  3.  YAML check missing dep <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>⛯ Reliability</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n><b><i>scripts/lint-staged-checks.mjs</i></b> requires <b><i>js-yaml</i></b>, but the root package.json does not declare it.\n>The hook relies on workspace-hoisting/transitive availability, which can break across npm/workspace\n>setups and cause pre-commit failures for YAML files.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[scripts/lint-staged-checks.mjs[R50-58]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/174/files#diff-1063eb8e02345a7969b0ffe9e387b8d671c6bddef745f0502ee66d537d5689b1R50-R58)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+  } else if (check === 'check-yaml') {\n>+    const require = createRequire(import.meta.url);\n>+    let jsYaml;\n>+    try {\n>+      jsYaml = require('js-yaml');\n>+    } catch {\n>+      console.error('js-yaml not found in node_modules');\n>+      process.exit(1);\n>+    }\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details >\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>The lint-staged check script directly <b><i>require(&#x27;js-yaml&#x27;)</i></b>, but root devDependencies do not include\n>it. It currently appears only as a workspace dependency (packages/cli), so availability at repo root\n>is not guaranteed unless hoisted.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[scripts/lint-staged-checks.mjs[48-60]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/1f4f432d432538aec2f198353b8d6c5728c8dbea/scripts/lint-staged-checks.mjs/#L48-L60)</code>\n> <code>[package.json[105-129]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/1f4f432d432538aec2f198353b8d6c5728c8dbea/package.json/#L105-L129)</code>\n> <code>[packages/cli/package.json[50-57]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/1f4f432d432538aec2f198353b8d6c5728c8dbea/packages/cli/package.json/#L50-L57)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>## Issue description\n>The pre-commit YAML validation depends on `js-yaml` but the root package does not declare it, making hook behavior dependent on hoisting/transitive deps.\n>### Issue Context\n>The root-level git hook runs from the repo root and should have all needed dependencies declared at the root.\n>### Fix Focus Areas\n>- package.json[105-142]\n>- scripts/lint-staged-checks.mjs[50-58]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n<br/>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/review-recommended.png\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Remediation recommended\">\n\n<details>\n<summary>  4.  <b><i>readFileSync</i></b> error swallowed <code>📘 Rule violation</code> <code>⛯ Reliability</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>When <b><i>readFileSync()</i></b> fails, the code catches the exception without capturing/logging the underlying\n>error, which reduces actionable context for debugging. This violates the requirement to provide\n>meaningful error context at failure points.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[scripts/lint-staged-checks.mjs[R22-28]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/174/files#diff-1063eb8e02345a7969b0ffe9e387b8d671c6bddef745f0502ee66d537d5689b1R22-R28)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+  try {\n>+    content = readFileSync(file, 'utf8');\n>+  } catch {\n>+    console.error(`Cannot read: ${file}`);\n>+    failed = true;\n>+    continue;\n>+  }\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details >\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>PR Compliance ID 3 requires meaningful, contextual error handling at failure points. The new code\n>catches the file read exception without an error object and only prints a generic message, losing\n>the reason for failure (e.g., permission denied, file removed).\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>Rule 3: Generic: Robust Error Handling and Edge Case Management</code>\n> <code>[scripts/lint-staged-checks.mjs[22-28]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/1f4f432d432538aec2f198353b8d6c5728c8dbea/scripts/lint-staged-checks.mjs/#L22-L28)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>## Issue description\n>`scripts/lint-staged-checks.mjs` catches `readFileSync()` failures without capturing the exception, so the output lacks the underlying reason for the failure.\n>## Issue Context\n>This script is run by `lint-staged` during pre-commit checks. When a file cannot be read (permissions, deleted file, encoding issues), developers need the actual error message to diagnose the problem.\n>## Fix Focus Areas\n>- scripts/lint-staged-checks.mjs[22-28]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>  ✅ 5.  <s>Hook missing shebang</s> <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>⛯ Reliability</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>The new <b><i>.husky/pre-commit</i></b> file starts with a comment and has no explicit interpreter line. Adding\n>a shebang improves portability and avoids environments where hooks aren’t executed as expected.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[.husky/pre-commit[R1-2]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/174/files#diff-d2bc4bbf14eadc292d84e0ef5f7a93115c23557f533809fc80b896934291529dR1-R2)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+# Check for large files (>500KB), excluding package-lock.json\n>+git diff --cached --name-only | grep -v 'package-lock\\.json' | while read file; do\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details >\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>The hook file begins with a comment (no interpreter directive). This is easy to make robust by\n>adding <b><i>#!/usr/bin/env sh</i></b> (and ensuring executable bit is set).\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[.husky/pre-commit[1-4]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/1f4f432d432538aec2f198353b8d6c5728c8dbea/.husky/pre-commit/#L1-L4)</code>\n> <code>Best Practice: Git hooks execution requirements</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>## Issue description\n>The hook lacks a shebang, which reduces portability/predictability of execution.\n>### Issue Context\n>Even if hooks often work without it, a shebang is a low-effort hardening step.\n>### Fix Focus Areas\n>- .husky/pre-commit[1-2]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n<pre>ⓘ The new review experience is currently in Beta. <a href=\"https://docs.qodo.ai/qodo-documentation/code-review\">Learn more</a></pre>\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<a href=\"https://www.qodo.ai\"><img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/qodo-logo.svg\" width=\"80\" alt=\"Qodo Logo\"></a>","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/comments/3935765436/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":484649,"client_id":"Iv1.8b06d3cf5deea057","slug":"qodo-code-review","node_id":"A_kwHOCuzIt84AB2Up","owner":{"login":"qodo-ai","id":183290039,"node_id":"O_kgDOCuzItw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183290039?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai","html_url":"https://github.com/qodo-ai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Qodo Code Review","description":"### The AI Code Review Platform\r\n\r\n## Get Started\r\nSimply sign into Github and click the \"Configure\" button. Check out our documentation for more info: https://docs.qodo.ai/get-started.\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\nQodo automatically reviews every GitHub pull request, identifies logic bugs, edge cases, security issues, and code quality problems, and provides actionable suggestions your team can apply immediately.\r\n\r\nInstall in minutes. Integrates seamlessly into your existing workflows.\r\n\r\n## Qodo is designed for developers who:\r\n- Handle frequent pull requests and need reliable review coverage\r\n- Balance code quality with fast delivery\r\n- Work in complex, multi-repo systems\r\n- Use AI-generated code and need stronger guardrails\r\n- Build production software where reliability matters\r\n\r\n## Qodo Capabilities\r\n- ## Automated PR Analysis\r\n  - Reviews every pull request automatically\r\n  - No manual trigger required\r\n\r\n- ## Context-Aware Code Review\r\n  - Understands cross-file changes\r\n  - Detects architectural inconsistencies\r\n\r\n- ## Actionable Suggestions\r\n  - Concrete code fixes\r\n  - Clear explanations\r\n  - Prioritized feedback\r\n\r\n- ## Security & Reliability Checks\r\n  - Identifies risky patterns\r\n  - Reduces attack surface area","external_url":"https://www.qodo.ai/","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","created_at":"2023-11-16T16:18:38Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T15:53:40Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"read","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","discussion_comment","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review_comment","push"]}}],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2833937863","pull_request_review_id":3832859972,"id":2833937863,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86o6nXH","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@\n+# Check for large files (>500KB), excluding package-lock.json\n+git diff --cached --name-only | grep -v 'package-lock\\.json' | while read file; do\n+  if [ -f \"$file\" ]; then\n+    size=$(wc -c < \"$file\")\n+    if [ \"$size\" -gt 512000 ]; then\n+      echo \"ERROR: $file is too large ($(( size / 1024 ))KB > 500KB)\"\n+      exit 1\n+    fi\n+  fi\n+done || exit 1\n+\n+npx lint-staged\n+npm run arch:check","path":".husky/pre-commit","commit_id":"51188243d2af25d8aaefc50be62ef368202909f0","original_commit_id":"51188243d2af25d8aaefc50be62ef368202909f0","user":{"login":"qodo-code-review[bot]","id":151058649,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/v2-action-required.svg\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Action required\">\n\n1\\. Lint-staged failure masked <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>✓ Correctness</code>\n\n<pre>\nThe pre-commit script runs <b><i>npx lint-staged</i></b> and then <b><i>npm run arch:check</i></b> without stopping on\nerrors. If lint-staged fails but arch:check succeeds, the hook exits 0 and the commit incorrectly\npasses.\n</pre>\n\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Agent Prompt</strong></summary>\n\n```\n### Issue description\nThe pre-commit hook can succeed even when `lint-staged` fails, because its exit code is overwritten by the subsequent `npm run arch:check`.\n\n### Issue Context\nWe want commits to be blocked when any pre-commit check fails.\n\n### Fix Focus Areas\n- .husky/pre-commit[12-13]\n```\n\n<code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n</details>","created_at":"2026-02-20T16:04:35Z","updated_at":"2026-02-20T16:04:35Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/174#discussion_r2833937863","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/174","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2833937863"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/174#discussion_r2833937863"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/174"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2833937863/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":12,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":13,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":13,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2833937874","pull_request_review_id":3832859972,"id":2833937874,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86o6nXS","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@\n+# Check for large files (>500KB), excluding package-lock.json\n+git diff --cached --name-only | grep -v 'package-lock\\.json' | while read file; do\n+  if [ -f \"$file\" ]; then\n+    size=$(wc -c < \"$file\")\n+    if [ \"$size\" -gt 512000 ]; then\n+      echo \"ERROR: $file is too large ($(( size / 1024 ))KB > 500KB)\"","path":".husky/pre-commit","commit_id":"51188243d2af25d8aaefc50be62ef368202909f0","original_commit_id":"51188243d2af25d8aaefc50be62ef368202909f0","user":{"login":"qodo-code-review[bot]","id":151058649,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/v2-action-required.svg\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Action required\">\n\n2\\. Large-file check not staged <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>✓ Correctness</code>\n\n<pre>\nThe large-file guard checks the working tree file size, not the staged blob size, so it can be\nbypassed (or falsely fail) when the index differs from the working tree (e.g., partial staging). It\nalso iterates filenames unsafely (breaks on spaces/backslashes).\n</pre>\n\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Agent Prompt</strong></summary>\n\n```\n### Issue description\nThe large-file check measures working tree size instead of staged blob size and uses unsafe filename iteration.\n\n### Issue Context\nHook should enforce a maximum on what is actually being committed (the index), and must correctly handle paths with spaces/special characters.\n\n### Fix Focus Areas\n- .husky/pre-commit[2-6]\n```\n\n<code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n</details>","created_at":"2026-02-20T16:04:35Z","updated_at":"2026-02-20T16:04:35Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/174#discussion_r2833937874","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/174","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2833937874"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/174#discussion_r2833937874"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/174"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2833937874/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":2,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":6,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":6,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2833937878","pull_request_review_id":3832859972,"id":2833937878,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86o6nXW","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,71 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env node\n+/**\n+ * File-quality checks for lint-staged (replaces prek built-in hooks).\n+ * Usage: node scripts/lint-staged-checks.mjs <check> <file1> [file2 ...]\n+ * Checks: trailing-whitespace | end-of-file | check-json | check-yaml\n+ */\n+\n+import { readFileSync } from 'fs';\n+import { createRequire } from 'module';\n+\n+const [, , check, ...files] = process.argv;\n+\n+if (!check || files.length === 0) {\n+  console.error('Usage: lint-staged-checks.mjs <check> <file...>');\n+  process.exit(1);\n+}\n+\n+let failed = false;\n+\n+for (const file of files) {\n+  let content;\n+  try {\n+    content = readFileSync(file, 'utf8');\n+  } catch {\n+    console.error(`Cannot read: ${file}`);\n+    failed = true;\n+    continue;\n+  }\n+\n+  if (check === 'trailing-whitespace') {\n+    const lines = content.split('\\n');\n+    for (let i = 0; i < lines.length; i++) {\n+      if (/[ \\t]+$/.test(lines[i])) {\n+        console.error(`${file}:${i + 1}: trailing whitespace`);\n+        failed = true;\n+      }\n+    }\n+  } else if (check === 'end-of-file') {\n+    if (content.length > 0 && !content.endsWith('\\n')) {\n+      console.error(`${file}: no newline at end of file`);\n+      failed = true;\n+    }\n+  } else if (check === 'check-json') {\n+    try {\n+      JSON.parse(content);\n+    } catch (e) {\n+      console.error(`${file}: invalid JSON — ${e.message}`);\n+      failed = true;\n+    }\n+  } else if (check === 'check-yaml') {\n+    const require = createRequire(import.meta.url);\n+    let jsYaml;\n+    try {\n+      jsYaml = require('js-yaml');\n+    } catch {\n+      console.error('js-yaml not found in node_modules');\n+      process.exit(1);\n+    }","path":"scripts/lint-staged-checks.mjs","commit_id":"33a3f4ebb0ea48d949525b5e695119afb6fb9f39","original_commit_id":"51188243d2af25d8aaefc50be62ef368202909f0","user":{"login":"qodo-code-review[bot]","id":151058649,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/v2-action-required.svg\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Action required\">\n\n3\\. Yaml check missing dep <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>⛯ Reliability</code>\n\n<pre>\n<b><i>scripts/lint-staged-checks.mjs</i></b> requires <b><i>js-yaml</i></b>, but the root package.json does not declare it.\nThe hook relies on workspace-hoisting/transitive availability, which can break across npm/workspace\nsetups and cause pre-commit failures for YAML files.\n</pre>\n\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Agent Prompt</strong></summary>\n\n```\n### Issue description\nThe pre-commit YAML validation depends on `js-yaml` but the root package does not declare it, making hook behavior dependent on hoisting/transitive deps.\n\n### Issue Context\nThe root-level git hook runs from the repo root and should have all needed dependencies declared at the root.\n\n### Fix Focus Areas\n- package.json[105-142]\n- scripts/lint-staged-checks.mjs[50-58]\n```\n\n<code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n</details>","created_at":"2026-02-20T16:04:35Z","upda