y>Diagram</summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n>\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  A[\"App Init\"] -->|\"loadPersisted\"| B[\"localStorage\"]\n  B -->|\"initialThemeId, initialScreensetId, initialLanguage, initialMockEnabled\"| C[\"createHAI3App config\"]\n  C -->|\"onInit\"| D[\"Framework Plugins\"]\n  D -->|\"apply initial values\"| E[\"Registries & State\"]\n  E -->|\"user changes\"| F[\"Framework Events\"]\n  F -->|\"theme/changed, i18n/language/changed, etc.\"| G[\"Studio persistenceEffects\"]\n  G -->|\"saveStudioState\"| B\n```\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<h3>File Changes</h3>\n\n<details>\n<summary>1. packages/framework/src/types.ts <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +16/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Add initial config fields for persisted settings\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/173/files#diff-dc93cf6a714a3f1036e2a1c31a110070b3c0c14d1cb24dbe54132a1523590cfa'> packages/framework/src/types.ts </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>2. packages/framework/src/plugins/themes.ts <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +13/-5 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Apply initial theme from config if valid\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/173/files#diff-7fe97e5a0ae90c91366485fe47874fc449f6eecb3f40a242fa33890497eda711'> packages/framework/src/plugins/themes.ts </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>3. packages/framework/src/plugins/i18n.ts <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +11/-4 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Apply initial language from config if supported\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/173/files#diff-e7b55cf938caf980885215025d1f07ebf39f07fb8fef0c9ddbb9deefe81b52e4'> packages/framework/src/plugins/i18n.ts </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary><ins><strong>View more (15)</strong></ins></summary><br/>\n<details>\n<summary>4. packages/framework/src/plugins/navigation.ts <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +10/-2 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Navigate to initial screenset if provided and exists\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/173/files#diff-26a4d2b459389017dc9e770912e9831f366ea39e95e1308e0c10346b98b85f4a'> packages/framework/src/plugins/navigation.ts </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>5. packages/framework/src/plugins/mock.ts <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +8/-4 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Enable initial mock mode from config if provided\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/173/files#diff-5b6602fd49744dbf20c5255806036ac3700e38ee90918401d5ad84e916cc09f0'> packages/framework/src/plugins/mock.ts </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>6. packages/react/src/hooks/useTranslation.ts <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +8/-3 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Emit language change event for persistence\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/173/files#diff-57cb42c3f1a9d03229c11a6df6d156b5b710ceb7da757a47085b4dc3b7e09f42'> packages/react/src/hooks/useTranslation.ts </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>7. packages/studio/src/types.ts <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +4/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Add storage keys for theme, screenset, language, mock\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/173/files#diff-03ebe77b904e3e12fad4128cb986f8018da062a40a01946824057ae73e555b46'> packages/studio/src/types.ts </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>8. packages/studio/src/effects/persistenceEffects.ts <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +44/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Subscribe to framework events and persist settings\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/173/files#diff-edcf25db72b675722f16d3e5f12d102ddb907790512a37dae43d76d13ef1c8e8'> packages/studio/src/effects/persistenceEffects.ts </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>9. packages/studio/src/index.ts <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +2/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Export persistence utilities and storage keys\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/173/files#diff-d69dcda4485e325b80fd074a0a52c07fb8d3385ee1c6536cbd496b6d0baa6b32'> packages/studio/src/index.ts </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>10. src/app/main.tsx <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +37/-2 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Load persisted settings and pass to app config\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/173/files#diff-552d660d22acfe906ed4631ca616209affcece85affbf50a747e2f313f8faa31'> src/app/main.tsx </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>11. packages/framework/package.json <code>⚙️ Configuration changes</code> <code> +1/-1 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Bump version to 0.2.0-alpha.5\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/173/files#diff-20dfa38ab5eb0c84ddc78f129e6b8f07b6885be7c4f6aec417d336a893e8398e'> packages/framework/package.json </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>12. packages/react/package.json <code>⚙️ Configuration changes</code> <code> +1/-1 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Bump version to 0.3.0-alpha.1\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/173/files#diff-1f344ac391eeecc21ec0f01fb07430a47f4b80d20485c125447d54c33c4bbfc4'> packages/react/package.json </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>13. packages/studio/package.json <code>⚙️ Configuration changes</code> <code> +1/-1 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Bump version to 0.3.0-alpha.3\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/173/files#diff-0ff3c19cc21615b0c2f6f8f0204c05eeabfd3a855f612a07bca5aac0eb851ad7'> packages/studio/package.json </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>14. openspec/specs/studio/spec.md <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +44/-4 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Add persistence scenarios to Studio requirements\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/173/files#diff-191948a1095a6603dd56dfa5fe7098cfbcc56716c1f406a28024984490bdc958'> openspec/specs/studio/spec.md </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>15. openspec/changes/archive/2026-02-13-studio-settings-persistance/proposal.md <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +32/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Document settings persistence change proposal\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/173/files#diff-293ba533b4fd428d535d07b7e877f26abe8a280319dcdb37ef16d19f67a85adc'> openspec/changes/archive/2026-02-13-studio-settings-persistance/proposal.md </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>16. openspec/changes/archive/2026-02-13-studio-settings-persistance/design.md <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +82/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Document detailed design and implementation strategy\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/173/files#diff-949bf987b5275b9e54d52fe9ce15d40c7bcc4f352df4e7db7b940951ece0fbb3'> openspec/changes/archive/2026-02-13-studio-settings-persistance/design.md </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>17. openspec/changes/archive/2026-02-13-studio-settings-persistance/specs/studio/spec.md <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +93/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Document delta specs for persistence requirements\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/173/files#diff-59b23d8ab4e0a4d292a4b046c4e01c636dc4e8ea7875a03016d7b816487913ac'> openspec/changes/archive/2026-02-13-studio-settings-persistance/specs/studio/spec.md </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>18. openspec/changes/archive/2026-02-13-studio-settings-persistance/tasks.md <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +48/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Document implementation tasks and verification steps\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/173/files#diff-cedbbaa7e26c783c77c010abf66ab9c469ebdbdbcf1db67d483124dcc6a2215f'> openspec/changes/archive/2026-02-13-studio-settings-persistance/tasks.md </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n<a href=\"https://www.qodo.ai\"><img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/qodo-logo.svg\" width=\"80\" alt=\"Qodo Logo\"></a>","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/comments/3896934740/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":484649,"client_id":"Iv1.8b06d3cf5deea057","slug":"qodo-code-review","node_id":"A_kwHOCuzIt84AB2Up","owner":{"login":"qodo-ai","id":183290039,"node_id":"O_kgDOCuzItw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183290039?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai","html_url":"https://github.com/qodo-ai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Qodo Code Review","description":"### The AI Code Review Platform\r\n\r\n## Get Started\r\nSimply sign into Github and click the \"Configure\" button. Check out our documentation for more info: https://docs.qodo.ai/get-started.\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\nQodo automatically reviews every GitHub pull request, identifies logic bugs, edge cases, security issues, and code quality problems, and provides actionable suggestions your team can apply immediately.\r\n\r\nInstall in minutes. Integrates seamlessly into your existing workflows.\r\n\r\n## Qodo is designed for developers who:\r\n- Handle frequent pull requests and need reliable review coverage\r\n- Balance code quality with fast delivery\r\n- Work in complex, multi-repo systems\r\n- Use AI-generated code and need stronger guardrails\r\n- Build production software where reliability matters\r\n\r\n## Qodo Capabilities\r\n- ## Automated PR Analysis\r\n  - Reviews every pull request automatically\r\n  - No manual trigger required\r\n\r\n- ## Context-Aware Code Review\r\n  - Understands cross-file changes\r\n  - Detects architectural inconsistencies\r\n\r\n- ## Actionable Suggestions\r\n  - Concrete code fixes\r\n  - Clear explanations\r\n  - Prioritized feedback\r\n\r\n- ## Security & Reliability Checks\r\n  - Identifies risky patterns\r\n  - Reduces attack surface area","external_url":"https://www.qodo.ai/","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","created_at":"2023-11-16T16:18:38Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T15:53:40Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"read","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","discussion_comment","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review_comment","push"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/comments/3896967166","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/173#issuecomment-3896967166","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/173","id":3896967166,"node_id":"IC_kwDOQBxSA87oRv_-","user":{"login":"qodo-code-review[bot]","id":151058649,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-13T12:32:48Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T12:32:48Z","body":"<h3>Code Review by Qodo</h3>\n\n<code>🐞 Bugs (2)</code>  <code>📘 Rule violations (2)</code>  <code>📎 Requirement gaps (0)</code>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<br/>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/action-required.png\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Action required\">\n\n<details>\n<summary>  1.  <b><i>loadPersisted()</i></b> lacks type guards <code>📘 Rule violation</code> <code>⛨ Security</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n><b><i>loadPersisted()</i></b> blindly <b><i>JSON.parse</i></b>s localStorage values and casts them to the requested type\n>without runtime validation, so malformed or unexpected values can flow into app config. Parse\n>failures are silently swallowed, making persistence issues hard to diagnose and potentially causing\n>incorrect restored settings.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[src/app/main.tsx[R27-33]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/173/files#diff-552d660d22acfe906ed4631ca616209affcece85affbf50a747e2f313f8faa31R27-R33)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+function loadPersisted<T>(key: string, defaultValue: T): T {\n>+  try {\n>+    const item = typeof localStorage !== 'undefined' ? localStorage.getItem(key) : null;\n>+    return item != null ? (JSON.parse(item) as T) : defaultValue;\n>+  } catch {\n>+    return defaultValue;\n>+  }\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details >\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>Compliance requires validating external inputs and handling edge cases with meaningful context. The\n>new <b><i>loadPersisted()</i></b> reads from <b><i>localStorage</i></b> (user-controllable input), <b><i>JSON.parse</i></b>s and casts\n>to <b><i>T</i></b> without checking the runtime type, and silently ignores exceptions by returning the default.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>Rule 6: Generic: Security-First Input Validation and Data Handling</code>\n> <code>Rule 3: Generic: Robust Error Handling and Edge Case Management</code>\n> <code>[src/app/main.tsx[27-33]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/baf96231922dc2ff791cb5dcfa7fa0ec2600d77f/src/app/main.tsx/#L27-L33)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>## Issue description\n>`loadPersisted()` parses and type-casts localStorage values without runtime validation and silently swallows parsing errors, allowing malformed values to propagate and making failures hard to debug.\n>\n>## Issue Context\n>localStorage is user-controllable input; persisted values should be validated (e.g., `typeof value === &#x27;string&#x27;` / `typeof value === &#x27;boolean&#x27;`) and invalid/unparseable values should fall back safely with minimal diagnostic logging.\n>\n>## Fix Focus Areas\n>- src/app/main.tsx[27-44]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>  2.  <b><i>initialMockEnabled</i></b> not boolean-checked <code>📘 Rule violation</code> <code>⛯ Reliability</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n><b><i>initialMockEnabled</i></b> is applied without verifying it is a boolean, so unexpected persisted values\n>can cause <b><i>toggleMockMode()</i></b> to emit a non-boolean payload and put the app into an invalid state.\n>This can break persistence correctness and downstream listeners that expect a boolean.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[packages/framework/src/plugins/mock.ts[R80-85]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/173/files#diff-5b6602fd49744dbf20c5255806036ac3700e38ee90918401d5ad84e916cc09f0R80-R85)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+      // Prefer persisted value from app config (e.g. Studio persistence), then plugin config, then dev heuristic\n>+      const initialMock = app.config.initialMockEnabled;\n>+      if (initialMock !== undefined && initialMock !== null) {\n>+        toggleMockMode(initialMock);\n>+        return;\n>+      }\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details >\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>The compliance checklist requires validating external inputs and handling edge cases explicitly. The\n>new code reads <b><i>app.config.initialMockEnabled</i></b> and forwards it directly into <b><i>toggleMockMode()</i></b> when\n>it is merely non-null, without checking <b><i>typeof initialMock === &#x27;boolean&#x27;</i></b>.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>Rule 6: Generic: Security-First Input Validation and Data Handling</code>\n> <code>Rule 3: Generic: Robust Error Handling and Edge Case Management</code>\n> <code>[packages/framework/src/plugins/mock.ts[80-85]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/baf96231922dc2ff791cb5dcfa7fa0ec2600d77f/packages/framework/src/plugins/mock.ts/#L80-L85)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>## Issue description\n>The mock plugin applies `app.config.initialMockEnabled` without verifying it is a boolean, which can result in invalid mock toggle events/state if persisted config is malformed.\n>\n>## Issue Context\n>`initialMockEnabled` is sourced from persisted storage/app config and should be treated as untrusted input at runtime.\n>\n>## Fix Focus Areas\n>- packages/framework/src/plugins/mock.ts[80-85]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>  3.  Duplicate language change emit <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>➹ Performance</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>useTranslation.setLanguage() calls app.actions.setLanguage() (which already emits\n>i18n/language/changed) and then emits the same event again, triggering translation loading twice per\n>change.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[packages/react/src/hooks/useTranslation.ts[R65-68]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/173/files#diff-57cb42c3f1a9d03229c11a6df6d156b5b710ceb7da757a47085b4dc3b7e09f42R65-R68)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+      if (app.actions.setLanguage) {\n>+        app.actions.setLanguage({ language: lang });\n>+        eventBus.emit('i18n/language/changed', { language: lang });\n>+        return;\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details >\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>In the common case where the framework i18n plugin is installed, app.actions.setLanguage is the\n>framework action that emits &#x27;i18n/language/changed&#x27;. The i18n plugin also subscribes to that event\n>and calls i18nRegistry.setLanguage(), which loads translations; emitting twice causes duplicate\n>async loads and duplicated persistence writes.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[packages/react/src/hooks/useTranslation.ts[62-71]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/baf96231922dc2ff791cb5dcfa7fa0ec2600d77f/packages/react/src/hooks/useTranslation.ts/#L62-L71)</code>\n> <code>[packages/framework/src/plugins/i18n.ts[18-26]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/baf96231922dc2ff791cb5dcfa7fa0ec2600d77f/packages/framework/src/plugins/i18n.ts/#L18-L26)</code>\n> <code>[packages/framework/src/plugins/i18n.ts[59-63]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/baf96231922dc2ff791cb5dcfa7fa0ec2600d77f/packages/framework/src/plugins/i18n.ts/#L59-L63)</code>\n> <code>[packages/i18n/src/I18nRegistry.ts[293-304]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/baf96231922dc2ff791cb5dcfa7fa0ec2600d77f/packages/i18n/src/I18nRegistry.ts/#L293-L304)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>### Issue description\n>`useTranslation().setLanguage()` emits `i18n/language/changed` twice when `app.actions.setLanguage` exists (action emits it, then the hook emits it again). This triggers duplicate translation loading and duplicate persistence writes.\n>\n>### Issue Context\n>The framework i18n plugin’s `setLanguage` action already emits `i18n/language/changed`, and the plugin subscribes to that event to call `i18nRegistry.setLanguage()`.\n>\n>### Fix Focus Areas\n>- packages/react/src/hooks/useTranslation.ts[62-73]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n<details><summary><ins><strong>View more (1)</strong></ins></summary><br/>\n<details>\n<summary>  4.  setLanguage resolves too early <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>⛯ Reliability</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>When app.actions.setLanguage exists, useTranslation.setLanguage() returns immediately (without\n>awaiting translation loading), breaking the Promise-based contract and creating race conditions for\n>callers that await it.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[packages/react/src/hooks/useTranslation.ts[R65-69]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/173/files#diff-57cb42c3f1a9d03229c11a6df6d156b5b710ceb7da757a47085b4dc3b7e09f42R65-R69)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+      if (app.actions.setLanguage) {\n>+        app.actions.setLanguage({ language: lang });\n>+        eventBus.emit('i18n/language/changed', { language: lang });\n>+        return;\n>+      }\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details >\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>UseTranslationReturn defines setLanguage as Promise&lt;void&gt;. Previously, the hook awaited\n>i18nRegistry.setLanguage(); now the main path returns immediately after emitting an event. Since\n>i18nRegistry.setLanguage is async and loads translations, callers awaiting setLanguage can proceed\n>before the language is actually ready.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[packages/react/src/types.ts[109-118]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/baf96231922dc2ff791cb5dcfa7fa0ec2600d77f/packages/react/src/types.ts/#L109-L118)</code>\n> <code>[packages/react/src/hooks/useTranslation.ts[62-71]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/baf96231922dc2ff791cb5dcfa7fa0ec2600d77f/packages/react/src/hooks/useTranslation.ts/#L62-L71)</code>\n> <code>[packages/i18n/src/I18nRegistry.ts[293-304]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/baf96231922dc2ff791cb5dcfa7fa0ec2600d77f/packages/i18n/src/I18nRegistry.ts/#L293-L304)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>### Issue description\n>`useTranslation().setLanguage()` is typed as returning `Promise&lt;void&gt;` but in the `app.actions.setLanguage` path it returns immediately after dispatching/emitting, so callers cannot reliably `await setLanguage()` to know when translations are loaded.\n>\n>### Issue Context\n>`i18nRegistry.setLanguage()` performs async translation loading. The current event-driven action path does not provide any mechanism to await completion.\n>\n>### Fix Focus Areas\n>- packages/react/src/hooks/useTranslation.ts[62-73]\n>- packages/framework/src/plugins/i18n.ts[18-77]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n</details>\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n<pre>ⓘ The new review experience is currently in Beta. <a href=\"https://docs.qodo.ai/qodo-documentation/code-review\">Learn more</a></pre>\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n<!-- https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/commit/baf96231922dc2ff791cb5dcfa7fa0ec2600d77f -->\n\n<a href=\"https://www.qodo.ai\"><img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/qodo-logo.svg\" width=\"80\" alt=\"Qodo Logo\"></a>","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/comments/3896967166/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":484649,"client_id":"Iv1.8b06d3cf5deea057","slug":"qodo-code-review","node_id":"A_kwHOCuzIt84AB2Up","owner":{"login":"qodo-ai","id":183290039,"node_id":"O_kgDOCuzItw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183290039?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai","html_url":"https://github.com/qodo-ai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Qodo Code Review","description":"### The AI Code Review Platform\r\n\r\n## Get Started\r\nSimply sign into Github and click the \"Configure\" button. Check out our documentation for more info: https://docs.qodo.ai/get-started.\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\nQodo automatically reviews every GitHub pull request, identifies logic bugs, edge cases, security issues, and code quality problems, and provides actionable suggestions your team can apply immediately.\r\n\r\nInstall in minutes. Integrates seamlessly into your existing workflows.\r\n\r\n## Qodo is designed for developers who:\r\n- Handle frequent pull requests and need reliable review coverage\r\n- Balance code quality with fast delivery\r\n- Work in complex, multi-repo systems\r\n- Use AI-generated code and need stronger guardrails\r\n- Build production software where reliability matters\r\n\r\n## Qodo Capabilities\r\n- ## Automated PR Analysis\r\n  - Reviews every pull request automatically\r\n  - No manual trigger required\r\n\r\n- ## Context-Aware Code Review\r\n  - Understands cross-file changes\r\n  - Detects architectural inconsistencies\r\n\r\n- ## Actionable Suggestions\r\n  - Concrete code fixes\r\n  - Clear explanations\r\n  - Prioritized feedback\r\n\r\n- ## Security & Reliability Checks\r\n  - Identifies risky patterns\r\n  - Reduces attack surface area","external_url":"https://www.qodo.ai/","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","created_at":"2023-11-16T16:18:38Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T15:53:40Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"read","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","discussion_comment","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review_comment","push"]}}],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2803987527","pull_request_review_id":3797021456,"id":2803987527,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86nIXRH","diff_hunk":"@@ -23,9 +23,33 @@ apiRegistry.register(AccountsApiService);\n // Initialize API services\n apiRegistry.initialize({});\n \n+// Restore Studio-persisted settings (same keys as @hai3/studio; app must not import Studio per lint)\n+function loadPersisted<T>(key: string, defaultValue: T): T {\n+  try {\n+    const item = typeof localStorage !== 'undefined' ? localStorage.getItem(key) : null;\n+    return item != null ? (JSON.parse(item) as T) : defaultValue;\n+  } catch {\n+    return defaultValue;\n+  }","path":"src/app/main.tsx","commit_id":"baf96231922dc2ff791cb5dcfa7fa0ec2600d77f","original_commit_id":"baf96231922dc2ff791cb5dcfa7fa0ec2600d77f","user":{"login":"qodo-code-review[bot]","id":151058649,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/v2-action-required.svg\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Action required\">\n\n1\\. <b><i>loadpersisted()</i></b> lacks type guards <code>📘 Rule violation</code> <code>⛨ Security</code>\n\n<pre>\n<b><i>loadPersisted()</i></b> blindly <b><i>JSON.parse</i></b>s localStorage values and casts them to the requested type\nwithout runtime validation, so malformed or unexpected values can flow into app config. Parse\nfailures are silently swallowed, making persistence issues hard to diagnose and potentially causing\nincorrect restored settings.\n</pre>\n\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Agent Prompt</strong></summary>\n\n```\n## Issue description\n`loadPersisted()` parses and type-casts localStorage values without runtime validation and silently swallows parsing errors, allowing malformed values to propagate and making failures hard to debug.\n\n## Issue Context\nlocalStorage is user-controllable input; persisted values should be validated (e.g., `typeof value === 'string'` / `typeof value === 'boolean'`) and invalid/unparseable values should fall back safely with minimal diagnostic logging.\n\n## Fix Focus Areas\n- src/app/main.tsx[27-44]\n```\n\n<code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n</details>","created_at":"2026-02-13T12:32:49Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T12:32:49Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/173#discussion_r2803987527","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/173","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2803987527"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/173#discussion_r2803987527"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/173"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2803987527/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":27,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":33,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":11,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2803987532","pull_request_review_id":3797021456,"id":2803987532,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86nIXRM","diff_hunk":"@@ -73,17 +73,21 @@ export function mock(config?: MockPluginConfig): HAI3Plugin {\n       },\n     },\n \n-    onInit() {\n+    onInit(app) {\n       // Initialize mock effects after store is ready\n       cleanup = initMockEffects();\n \n-      // Determine if mock mode should be enabled by default\n-      // Auto-detect dev environment (localhost) unless explicitly configured\n+      // Prefer persisted value from app config (e.g. Studio persistence), then plugin config, then dev heuristic\n+      const initialMock = app.config.initialMockEnabled;\n+      if (initialMock !== undefined && initialMock !== null) {\n+        toggleMockMode(initialMock);\n+        return;\n+      }","path":"packages/framework/src/plugins/mock.ts","commit_id":"baf96231922dc2ff791cb5dcfa7fa0ec2600d77f","original_commit_id":"baf96231922dc2ff791cb5dcfa7fa0ec2600d77f","user":{"login":"qodo-code-review[bot]","id":151058649,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/v2-action-required.svg\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Action required\">\n\n2\\. <b><i>initialmockenabled</i></b> not boolean-checked <code>📘 Rule violation</code> <code>⛯ Reliability</code>\n\n<pre>\n<b><i>initialMockEnabled</i></b> is applied without verifying it is a boolean, so unexpected persisted values\ncan cause <b><i>toggleMockMode()</i></b> to emit a non-boolean payload and put the app into an invalid state.\nThis can break persistence correctness and downstream listeners that expect a boolean.\n</pre>\n\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Agent Prompt</strong></summary>\n\n```\n## Issue description\nThe mock plugin applies `app.config.initialMockEnabled` without verifying it is a boolean, which can result in invalid mock toggle events/state if persisted config is malformed.\n\n## Issue Context\n`initialMockEnabled` is sourced from persisted storage/app config and should be treated as untrusted input at runtime.\n\n## Fix Focus Areas\n- packages/framework/src/plugins/mock.ts[80-85]\n```\n\n<code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n</details>","created_at":"2026-02-13T12:32:49Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T12:32:49Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/173#discussion_r2803987532","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/173","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2803987532"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/173#discussion_r2803987532"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/173"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2803987532/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":80,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":85,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":16,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2803987537","pull_request_review_id":3797021456,"id":2803987537,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86nIXRR","diff_hunk":"@@ -59,12 +59,17 @@ export function useTranslation(): UseTranslationReturn {\n     [i18nRegistry]\n   );\n \n-  // Set language function\n+  // Set language: use action so registry updates, and emit so Studio persistence (and other listeners) receive the event\n   const setLanguage = useCallback(\n     async (lang: Language) => {\n+      if (app.actions.setLanguage) {\n+        app.actions.setLanguage({ language: lang });\n+        eventBus.emit('i18n/language/changed', { language: lang });\n+        return;","path":"packages/react/src/hooks/useTranslation.ts","commit_id":"baf96231922dc2ff791cb5dcfa7fa0ec2600d77f","original_commit_id":"baf96231922dc2ff791cb5dcfa7fa0ec2600d77f","user":{"login":"qodo-code-review[bot]","id":151058649,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/v2-action-required.svg\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Action required\">\n\n3\\. Duplicate language change emit <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>➹ Performance</code>\n\n<pre>\nuseTranslation.setLanguage() calls app.actions.setLanguage() (which already emits\ni18n/language/changed) and then emits the same event again, triggering translation loading twice per\nchange.\n</pre>\n\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Agent Prompt</strong></summary>\n\n```\n### Issue description\n`useTranslation().setLanguage()` emits `i18n/language/changed` twice when `app.actions.setLanguage` exists (action emits it, then the hook emits it again). This triggers duplicate translation loading and duplicate persistence writes.\n\n### Issue Context\nThe framework i18n plugin’s `setLanguage` action already emits `i18n/language/changed`, and the plugin subscribes to that event to call `i18nRegistry.setLanguage()`.\n\n### Fix Focus Areas\n- packages/react/src/hooks/useTranslation.ts[62-73]\n```\n\n<code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n</details>","created_at":"2026-02-13T12:32:49Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T12:32:49Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/173#discussion_r2803987537","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/173","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2803987537"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/173#discussion_r2803987537"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/173"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2803987537/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":65,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":68,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":20,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2803987542","pull_request_review_id":3797021456,"id":2803987542,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86nIXRW","diff_hunk":"@@ -59,12 +59,17 @@ export function useTranslation(): UseTranslationReturn {\n     [i18nRegistry]\n   );\n \n-  // Set language function\n+  // Set language: use action so registry updates, and emit so Studio persistence (and other listeners) receive the event\n   const setLanguage = useCallback(\n     async (lang: Language) => {\n+      if (app.actions.setLanguage) {\n+        app.actions.setLanguage({ language: lang });\n+        eventBus.emit('i18n/language/changed', { language: lang });\n+        return;\n+      }","path":"packages/react/src/hooks/useTranslation.ts","commit_id":"baf96231922dc2ff791cb5dcfa7fa0ec2600d77f","original_commit_id":"baf96231922dc2ff791cb5dcfa7fa0ec2600d77f","user":{"login":"qodo-code-review[bot]","id":151058649,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/v2-action-required.svg\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Action required\">\n\n4\\. Setlanguage resolves too early <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>⛯ Reliability</code>\n\n<pre>\nWhen app.actions.setLanguage exists, useTranslation.setLanguage() returns immediately (without\nawaiting translation loading), breaking the Promise-based contract and creating race conditions for\ncallers that await it.\n</pre>\n\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Agent Prompt</strong></summary>\n\n```\n### Issue description\n`useTranslation().setLanguage()` is typed as returning `Promise<void>` but in the `app.actions.setLanguage` path it returns immediately after dispatching/emitting, so callers cannot reliably `await setLanguage()` to know when translations are loaded.\n\n### Issue Context\n`i18nRegistry.setLanguage()` performs async translation loading. The current event-driven action path does not provide any mechanism to await completion.\n\n### Fix Focus Areas\n- packages/react/src/hooks/useTranslation.ts[62-73]\n- packages/framework/src/plugins/i18n.ts[18-77]\n```\n\n<code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n</details>","created_at":"2026-02-13T12:32:49Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T12:32:49Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/173#discussion_r2803987542","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/173","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2803987542"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/173#discussion_r2803987542"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/173"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2803987542/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":65,"original_start_line":65,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":67,"original_line":69,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":21,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"}],"source_reviews":[{"id":3800947957,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOQBxSA87ijdz1","user":{"login":"GeraBart","id":246844849,"node_id":"U_kgDODraNsQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/246844849?u=a983485ea6e632a911c48b8dc160937e6252ae5d&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart","html_url":"https://github.com/GeraBart","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Review: Architectural Violation — Studio Zero-Footprint Principle\n\n### Core Issue\n\nThe Studio package was designed with a clear architectural contract: **zero footprint on the app and framework**. Studio is a dev-only overlay that reads/controls app state through hooks and events, and should be completely excluded from production builds. The app and framework should know nothing about Studio's existence.\n\nThis PR breaks that contract by solving the **load path** (restoring persisted settings on reload) in the wrong layers.\n\n---\n\n### What Was Added Where It Shouldn't Be\n\n**1. Framework layer polluted with Studio concerns (`packages/framework/src/types.ts`)**\n\n4 new fields added to `HAI3Config` — the framework's public API — with comments explicitly referencing Studio:\n\n```typescript\ninitialThemeId?: string | null;    // \"e.g. from Studio persistence\"\ninitialScreensetId?: string | null; // \"e.g. from Studio persistence\"\ninitialLanguage?: string | null;    // \"e.g. from Studio persistence\"\ninitialMockEnabled?: boolean | null; // \"e.g. from Studio persistence\"\n```\n\nThis makes Studio a documented part of the framework contract. Every HAI3 consumer ships these fields and the associated plugin logic, even projects that never use Studio.\n\n**2. Four framework plugins modified to consume Studio-specific config**\n\nEach plugin (`themes.ts`, `i18n.ts`, `navigation.ts`, `mock.ts`) gained new `onInit` logic to check `app.config.initial*` values. This code runs on every startup for every HAI3 app — ~40 lines of conditional logic across 4 plugins that only exists to serve Studio persistence.\n\n**3. App's `main.tsx` gained ~35 lines of Studio-aware boilerplate**\n\nThe app now:\n- Defines a `loadPersisted<T>()` helper\n- Hardcodes Studio's `hai3:studio:*` storage key strings\n- Reads 4 localStorage values on every startup (including production)\n- Passes them to `createHAI3App()`\n- Does its own theme validation after registration (duplicating plugin logic)\n\nBefore this PR, app creation was clean:\n```typescript\nconst app = createHAI3App({\n  themes: { applyFn: applyTheme as ThemeApplyFn },\n});\n```\n\nNow it's 35+ lines of persistence orchestration that shouldn't be the app's responsibility.\n\n---\n\n### Why This Approach Is Wrong\n\nStudio already has the right pattern for the **save path** — event-driven effects in `persistenceEffects.ts` that subscribe to framework events and write to localStorage. The **load path** should use the same pattern in reverse.\n\nThe framework plugins already listen to events:\n- `themes.ts` → `eventBus.on('theme/changed', ...)` → calls `themeRegistry.apply()`\n- `i18n.ts` → `eventBus.on('i18n/language/changed', ...)` → calls `i18nRegistry.setLanguage()`\n- `navigation.ts` → `eventBus.on('navigation/screenset/navigated', ...)` → navigates\n- `mock.ts` → `toggleMockMode()` is an exported action\n\nStudio could restore persisted settings by **emitting these same events on initialization**. The framework already knows how to handle them. Zero framework changes needed, zero app changes needed. The load path mirrors the save path, and Studio remains self-contained.\n\n---\n\n### Additional Code Issues\n\n| Issue | Location | Severity |\n|-------|----------|----------|\n| Double `i18n/language/changed` emission — `app.actions.setLanguage()` already emits the event, then line 67 emits it again | `packages/react/src/hooks/useTranslation.ts:67` | Bug |\n| `initialThemeId` config is dead code in themes plugin — themes are registered *after* `createHAI3App()`, so `themeRegistry.getAll()` returns `[]` during `onInit` and the bootstrap block is skipped entirely | `packages/framework/src/plugins/themes.ts:70-81` | Dead code |\n| Theme validation duplicated between `main.tsx:66-76` and `themes.ts:73-75` | `src/app/main.tsx`, `packages/framework/src/plugins/themes.ts` | Duplication |\n| Hardcoded `hai3:studio:*` key strings in app layer duplicate `STORAGE_KEYS` from studio types — drift risk | `src/app/main.tsx:35-40` vs `packages/studio/src/types.ts:54-63` | Coupling |\n| Design doc still lists two \"Open Questions\" as unresolved despite being answered in implementation | `openspec/changes/archive/.../design.md:79-82` | Doc |\n| Delta spec missing the \"Studio settings restoration (load path)\" requirement that was added to main spec | `openspec/changes/archive/.../specs/studio/spec.md` | Doc |\n\n---\n\n### Recommendation\n\nRevert the framework and app-layer changes. Handle the load path entirely within Studio's initialization by emitting existing framework events to restore persisted state. This keeps Studio self-contained and preserves the zero-footprint architecture.","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/173#pullrequestreview-3800947957","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/173","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/173#pullrequestreview-3800947957"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/173"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-14T05:10:34Z","commit_id":"baf96231922dc2ff791cb5dcfa7fa0ec2600d77f"},{"id":3874148213,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOQBxSA87m6s91","user":{"login":"GeraBart","id":246844849,"node_id":"U_kgDODraNsQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/246844849?u=a983485ea6e632a911c48b8dc160937e6252ae5d&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart","html_url":"https://github.com/GeraBart","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Review: APPROVE\n\nClean, well-scoped PR. Implementation faithfully follows the spec and extends the existing event-driven persistence pattern.\n\n### What looks good\n\n- Save path follows the exact same `eventBus.on` → `saveStudioState` pattern as existing position/size persistence\n- All 7 subscriptions properly cleaned up on unmount\n- Restore hooks validate values before emitting, handle missing registry / invalid IDs gracefully\n- `ActivePackageChangedPayload` properly registered via module augmentation for type safety\n- Zero framework footprint — only `packages/studio` files changed, no new cross-layer dependencies\n- No forbidden patterns (`as any`, `eslint-disable`, `@ts-ignore`)\n\n### Non-blocking observations (can be addressed in follow-up)\n\n1. **Duplicated `isScreenExtension` type guard** — identical function in `MfePackageSelector.tsx` and `useRestoreStudioSettings.ts`. Consider extracting to a shared utility.\n2. **Duplicated screen extension selection logic** — both files share the same get-extensions → filter → sort → mount-first flow. A shared `mountFirstScreenExtension(registry, packageId)` helper would reduce duplication.\n3. **`as ScreenExtension[]` cast after filter** (`useRestoreStudioSettings.ts:65`) — splitting into `.filter(ext => ext.domain === HAI3_SCREEN_DOMAIN).filter(isScreenExtension)` would let TS narrow automatically and remove the cast.\n\n### Pre-existing issues (outside PR scope, noted for tracking)\n\n1. `toggleCollapsed` in `StudioProvider.tsx` calls `saveStudioState` directly, bypassing the event-driven persistence pattern. No `CollapsedChanged` event exists.\n2. `loadStudioState` returns `JSON.parse` output as generic `T` without runtime validation.","state":"APPROVED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/173#pullrequestreview-3874148213","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/173","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/173#pullrequestreview-3874148213"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/173"}},"submitted_at":"2026-03-02T05:32:53Z","commit_id":"e351b5dd8a137570f3a119e38b54d5771cbec42b"}]},{"source_pr_number":171,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/171","source_state":"closed","source_author":"tscbmstubp","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #171] fix(studio): prevent out of bounds positioning","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"fix/studio-position","pr_head_sha":"f7393fb92c7e4b316c5d49553618dd01d28c9abe","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"tscbmstubp","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/171","id":3276425538,"node_id":"PR_kwDOQBxSA87DSklC","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/171","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/171.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/171.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/171","number":171,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(studio): prevent out of bounds positioning","user":{"login":"tscbmstubp","id":225432371,"node_id":"U_kgDODW_TMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225432371