CQD42Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-12T14:06:07Z","updated_at":"2026-02-12T14:06:07Z","body":"<h3>Review Summary by Qodo</h3>\n\nPrevent Studio button and panel from positioning off-screen\n\n<code>🐞 Bug fix</code>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<h3>Walkthroughs</h3>\n\n<details open>\n<summary>Description</summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n<pre>\n• Add viewport clamping to prevent Studio elements from positioning off-screen\n• Clamp position on initial load using stored or default values\n• Re-clamp position when window resizes to keep elements visible\n• Apply consistent 20px margin from viewport edges for all positioning\n• Emit position-change events on resize to persist corrected positions\n</pre>\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Diagram</summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n>\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  Load[\"Load stored position\"] -->|clampToViewport| Initial[\"Initial position clamped\"]\n  Drag[\"User drags element\"] -->|clampToViewport| DragClamped[\"Position clamped during drag\"]\n  Resize[\"Window resize event\"] -->|clampToViewport| ResizeClamped[\"Position re-clamped\"]\n  ResizeClamped -->|emit event| Persist[\"Position persisted to storage\"]\n  Initial --> Render[\"Element renders in viewport\"]\n  DragClamped --> Render\n  ResizeClamped --> Render\n```\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<h3>File Changes</h3>\n\n<details>\n<summary>1. packages/studio/src/hooks/useDraggable.ts\n <code>🐞 Bug fix</code> <code> +35/-13 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Add viewport clamping and resize handling to useDraggable\n><pre>\n>• Add <b><i>VIEWPORT_MARGIN</i></b> constant set to 20px for consistent edge spacing\n>• Introduce <b><i>clampToViewport()</i></b> helper function to constrain positions within viewport bounds\n>• Clamp initial position on state initialization using loaded or default values\n>• Update drag handler to use same viewport margin and bounds as clamping helper\n>• Add <b><i>useEffect</i></b> to listen for window resize events and re-clamp position when needed\n>• Emit existing position-change events on resize to trigger persistence when position changes\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/171/files#diff-b752e6f4b6a8e40f08451a1d2d3f290d30833e5896111f6d625d04a8ee76040e'> packages/studio/src/hooks/useDraggable.ts\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>2. packages/studio/package.json\n <code>⚙️ Configuration changes</code> <code> +1/-1 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Update package version for release\n><pre>\n>• Bump version from 0.3.0-alpha.1 to 0.3.0-alpha.2\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/171/files#diff-0ff3c19cc21615b0c2f6f8f0204c05eeabfd3a855f612a07bca5aac0eb851ad7'> packages/studio/package.json\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>3. openspec/changes/archive/2026-02-12-studio-position/.openspec.yaml\n <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +2/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Add OpenSpec metadata for change documentation\n><pre>\n>• Add OpenSpec metadata file for change tracking\n>• Define schema as spec-driven with creation date\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/171/files#diff-97c8bc732144b35a63db4ecc04faf50be8775ef48327378ecf3857932570e43d'> openspec/changes/archive/2026-02-12-studio-position/.openspec.yaml\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary><ins><strong>View more (5)</strong></ins></summary><br/>\n<details>\n<summary>4. openspec/changes/archive/2026-02-12-studio-position/design.md\n <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +68/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Design documentation for viewport positioning\n><pre>\n>• Document design approach for viewport positioning fix\n>• Explain single implementation point in <b><i>useDraggable</i></b> hook\n>• Detail viewport clamping helper with margin constant\n>• Describe clamp-on-load and clamp-on-resize behavior\n>• Outline event and persistence flow integration\n>• Address edge cases and SSR considerations\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/171/files#diff-45f61ab085187ffa6c7192453173e4ee96f948e0c935062d6f1859b4664c8744'> openspec/changes/archive/2026-02-12-studio-position/design.md\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>5. openspec/changes/archive/2026-02-12-studio-position/proposal.md\n <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +29/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Change proposal for studio position fix\n><pre>\n>• Explain problem: stored positions can fall outside viewport on different resolutions\n>• Describe manifestations: collapsed button and panel off-screen\n>• Outline changes to <b><i>useDraggable.ts</i></b> for clamping on load and resize\n>• List unchanged components and persistence mechanisms\n>• Assess low rollback risk and impact scope\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/171/files#diff-3c3898b12248ef7cf11afc5b1e92e6a6cb3312ff9599535dbffed2c10e513d53'> openspec/changes/archive/2026-02-12-studio-position/proposal.md\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>6. openspec/changes/archive/2026-02-12-studio-position/specs/studio-viewport-positioning/spec.md\n <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +43/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Formal specification for viewport positioning\n><pre>\n>• Define requirement for position clamping on initial load\n>• Specify scenarios for off-screen and in-view stored positions\n>• Define requirement for position clamping on viewport resize\n>• Describe scenarios for window shrinking and growing\n>• Require shared behavior for both button and panel elements\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/171/files#diff-8739df3f4c4143cb29240bd14a9a08f67d39d8379f85ef5820c5658eeb1830d3'> openspec/changes/archive/2026-02-12-studio-position/specs/studio-viewport-positioning/spec.md\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>7. openspec/specs/studio-viewport-positioning/spec.md\n <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +43/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Formal specification for viewport positioning\n><pre>\n>• Define purpose and requirements for studio viewport positioning\n>• Specify position clamping behavior on load and resize\n>• Detail scenarios for off-screen positions and window size changes\n>• Require shared implementation for button and panel\n>• Establish viewport margin constant and bounds constraints\n></pre>\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/171/files#diff-a2f6d7d29e2c9c551186509ccc1be7a0983a09a9d839bab5ac6881dc6b705e51'> openspec/specs/studio-viewport-positioning/spec.md\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>8. openspec/changes/archive/2026-02-12-studio-position/tasks.md\n <code> Additional files </code> <code> +20/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>...\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/171/files#diff-2f24f82c34c7c8b64501ff584b0386da83cfe096cc852647f2788cf15d35b296'> openspec/changes/archive/2026-02-12-studio-position/tasks.md\n </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n<a href=\"https://www.qodo.ai\"><img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/qodo-logo.svg\" width=\"80\" alt=\"Qodo Logo\"></a>","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/comments/3891158429/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":484649,"client_id":"Iv1.8b06d3cf5deea057","slug":"qodo-code-review","node_id":"A_kwHOCuzIt84AB2Up","owner":{"login":"qodo-ai","id":183290039,"node_id":"O_kgDOCuzItw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183290039?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai","html_url":"https://github.com/qodo-ai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Qodo Code Review","description":"### The AI Code Review Platform\r\n\r\n## Get Started\r\nSimply sign into Github and click the \"Configure\" button. Check out our documentation for more info: https://docs.qodo.ai/get-started.\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\nQodo automatically reviews every GitHub pull request, identifies logic bugs, edge cases, security issues, and code quality problems, and provides actionable suggestions your team can apply immediately.\r\n\r\nInstall in minutes. Integrates seamlessly into your existing workflows.\r\n\r\n## Qodo is designed for developers who:\r\n- Handle frequent pull requests and need reliable review coverage\r\n- Balance code quality with fast delivery\r\n- Work in complex, multi-repo systems\r\n- Use AI-generated code and need stronger guardrails\r\n- Build production software where reliability matters\r\n\r\n## Qodo Capabilities\r\n- ## Automated PR Analysis\r\n  - Reviews every pull request automatically\r\n  - No manual trigger required\r\n\r\n- ## Context-Aware Code Review\r\n  - Understands cross-file changes\r\n  - Detects architectural inconsistencies\r\n\r\n- ## Actionable Suggestions\r\n  - Concrete code fixes\r\n  - Clear explanations\r\n  - Prioritized feedback\r\n\r\n- ## Security & Reliability Checks\r\n  - Identifies risky patterns\r\n  - Reduces attack surface area","external_url":"https://www.qodo.ai/","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","created_at":"2023-11-16T16:18:38Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T15:53:40Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"read","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","discussion_comment","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review_comment","push"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/comments/3891188758","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/171#issuecomment-3891188758","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/171","id":3891188758,"node_id":"IC_kwDOQBxSA87n7tQW","user":{"login":"qodo-code-review[bot]","id":151058649,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-12T14:12:15Z","updated_at":"2026-02-12T14:12:15Z","body":"<h3>Code Review by Qodo</h3>\n\n<code>🐞 Bugs (1)</code>  <code>📘 Rule violations (0)</code>  <code>📎 Requirement gaps (0)</code>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<br/>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/review-recommended.png\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Remediation recommended\">\n\n<details>\n<summary>  1.  Impure setState updater <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>⛯ Reliability</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>The resize handler emits StudioEvents from inside the <b><i>setPosition(prev =&gt; ...)</i></b> updater, which\n>should be a pure computation; in React StrictMode/concurrent rendering the updater may be invoked\n>more than once for a single resize, causing duplicate emissions and repeated localStorage writes.\n>This is unlikely to corrupt data but can create noisy persistence traffic and unexpected side\n>effects for any other subscribers.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[packages/studio/src/hooks/useDraggable.ts[R78-89]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/171/files#diff-b752e6f4b6a8e40f08451a1d2d3f290d30833e5896111f6d625d04a8ee76040eR78-R89)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+  useEffect(() => {\n>+    const handleResize = () => {\n>+      setPosition((prev) => {\n>+        const clamped = clampToViewport(prev, panelSize);\n>+        if (clamped.x === prev.x && clamped.y === prev.y) return prev;\n>+        const eventName =\n>+          storageKey === STORAGE_KEYS.BUTTON_POSITION\n>+            ? StudioEvents.ButtonPositionChanged\n>+            : StudioEvents.PositionChanged;\n>+        eventBus.emit(eventName, { position: clamped });\n>+        return clamped;\n>+      });\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details >\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n><b><i>eventBus.emit(...)</i></b> is executed inside the <b><i>setPosition</i></b> functional updater in the new resize\n>effect. Those events are persisted by <b><i>initPersistenceEffects()</i></b> into localStorage, so duplicate\n>updater invocations can directly translate into duplicate localStorage writes for the same resize\n>event when clamping occurs.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[packages/studio/src/hooks/useDraggable.ts[78-89]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/f7393fb92c7e4b316c5d49553618dd01d28c9abe/packages/studio/src/hooks/useDraggable.ts/#L78-L89)</code>\n> <code>[packages/studio/src/effects/persistenceEffects.ts[16-39]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/f7393fb92c7e4b316c5d49553618dd01d28c9abe/packages/studio/src/effects/persistenceEffects.ts/#L16-L39)</code>\n> <code>[packages/studio/src/utils/persistence.ts[9-14]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/f7393fb92c7e4b316c5d49553618dd01d28c9abe/packages/studio/src/utils/persistence.ts/#L9-L14)</code>\n> <code>Best Practice: React docs (useState functional updates)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>## Issue description\n>The window `resize` handler emits `eventBus` events from inside the `setPosition(prev =&gt; ...)` functional updater. React expects these updater functions to be pure; in StrictMode/concurrent rendering they can be invoked more than once for a single resize update, which can duplicate `eventBus.emit(...)` calls and thus duplicate persistence writes.\n>\n>## Issue Context\n>- Resize clamping is correct, but persistence should happen deterministically once per resize event when the position actually changes.\n>- `initPersistenceEffects()` persists these events to localStorage, so duplicate emits become duplicate writes.\n>\n>## Fix Focus Areas\n>- packages/studio/src/hooks/useDraggable.ts[78-93]\n>\n>### Suggested implementation direction\n>- Add `positionRef` updated via `useEffect(() =&gt; { positionRef.current = position; }, [position])`.\n>- Add `panelSizeRef` and `storageKeyRef` similarly (or update inside effect deps).\n>- Register a stable `handleResize` that:\n>  1) reads `prev = positionRef.current`\n>  2) computes `clamped = clampToViewport(prev, panelSizeRef.current)`\n>  3) if changed: `setPosition(clamped)` and `eventBus.emit(eventName, { position: clamped })`\n>- This keeps the state updater pure and ensures a single emit per resize event that causes a clamp.\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n<pre>ⓘ The new review experience is currently in Beta. <a href=\"https://docs.qodo.ai/qodo-documentation/code-review\">Learn more</a></pre>\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n<!-- https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/commit/f7393fb92c7e4b316c5d49553618dd01d28c9abe -->\n\n<a href=\"https://www.qodo.ai\"><img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/qodo-logo.svg\" width=\"80\" alt=\"Qodo Logo\"></a>","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/comments/3891188758/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":484649,"client_id":"Iv1.8b06d3cf5deea057","slug":"qodo-code-review","node_id":"A_kwHOCuzIt84AB2Up","owner":{"login":"qodo-ai","id":183290039,"node_id":"O_kgDOCuzItw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183290039?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai","html_url":"https://github.com/qodo-ai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Qodo Code Review","description":"### The AI Code Review Platform\r\n\r\n## Get Started\r\nSimply sign into Github and click the \"Configure\" button. Check out our documentation for more info: https://docs.qodo.ai/get-started.\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\nQodo automatically reviews every GitHub pull request, identifies logic bugs, edge cases, security issues, and code quality problems, and provides actionable suggestions your team can apply immediately.\r\n\r\nInstall in minutes. Integrates seamlessly into your existing workflows.\r\n\r\n## Qodo is designed for developers who:\r\n- Handle frequent pull requests and need reliable review coverage\r\n- Balance code quality with fast delivery\r\n- Work in complex, multi-repo systems\r\n- Use AI-generated code and need stronger guardrails\r\n- Build production software where reliability matters\r\n\r\n## Qodo Capabilities\r\n- ## Automated PR Analysis\r\n  - Reviews every pull request automatically\r\n  - No manual trigger required\r\n\r\n- ## Context-Aware Code Review\r\n  - Understands cross-file changes\r\n  - Detects architectural inconsistencies\r\n\r\n- ## Actionable Suggestions\r\n  - Concrete code fixes\r\n  - Clear explanations\r\n  - Prioritized feedback\r\n\r\n- ## Security & Reliability Checks\r\n  - Identifies risky patterns\r\n  - Reduces attack surface area","external_url":"https://www.qodo.ai/","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","created_at":"2023-11-16T16:18:38Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T15:53:40Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"read","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","discussion_comment","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review_comment","push"]}}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":169,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/169","source_state":"closed","source_author":"m231-a","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #169] Feat/docs: preliminary implementation of docs package ","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"feat/docs_simplified","pr_head_sha":"5ebceec8a6996fd527886505f98df3bea6e41096","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"m231-a","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.c