ing\n• Configure custom theme with HAI3 branding and styling\n• Update root package.json with docs scripts and dependencies\n</pre>\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Diagram</summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n>\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  A[\"Documentation Content<br/>Markdown Files\"] --> B[\"VitePress Config<br/>Navigation & Theme\"]\n  B --> C[\"Custom CSS<br/>HAI3 Branding\"]\n  C --> D[\"Build Process<br/>Static Site Generation\"]\n  D --> E[\"GitHub Pages<br/>Automated Deployment\"]\n  F[\"Root package.json<br/>Docs Scripts\"] --> D\n```\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<h3>File Changes</h3>\n\n<details>\n<summary>1. packages/docs/.vitepress/config.ts <code>⚙️ Configuration changes</code> <code> +68/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>VitePress site configuration with navigation\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/169/files#diff-61daf7647ecc7b20e3d3c1d70646fe5ab9c4eefd8c58fa36e3b857f39966fc7b'> packages/docs/.vitepress/config.ts </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>2. packages/docs/.vitepress/theme/index.ts <code>✨ Enhancement</code> <code> +17/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Custom theme setup extending VitePress default\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/169/files#diff-f020b2fe35eafedf7c988ab38cec3e2a17057ffacb8f3328549a1d4f4b8ffbb5'> packages/docs/.vitepress/theme/index.ts </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>3. packages/docs/.vitepress/theme/custom.css <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +80/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>HAI3 brand colors and component styling\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/169/files#diff-854c7db6b6479ff13304c4cad2fff5d7c3a36de69931bdf134ad87468063b1d5'> packages/docs/.vitepress/theme/custom.css </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary><ins><strong>View more (12)</strong></ins></summary><br/>\n<details>\n<summary>4. packages/docs/postcss.config.js <code>⚙️ Configuration changes</code> <code> +5/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Minimal PostCSS configuration for VitePress\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/169/files#diff-bd3900057ab1f14b0485608a0bd49d90cb05d2ef3b0983f32880a5c611d0a38b'> packages/docs/postcss.config.js </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>5. packages/docs/package.json <code> Dependencies </code> <code> +26/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Docs package with VitePress dependencies\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/169/files#diff-5926d0c6229942021583ce21a7c24dcc3d5f10e744bf6d560b5bee2d85635792'> packages/docs/package.json </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>6. packages/docs/tsconfig.json <code>⚙️ Configuration changes</code> <code> +18/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>TypeScript configuration for VitePress\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/169/files#diff-a575191c457994c51237fbfa8f74ccef8c3416632f9bbbf9929465b721cd0120'> packages/docs/tsconfig.json </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>7. packages/docs/README.md <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +178/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Comprehensive documentation setup and usage guide\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/169/files#diff-3e5c648b80d4eda8bbfcec04f986b5911ed1c7290594a58882e9c63106eab3fe'> packages/docs/README.md </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>8. packages/docs/src/index.md <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +43/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Homepage with hero section and feature cards\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/169/files#diff-e28d252130a417918f0bd93f95321497e518dca0ab27a60512d0065efcea38f6'> packages/docs/src/index.md </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>9. packages/docs/src/getting-started.md <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +21/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Getting started guide placeholder\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/169/files#diff-266e3bc454a55b4b19de39499eb76a71ccca51d4f40c92202f2fb4e736cb4734'> packages/docs/src/getting-started.md </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>10. packages/docs/src/lifecycle/index.md <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +16/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>AI Product Lifecycle section overview\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/169/files#diff-eb3807a4b705e18372b17144ef60d2e0c6210ed922ac41774524aa6c57ef200c'> packages/docs/src/lifecycle/index.md </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>11. packages/docs/src/hai3/index.md <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +17/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>HAI3 Framework section overview\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/169/files#diff-dffa8d0128cc377a8cc90e0147640346403bed1525cd8c0adf125911f9fa276e'> packages/docs/src/hai3/index.md </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>12. packages/docs/src/case-studies/index.md <code>📝 Documentation</code> <code> +15/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Case studies section overview\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/169/files#diff-69d996b8e3dc57a773cda9e6d74b615717db0dae52ae34ed7d845ba568cf3c33'> packages/docs/src/case-studies/index.md </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>13. .github/workflows/docs.yml <code>⚙️ Configuration changes</code> <code> +59/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>GitHub Actions workflow for docs deployment\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/169/files#diff-9cf2000c53760d837a449f874e53f792819108d3a4bf346336d0f7d082deae2c'> .github/workflows/docs.yml </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>14. eslint.config.js <code>⚙️ Configuration changes</code> <code> +1/-0 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Add VitePress directory to ESLint ignores\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/169/files#diff-a32a0887ed9d1d707bbb3b845b7df7fd40e673c47e7b60a3ebd896b68d3b8839'> eslint.config.js </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>15. package.json <code>⚙️ Configuration changes</code> <code> +9/-4 </code>  </summary>  \n\n<br/>\n\n>Add docs scripts and update Node/npm versions\n>\n><a href='https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/169/files#diff-7ae45ad102eab3b6d7e7896acd08c427a9b25b346470d7bc6507b6481575d519'> package.json </a>\n<hr/>\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n<a href=\"https://www.qodo.ai\"><img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/qodo-logo.svg\" width=\"80\" alt=\"Qodo Logo\"></a>","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/comments/3880955496/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":484649,"client_id":"Iv1.8b06d3cf5deea057","slug":"qodo-code-review","node_id":"A_kwHOCuzIt84AB2Up","owner":{"login":"qodo-ai","id":183290039,"node_id":"O_kgDOCuzItw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183290039?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai","html_url":"https://github.com/qodo-ai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Qodo Code Review","description":"### The AI Code Review Platform\r\n\r\n## Get Started\r\nSimply sign into Github and click the \"Configure\" button. Check out our documentation for more info: https://docs.qodo.ai/get-started.\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\nQodo automatically reviews every GitHub pull request, identifies logic bugs, edge cases, security issues, and code quality problems, and provides actionable suggestions your team can apply immediately.\r\n\r\nInstall in minutes. Integrates seamlessly into your existing workflows.\r\n\r\n## Qodo is designed for developers who:\r\n- Handle frequent pull requests and need reliable review coverage\r\n- Balance code quality with fast delivery\r\n- Work in complex, multi-repo systems\r\n- Use AI-generated code and need stronger guardrails\r\n- Build production software where reliability matters\r\n\r\n## Qodo Capabilities\r\n- ## Automated PR Analysis\r\n  - Reviews every pull request automatically\r\n  - No manual trigger required\r\n\r\n- ## Context-Aware Code Review\r\n  - Understands cross-file changes\r\n  - Detects architectural inconsistencies\r\n\r\n- ## Actionable Suggestions\r\n  - Concrete code fixes\r\n  - Clear explanations\r\n  - Prioritized feedback\r\n\r\n- ## Security & Reliability Checks\r\n  - Identifies risky patterns\r\n  - Reduces attack surface area","external_url":"https://www.qodo.ai/","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","created_at":"2023-11-16T16:18:38Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T15:53:40Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"read","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","discussion_comment","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review_comment","push"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/comments/3880972581","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/169#issuecomment-3880972581","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/169","id":3880972581,"node_id":"IC_kwDOQBxSA87nUvEl","user":{"login":"qodo-code-review[bot]","id":151058649,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-10T22:01:55Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T03:44:09Z","body":"<h3>Code Review by Qodo</h3>\n\n<code>🐞 Bugs (4)</code>  <code>📘 Rule violations (0)</code>  <code>📎 Requirement gaps (0)</code>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<br/>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/action-required.png\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Action required\">\n\n<details>\n<summary>  ✅ 1.  <s>Docs CI uses Node 20</s> <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>⛯ Reliability</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>The docs GitHub Pages workflow uses Node 20, but the repo enforces engines with <b><i>engine-strict=true</i></b>\n>and requires Node &gt;=22. This will cause <b><i>npm ci</i></b> to fail and block docs deployment on every run.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[.github/workflows/docs.yml[R27-37]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/169/files#diff-9cf2000c53760d837a449f874e53f792819108d3a4bf346336d0f7d082deae2cR27-R37)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+      - name: Setup Node\n>+        uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n>+        with:\n>+          node-version: '20'\n>+          cache: 'npm'\n>+\n>+      - name: Setup Pages\n>+        uses: actions/configure-pages@v4\n>+\n>+      - name: Install dependencies\n>+        run: npm ci\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details >\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n><b><i>engine-strict=true</i></b> makes npm treat the <b><i>engines</i></b> field as a hard requirement. The workflow pins\n>Node 20, which violates <b><i>engines.node: &gt;=22.0.0</i></b>, so <b><i>npm ci</i></b> will error and the workflow cannot\n>proceed to build/upload.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[.npmrc[1-2]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/5ebceec8a6996fd527886505f98df3bea6e41096/.npmrc/#L1-L2)</code>\n> <code>[package.json[7-10]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/5ebceec8a6996fd527886505f98df3bea6e41096/package.json/#L7-L10)</code>\n> <code>[.github/workflows/docs.yml[27-37]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/5ebceec8a6996fd527886505f98df3bea6e41096/.github/workflows/docs.yml/#L27-L37)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>## Issue description\n>Docs deployment workflow runs on Node 20, but the repo enforces `engines.node &amp;amp;gt;= 22.0.0` with `engine-strict=true`, causing `npm ci` to fail.\n>## Issue Context\n>This prevents the GitHub Pages docs pipeline from running successfully on pushes to `main`.\n>## Fix\n>- Change `actions/setup-node` in the docs workflow to `node-version: &amp;amp;#x27;22.x&amp;amp;#x27;` (or `&amp;amp;#x27;25.x&amp;amp;#x27;` to match existing CI).\n>## Fix Focus Areas\n>- .github/workflows/docs.yml[27-37]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>  2.  VitePress config not used <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>✓ Correctness</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>Docs scripts build VitePress with root directory set to <b><i>src</i></b>, but the VitePress config/theme are\n>placed in <b><i>packages/docs/.vitepress</i></b> (outside <b><i>src</i></b>). This likely causes the build to ignore the\n>intended config (base path, nav, theme), producing a silently incorrect site for GitHub Pages.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[packages/docs/package.json[R7-11]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/169/files#diff-5926d0c6229942021583ce21a7c24dcc3d5f10e744bf6d560b5bee2d85635792R7-R11)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+  \"scripts\": {\n>+    \"docs:dev\": \"vitepress dev src\",\n>+    \"docs:build\": \"vitepress build src\",\n>+    \"docs:preview\": \"vitepress preview src\"\n>+  },\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details >\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>The docs workspace scripts explicitly run <b><i>vitepress ... src</i></b>, and the workflow uploads\n><b><i>packages/docs/src/.vitepress/dist</i></b>, implying <b><i>src</i></b> is the VitePress root. However, the committed\n>config file is at <b><i>packages/docs/.vitepress/config.ts</i></b> (not under <b><i>src/.vitepress</i></b>), so the build\n>likely runs without that config and uses default VitePress settings.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[packages/docs/package.json[7-11]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/5ebceec8a6996fd527886505f98df3bea6e41096/packages/docs/package.json/#L7-L11)</code>\n> <code>[packages/docs/.vitepress/config.ts[1-14]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/5ebceec8a6996fd527886505f98df3bea6e41096/packages/docs/.vitepress/config.ts/#L1-L14)</code>\n> <code>[.github/workflows/docs.yml[39-47]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/5ebceec8a6996fd527886505f98df3bea6e41096/.github/workflows/docs.yml/#L39-L47)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>## Issue description\n>VitePress is built with root `src`, but `.vitepress/config.ts` and theme files are located at `packages/docs/.vitepress/*`, so the build likely ignores the custom config/theme.\n>## Issue Context\n>The GitHub Pages workflow sets `VITE_BASE` expecting it to be applied via the VitePress config, but the config may not be loaded depending on the chosen VitePress root.\n>## Fix options (pick one)\n>### Option A (keep `src` as VitePress root)\n>- Move `packages/docs/.vitepress/` to `packages/docs/src/.vitepress/`.\n>- Update any related paths (tsconfig include, .gitignore, workflow upload path if needed).\n>### Option B (use package root as VitePress root)\n>- Change scripts to `vitepress dev` / `vitepress build` (no `src` arg).\n>- Set `srcDir: &amp;amp;#x27;src&amp;amp;#x27;` in `defineConfig({ ... })`.\n>- Update workflow artifact upload path to `packages/docs/.vitepress/dist`.\n>## Fix Focus Areas\n>- packages/docs/package.json[7-11]\n>- packages/docs/.vitepress/config.ts[1-14]\n>- .github/workflows/docs.yml[39-47]\n>- packages/docs/tsconfig.json[16-17]\n>- packages/docs/.gitignore[4-9]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n<br/>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/review-recommended.png\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Remediation recommended\">\n\n<details>\n<summary>  3.  Docs README incorrect <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>⛯ Reliability</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>The newly added docs README lists Node/NPM requirements and build output paths that contradict the\n>repo’s enforced engines and the workflow’s artifact path. This will cause contributors to follow\n>instructions that fail under <b><i>engine-strict</i></b> or look in the wrong output directory.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[packages/docs/README.md[R18-20]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/169/files#diff-3e5c648b80d4eda8bbfcec04f986b5911ed1c7290594a58882e9c63106eab3feR18-R20)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+- Node.js >= 25.1.0\n>+- npm >= 11.6.0\n>+\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details >\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>The README claims Node &gt;=25.1.0 and npm &gt;=11.6.0, but the repo now enforces Node &gt;=22 and npm &gt;=10\n>with <b><i>engine-strict=true</i></b>, meaning incorrect versions can hard-fail install. It also states the\n>build output is <b><i>packages/docs/dist/</i></b>, while the workflow uploads\n><b><i>packages/docs/src/.vitepress/dist</i></b> (and the docs gitignore includes VitePress dist directories).\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[packages/docs/README.md[18-20]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/5ebceec8a6996fd527886505f98df3bea6e41096/packages/docs/README.md/#L18-L20)</code>\n> <code>[packages/docs/README.md[45-45]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/5ebceec8a6996fd527886505f98df3bea6e41096/packages/docs/README.md/#L45-L45)</code>\n> <code>[package.json[7-10]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/5ebceec8a6996fd527886505f98df3bea6e41096/package.json/#L7-L10)</code>\n> <code>[.npmrc[1-2]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/5ebceec8a6996fd527886505f98df3bea6e41096/.npmrc/#L1-L2)</code>\n> <code>[.github/workflows/docs.yml[44-47]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/5ebceec8a6996fd527886505f98df3bea6e41096/.github/workflows/docs.yml/#L44-L47)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>## Issue description\n>`packages/docs/README.md` contains Node/NPM prerequisites and a build output path that do not match the repo’s enforced engines and the workflow’s configured artifact path.\n>## Issue Context\n>The repo uses `engine-strict=true`, so incorrect Node versions can cause install failures.\n>## Fix\n>- Update prerequisites to align with `package.json` engines.\n>- Update build output path documentation to match the actual VitePress output directory after resolving the VitePress root/config mismatch.\n>## Fix Focus Areas\n>- packages/docs/README.md[18-20]\n>- packages/docs/README.md[45-45]\n>- package.json[7-11]\n>- .github/workflows/docs.yml[44-47]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n<br/>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/other.png\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Advisory comments\">\n\n<details>\n<summary>  4.  Hardcoded Pages base <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>⛯ Reliability</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>The docs workflow hardcodes <b><i>VITE_BASE</i></b> to <b><i>/HAI3/</i></b>, which is correct for the canonical repo but\n>will break Pages routing if the repo name/base path changes (e.g., forks/renames) unless manually\n>updated.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[.github/workflows/docs.yml[R39-42]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/169/files#diff-9cf2000c53760d837a449f874e53f792819108d3a4bf346336d0f7d082deae2cR39-R42)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+      - name: Build docs\n>+        env:\n>+          VITE_BASE: '/HAI3/'\n>+        run: npm run docs:build -w packages/docs\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details >\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>The VitePress config is already designed to read the base from <b><i>process.env.VITE_BASE</i></b>, and the\n>workflow sets it to a fixed value. This is a maintainability limitation rather than an immediate\n>bug.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[.github/workflows/docs.yml[39-42]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/5ebceec8a6996fd527886505f98df3bea6e41096/.github/workflows/docs.yml/#L39-L42)</code>\n> <code>[packages/docs/.vitepress/config.ts[7-10]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/5ebceec8a6996fd527886505f98df3bea6e41096/packages/docs/.vitepress/config.ts/#L7-L10)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>## Issue description\n>The workflow sets `VITE_BASE` to a hardcoded repository path (`/HAI3/`). This is fine for the primary repo but is brittle for forks/renames.\n>## Issue Context\n>VitePress already supports configuring `base` via `process.env.VITE_BASE`.\n>## Fix\n>- Consider setting `VITE_BASE` dynamically, e.g. `/${{ github.event.repository.name }}/` for project pages, or document the fork/rename requirement.\n>## Fix Focus Areas\n>- .github/workflows/docs.yml[39-42]\n>- packages/docs/.vitepress/config.ts[7-10]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n<pre>ⓘ The new review experience is currently in Beta. <a href=\"https://docs.qodo.ai/qodo-documentation/code-review\">Learn more</a></pre>\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<a href=\"https://www.qodo.ai\"><img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/qodo-logo.svg\" width=\"80\" alt=\"Qodo Logo\"></a>","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/comments/3880972581/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":484649,"client_id":"Iv1.8b06d3cf5deea057","slug":"qodo-code-review","node_id":"A_kwHOCuzIt84AB2Up","owner":{"login":"qodo-ai","id":183290039,"node_id":"O_kgDOCuzItw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183290039?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai","html_url":"https://github.com/qodo-ai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Qodo Code Review","description":"### The AI Code Review Platform\r\n\r\n## Get Started\r\nSimply sign into Github and click the \"Configure\" button. Check out our documentation for more info: https://docs.qodo.ai/get-started.\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\nQodo automatically reviews every GitHub pull request, identifies logic bugs, edge cases, security issues, and code quality problems, and provides actionable suggestions your team can apply immediately.\r\n\r\nInstall in minutes. Integrates seamlessly into your existing workflows.\r\n\r\n## Qodo is designed for developers who:\r\n- Handle frequent pull requests and need reliable review coverage\r\n- Balance code quality with fast delivery\r\n- Work in complex, multi-repo systems\r\n- Use AI-generated code and need stronger guardrails\r\n- Build production software where reliability matters\r\n\r\n## Qodo Capabilities\r\n- ## Automated PR Analysis\r\n  - Reviews every pull request automatically\r\n  - No manual trigger required\r\n\r\n- ## Context-Aware Code Review\r\n  - Understands cross-file changes\r\n  - Detects architectural inconsistencies\r\n\r\n- ## Actionable Suggestions\r\n  - Concrete code fixes\r\n  - Clear explanations\r\n  - Prioritized feedback\r\n\r\n- ## Security & Reliability Checks\r\n  - Identifies risky patterns\r\n  - Reduces attack surface area","external_url":"https://www.qodo.ai/","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","created_at":"2023-11-16T16:18:38Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T15:53:40Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"read","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","discussion_comment","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review_comment","push"]}}],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2790503605","pull_request_review_id":3781869991,"id":2790503605,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86mU7S1","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@\n+name: Deploy Documentation\n+\n+on:\n+  push:\n+    branches:\n+      - main\n+  workflow_dispatch:\n+\n+permissions:\n+  contents: read\n+  pages: write\n+  id-token: write\n+\n+concurrency:\n+  group: pages\n+  cancel-in-progress: false\n+\n+jobs:\n+  build:\n+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n+    steps:\n+      - name: Checkout\n+        uses: actions/checkout@v4\n+        with:\n+          fetch-depth: 0\n+\n+      - name: Setup Node\n+        uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n+        with:\n+          node-version: '20'\n+          cache: 'npm'\n+\n+      - name: Setup Pages\n+        uses: actions/configure-pages@v4\n+\n+      - name: Install dependencies\n+        run: npm ci","path":".github/workflows/docs.yml","commit_id":"5ebceec8a6996fd527886505f98df3bea6e41096","original_commit_id":"33a440683ade1906f2a5d8dd3ec3bb73b45b68e5","user":{"login":"qodo-code-review[bot]","id":151058649,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/v2-action-required.svg\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Action required\">\n\n1\\. Docs ci uses node 20 <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>⛯ Reliability</code>\n\n<pre>\nThe docs GitHub Pages workflow uses Node 20, but the repo enforces engines with <b><i>engine-strict=true</i></b>\nand requires Node &gt;=22. This will cause <b><i>npm ci</i></b> to fail and block docs deployment on every run.\n</pre>\n\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Agent Prompt</strong></summary>\n\n```\n## Issue description\nDocs deployment workflow runs on Node 20, but the repo enforces `engines.node >= 22.0.0` with `engine-strict=true`, causing `npm ci` to fail.\n\n## Issue Context\nThis prevents the GitHub Pages docs pipeline from running successfully on pushes to `main`.\n\n## Fix\n- Change `actions/setup-node` in the docs workflow to `node-version: '22.x'` (or `'25.x'` to match existing CI).\n\n## Fix Focus Areas\n- .github/workflows/docs.yml[27-37]\n```\n\n<code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n</details>","created_at":"2026-02-10T22:01:55Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T22:01:55Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/169#discussion_r2790503605","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/169","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2790503605"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/169#discussion_r2790503605"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/169"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2790503605/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":27,"original_start_line":27,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":37,"original_line":37,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":37,"position":37,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2790503610","pull_request_review_id":3781869991,"id":2790503610,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86mU7S6","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@\n+{\n+  \"name\": \"@hai3/docs\",\n+  \"version\": \"0.2.0-alpha.1\",\n+  \"description\": \"HAI3 documentation site - AI-driven product lifecycle and framework docs\",\n+  \"type\": \"module\",\n+  \"private\": true,\n+  \"scripts\": {\n+    \"docs:dev\": \"vitepress dev src\",\n+    \"docs:build\": \"vitepress build src\",\n+    \"docs:preview\": \"vitepress preview src\"\n+  },","path":"packages/docs/package.json","commit_id":"5ebceec8a6996fd527886505f98df3bea6e41096","original_commit_id":"33a440683ade1906f2a5d8dd3ec3bb73b45b68e5","user":{"login":"qodo-code-review[bot]","id":151058649,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCQD42Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/484649?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-code-review%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/v2-action-required.svg\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Action required\">\n\n2\\. Vitepress config not used <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>✓ Correctness</code>\n\n<pre>\nDocs scripts build VitePress with root directory set to <b><i>src</i></b>, but the VitePress config/theme are\nplaced in <b><i>packages/docs/.vitepress</i></b> (outside <b><i>src</i></b>). This likely causes the build to ignore the\nintended config (base path, nav, theme), producing a silently incorrect site for GitHub Pages.\n</pre>\n\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Agent Prompt</strong></summary>\n\n```\n## Issue description\nVitePress is built with root `src`, but `.vitepress/config.ts` and theme files are located at `packages/docs/.vitepress/*`, so the build likely ignores the custom config/theme.\n\n## Issue Context\nThe GitHub Pages workflow sets `VITE_BASE` expecting it to be applied via the VitePress config, but the config may not be loaded depending on the chosen VitePress root.\n\n## Fix options (pick one)\n### Option A (keep `src` as VitePress root)\n- Move `packages/docs/.vitepress/` to `packages/docs/src/.vitepress/`.\n- Update any related paths (tsconfig include, .gitignore, workflow upload path if needed).\n\n### Option B (use package root as VitePress root)\n- Change scripts to `vitepress dev` / `vitepress build` (no `src` arg).\n- Set `srcDir: 'src'` in `defineConfig({ ... })`.\n- Update workflow artifact upload path to `packages/docs/.vitepress/dist`.\n\n## Fix Focus Areas\n- packages/docs/package.json[7-11]\n- packages/docs/.vitepress/config.ts[1-14]\n- .github/workflows/docs.yml[39-47]\n- packages/docs/tsconfig.json[16-17]\n- packages/docs/.gitignore[4-9]\n```\n\n<code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n</details>","created_at":"2026-02-10T22:01:55Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T22:01:55Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/169#discussion_r2790503610","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/169","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2790503610"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/169#discussion_r2790503610"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/169"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2790503610/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":7,"original_start_line":7,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":11,"original_line":11,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":11,"position":11,"subject_type":"line"}],"source_reviews":[{"id":3782670058,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOQBxSA87hdvbq","user":{"login":"GeraBart","id":246844849,"node_id":"U_kgDODraNsQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/246844849?u=a983485ea6e632a911c48b8dc160937e6252ae5d&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart","html_url":"https://github.com/GeraBart","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"# PR #169 Review — Docs Package Skeleton\n\n**Approved.** Clean scaffolding PR. Two minor items noted below — can be fixed in a follow-up.\n\n---\n\n## Minor Issues (non-blocking)\n\n### 1. Node version mismatch in README\n\n`packages/docs/README.md` references Node >= 25.1.0 and npm >= 11.6.0 (lines 18-19), and the example workflow uses `node-version: '25.1.0'` (line 143). However:\n- Root `package.json` engines: `\"node\": \">=22.0.0\"`, `\"npm\": \">=10.0.0\"`\n- `.github/workflows/docs.yml`: `node-version: '22'`\n\n**Fix:** Update README prerequisites and example workflow to match (Node 22, npm 10).\n\n### 2. tsconfig include path doesn't match file location\n\n`packages/docs/tsconfig.json` line 17:\n```json\n\"include\": [\".vitepress/**/*.ts\", \".vitepress/**/*.vue\"]\n```\n\nActual VitePress config is at `packages/docs/src/.vitepress/`, not `packages/docs/.vitepress/`. IDE type-checking won't cover the config file.\n\n**Fix:** Change to `\"src/.vitepress/**/*.ts\"` and `\"src/.vitepress/**/*.vue\"`.\n\nThe README directory structure diagram (lines 50-64) has the same discrepancy — shows `.vitepress/` at the package root instead of under `src/`.\n\n---\n\nEverything else looks good: VitePress config, theme, CSS, PostCSS override, GitHub Actions workflow, placeholder content, and gitignore are all well-structured.","state":"APPROVED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/169#pullrequestreview-3782670058","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/169","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/169#pullrequestreview-3782670058"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/169"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-11T03:35:48Z","commit_id":"5ebceec8a6996fd527886505f98df3bea6e41096"}]},{"source_pr_number":168,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/168","source_state":"closed","source_author":"GeraBart","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #168] Feat/mfe implementation","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"feat/MFE_implementation","pr_head_sha":"7a26e3ca43e6735b2309c01053d1133985c0a4f1","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"GeraBart","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/168","id":3266721448,"node_id":"PR_kwDOQBxSA87Ctjao","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/168","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/168.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/168.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/168","number":168,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Feat/mfe implementation","user":{"login":"GeraBart","id":246844849,"node_id":"U_kg