content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<br/>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/review-recommended.png\" height=\"20\" alt=\"Remediation recommended\">\n\n<details>\n<summary>  1.  Ambiguous import/ID guidance <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>✓ Correctness</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>• <b><i>openspec/config.yaml</i></b> forbids “barrel exports hiding imports” and “central ID constants”, but the\n>   repo intentionally uses barrel-style package entrypoints (<b><i>index.ts</i></b> re-exports) as the public API\n>   surface.\n>• The repo also documents and uses per-screenset <b><i>ids.ts</i></b> constants as the canonical place for IDs;\n>   the new wording is broad enough to be misread as forbidding this pattern.\n>• If followed literally, contributors/agents may start deep-importing internals or\n>   inlining/scattering IDs, increasing circular-dep risk and reducing consistency with existing\n>   architecture.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[openspec/config.yaml[10]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/167/files#diff-3463ab4be8fd566433dddf71a3b6c17f6914d9fafae4b8f8dafcf39937832af3R10-R10)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+  Imports: same package = relative; app cross-branch = @/; cross-package = workspace name (@hai3/…). Forbidden: package internals (@hai3/*/src/*), any, \"as unknown as\", barrel exports hiding imports, central ID constants (define where used).\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details >\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>The new config forbids barrel exports and central ID constants. However, the codebase uses\n><b><i>index.ts</i></b> files to re-export public APIs (a barrel pattern) and explicitly documents IDs living in\n><b><i>ids.ts</i></b> per screenset, with concrete examples in <b><i>src/screensets/demo/ids.ts</i></b>. This makes the new\n>rule wording ambiguous and potentially contradictory to established conventions.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[openspec/config.yaml[7-12]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/7524b41788d8500b9326eb069aa356fed09db0ad/openspec/config.yaml/#L7-L12)</code>\n> <code>[packages/framework/src/index.ts[1-50]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/7524b41788d8500b9326eb069aa356fed09db0ad/packages/framework/src/index.ts/#L1-L50)</code>\n> <code>[packages/react/src/index.ts[1-46]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/7524b41788d8500b9326eb069aa356fed09db0ad/packages/react/src/index.ts/#L1-L46)</code>\n> <code>[src/screensets/screensetRegistry.tsx[44-57]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/7524b41788d8500b9326eb069aa356fed09db0ad/src/screensets/screensetRegistry.tsx/#L44-L57)</code>\n> <code>[src/screensets/demo/ids.ts[1-22]](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/blob/7524b41788d8500b9326eb069aa356fed09db0ad/src/screensets/demo/ids.ts/#L1-L22)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>## Issue description\n>`openspec/config.yaml` currently forbids “barrel exports hiding imports” and “central ID constants”, but the repo intentionally uses barrel-style package entrypoints (`packages/*/src/index.ts`) as the public API and documents per-screenset `ids.ts` as the canonical place for IDs.\n>\n>This wording is ambiguous and can cause contributors/agents to misinterpret the intended patterns, leading to deep-imports into internals or scattered ID definitions.\n>\n>## Issue Context\n>Existing conventions:\n>- Package entrypoints re-export public APIs (expected consumer import surface)\n>- Screenset IDs are centralized per screenset in `src/screensets/&lt;name&gt;/ids.ts`\n>\n>## Fix Focus Areas\n>- openspec/config.yaml[10-10]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n<pre>ⓘ The new review experience is currently in Beta. <a href=\"https://docs.qodo.ai/qodo-documentation/code-review\">Learn more</a></pre>\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n<!-- https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/commit/7524b41788d8500b9326eb069aa356fed09db0ad -->\n\n<a href=\"https://www.qodo.ai\"><img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/qodo-logo.svg\" width=\"80\" alt=\"Qodo Logo\"></a>","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/comments/3860330721/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":484649,"client_id":"Iv1.8b06d3cf5deea057","slug":"qodo-code-review","node_id":"A_kwHOCuzIt84AB2Up","owner":{"login":"qodo-ai","id":183290039,"node_id":"O_kgDOCuzItw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183290039?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai","html_url":"https://github.com/qodo-ai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qodo-ai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Qodo Code Review","description":"### The A