rue,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":6,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":50,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["ai","llm","nocode","react","saas","shadcn","tailwind","typescript"],"visibility":"private","forks":6,"open_issues":50,"watchers":15,"default_branch":"main"}},"_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/148"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/148"},"issue":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/148"},"comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/148/comments"},"review_comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/148/comments"},"review_comment":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments{/number}"},"commits":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/148/commits"},"statuses":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/statuses/d938e0f6dc6592b9fc2ef365deb5f7e1e65a7633"}},"author_association":"MEMBER","auto_merge":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},"source_issue_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/comments/3797996024","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/148#issuecomment-3797996024","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/148","id":3797996024,"node_id":"IC_kwDOQBxSA87iYNH4","user":{"login":"GeraBart","id":246844849,"node_id":"U_kgDODraNsQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/246844849?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart","html_url":"https://github.com/GeraBart","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T05:53:38Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T05:56:40Z","body":"## Implementation Review Feedback\r\n\r\nThe implementation looks solid overall. Here are a few minor suggestions for improvement before merging:\r\n\r\n### 1. Duplicate Type Definition\r\n**Files:** `packages/framework/src/types.ts` and `packages/framework/src/utils/routeMatcher.ts`\r\n\r\n`RouteMatchResult` is defined identically in both files. Consider removing the duplicate from `routeMatcher.ts` and importing from `../types` instead.\r\n\r\n### 2. Missing Type Export\r\n**File:** `packages/framework/src/index.ts`\r\n\r\n`RouteMatchResult` is not exported from the framework package. While `RouteRegistry` (which uses `RouteMatchResult` in its method signatures) is exported, consumers cannot import the `RouteMatchResult` type directly. Consider adding it to the type exports.\r\n\r\n### 3. Hook Export Inconsistency\r\n**File:** `packages/react/src/hooks/index.ts`\r\n\r\n`useRouteParams` is exported from the main `index.ts` but not from the hooks barrel file (`hooks/index.ts`). Other hooks like `useNavigation` and `useTheme` are exported from both. Consider adding `useRouteParams` to the hooks barrel for consistency.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThese are all minor housekeeping items and don't block approval. Nice work on the parameterized routing implementation!","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/comments/3797996024/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/comments/3797999059","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/148#issuecomment-3797999059","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/148","id":3797999059,"node_id":"IC_kwDOQBxSA87iYN3T","user":{"login":"GeraBart","id":246844849,"node_id":"U_kgDODraNsQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/246844849?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart","html_url":"https://github.com/GeraBart","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T05:55:28Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T05:58:11Z","body":"## Additional Feedback\r\n\r\n### 4. Type Safety Enhancement - Module Augmentation for Route Params\r\n\r\nThe current implementation returns `Record<string, string>` from `useRouteParams()`, which provides no compile-time safety that expected parameters exist. Consider adding module augmentation support for type-safe route params in a follow-up:\r\n\r\n```typescript\r\n// In screenset definition\r\ndeclare module '@hai3/framework' {\r\n  interface RouteParams {\r\n    'users.detail': { userId: string };\r\n    'users.posts.detail': { userId: string; postId: string };\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n\r\n// Hook becomes type-safe\r\nconst { userId } = useRouteParams<'users.detail'>();  // Type: { userId: string }\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis aligns with HAI3's existing pattern of using module augmentation for type extensions (as seen with events) and would provide compile-time validation that route parameter names match what's defined in the path patterns.\r\n\r\n### 5. Package Version Bumps Required\r\n\r\nThis PR introduces new public API surface (`useRouteParams` hook, `RouteParamsContext`, `path` property in `MenuItemConfig`). The following packages need version bumps:\r\n\r\n- `@hai3/framework` - new `routeMatcher` utility, `RouteRegistry` methods, `path-to-regexp` dependency\r\n- `@hai3/react` - new `useRouteParams` hook and `RouteParamsContext`\r\n- `@hai3/screensets` - new `path` property in `MenuItemConfig` type\r\n- `@hai3/cli` - if it references any of the above\r\n\r\nPlease ensure your PR is rebased, and versions are bumped according to semver before merging.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/comments/3797999059/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[{"id":3705313561,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOQBxSA87c2pkZ","user":{"login":"dingoatemytokens","id":244849678,"node_id":"U_kgDODpgcDg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244849678?u=0b136d35ff3c695595a23e7523b62f0b779f0e06&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens","html_url":"https://github.com/dingoatemytokens","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Overall, everything looks good, but there are a few issues worth addressing before merging.\n\n### 1. Route params are not reliably available to components\n\n**Files:** `navigation.ts`, `AppRouter.tsx`\n\n**Problem:**  \nRoute params are derived from the URL in two separate places (`AppRouter.tsx:44-56` and `navigation.ts:134-137`). There is no single source of truth for params.\n\nThis causes:\n- Race condition: screen component renders with empty params before `useEffect` runs\n- On browser Back/Forward (`popstate`), params are extracted but then dropped — only `screenId` is dispatched\n\n**Impact:**  \nIf a screen uses `params.id` immediately (e.g. for a fetch), it will be `undefined` on the first render.\n\n### 2. No validation for required route params\n\n**File:** `navigation.ts:148-157`\n\n**Problem:**  \nThe code checks only that `payload.params` object exists, but does not verify that all required params from the route pattern are provided.\n\nExample: calling `navigateToScreen('x', 'y', { userId: '1' })` for route `/users/:userId/posts/:postId` — `postId` is missing but navigation proceeds, generating an invalid URL.\n\n### 3. Route matching order is not deterministic\n\n**File:** `routeRegistry.ts:47-66`\n\n**Problem:**  \nRoutes are added in iteration order. The matcher returns the first match.\n\nIf `/users/new` is registered after `/users/:id`, then URL `/users/new` will be matched as `/users/:id` with `params = { id: 'new' }` instead of the static route.\n","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/148#pullrequestreview-3705313561","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/148","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/148#pullrequestreview-3705313561"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/148"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-26T09:52:31Z","commit_id":"cccd834fda19fe3ca45ae80e18c1993b83c22f93"}]},{"source_pr_number":147,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/147","source_state":"closed","source_author":"Artifizer","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #147] [Snyk] Security upgrade lodash from 4.17.21 to 4.17.23","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"snyk-fix-585b717df56ee3d0c81d2ecf7a73c12c","pr_head_sha":"6e1bc3f81d5a52397580aa38ecd318f82b049b2d","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"cyberfabric","pr_from_fork":0,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/147","id":3199250425,"node_id":"PR_kwDOQBxSA86-sK_5","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/147","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/147.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/147.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/147","number":147,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[Snyk] Security upgrade lodash from 4.17.21 to 4.17.23","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"![snyk-top-banner](https://res.cloudinary.com/snyk/image/upload/r-d/scm-platform/snyk-pull-requests/pr-banner-default.svg)\n\n### Snyk has created this PR to fix 1 vulnerabilities in the npm dependencies of this project.\n\n#### Snyk changed the following file(s):\n\n- `package.json`\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚠️ <b>Warning</b></summary>\n\n```\nFailed to update the package-lock.json, please update manually before merging.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n#### Vulnerabilities that will be fixed with an upgrade:\n\n|  | Issue | Score | \n:-------------------------:|:-------------------------|:-------------------------\n![medium severity](https://res.cloudinary.com/snyk/image/upload/w_20,h_20/v1561977819/icon/m.png 'medium severity') | Prototype Pollution <br/>[SNYK-JS-LODASH-15053838](https://snyk.io/vuln/SNYK-JS-LODASH-15053838) | &nbsp;&nbsp;**631**&nbsp;&nbsp; \n\n\n\n\n---\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n>\n> - Check the changes in this PR to ensure they won't cause issues with your project.\n> - Max score is 1000. Note that the real score may have changed since the PR was raised.\n> - This PR was automatically created by Snyk using the credentials of a real user.\n\n---\n\n**Note:** _You are seeing this because you or someone else with access to this repository has authorized Snyk to open fix PRs._\n\nFor more information: <img src=\"https://api.segment.io/v1/pixel/track?data=eyJ3cml0ZUtleSI6InJyWmxZcEdHY2RyTHZsb0lYd0dUcVg4WkFRTnNCOUEwIiwiYW5vbnltb3VzSWQiOiJjMDQyOTg1Ni1mZWZhLTQwNzQtODNhNC03Zjc3ZWZlZDExNWMiLCJldmVudCI6IlBSIHZpZXdlZCIsInByb3BlcnRpZXMiOnsicHJJZCI6ImMwNDI5ODU2LWZlZmEtNDA3NC04M2E0LTdmNzdlZmVkMTE1YyJ9fQ==\" width=\"0\" height=\"0\"/>\n🧐 [View latest project report](https://app.snyk.io/org/artifizer/project/b5420301-5200-45de-b9b9-ed0000044af6?utm_source&#x3D;github&amp;utm_medium&#x3D;referral&amp;page&#x3D;fix-pr)\n📜 [Customise PR templates](https://docs.snyk.io/scan-using-snyk/pull-requests/snyk-fix-pull-or-merge-requests/customize-pr-templates?utm_source=github&utm_content=fix-pr-template)\n🛠 [Adjust project settings](https://app.snyk.io/org/artifizer/project/b5420301-5200-45de-b9b9-ed0000044af6?utm_source&#x3D;github&amp;utm_medium&#x3D;referral&amp;page&#x3D;fix-pr/settings)\n📚 [Read about Snyk's upgrade logic](https://docs.snyk.io/scan-with-snyk/snyk-open-source/manage-vulnerabilities/upgrade-package-versions-to-fix-vulnerabilities?utm_source=github&utm_content=fix-pr-template)\n\n---\n\n**Learn how to fix vulnerabilities with free interactive lessons:**\n\n🦉 [Prototype Pollution](https://learn.snyk.io/lesson/prototype-pollution/?loc&#x3D;fix-pr)\n\n[//]: # 'snyk:metadata:{\"breakingChangeRiskLevel\":null,\"FF_showPullRequestBreakingChanges\":false,\"FF_showPullRequestBreakingChangesWebSearch\":false,\"customTemplate\":{\"variablesUsed\":[],\"fieldsUsed\":[]},\"dependencies\":[{\"name\":\"lodash\",\"from\":\"4.17.21\",\"to\":\"4.17.23\"}],\"env\":\"prod\",\"issuesToFix\":[\"SNYK-JS-LODASH-15053838\"],\"prId\":\"c0429856-fefa-4074-83a4-7f77efed115c\",\"prPublicId\":\"c0429856-fefa-4074-83a4-7f77efed115c\",\"packageManager\":\"npm\",\"priorityScoreList\":[631],\"projectPublicId\":\"b54