gistry\n+- Own `@hai3/state` container\n+- Can use ANY UI framework (host uses React, MFEs can use Vue 3, Angular, Svelte, etc.)","path":"openspec/changes/add-microfrontend-support/proposal.md","commit_id":"857055e6df3343d7e78949a0f911f3ecc2173cc8","original_commit_id":"0c146565c7ab92c566d5ef92723d97f1bb958ddc","user":{"login":"GeraBart","id":246844849,"node_id":"U_kgDODraNsQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/246844849?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart","html_url":"https://github.com/GeraBart","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"No, it was a mistake.","created_at":"2026-02-04T03:17:45Z","updated_at":"2026-02-04T03:17:46Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/131#discussion_r2761972547","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/131","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2761972547"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/131#discussion_r2761972547"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/131"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2761972547/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":21,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2676427650,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":21,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2761973615","pull_request_review_id":3748719329,"id":2761973615,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86koF9v","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,254 @@\n+# Change: Add Microfrontend Support\n+\n+## Why\n+\n+HAI3 applications need to compose functionality from multiple independently deployed microfrontends (MFEs). Vendors can create MFE extensions that integrate into host applications through well-defined extension points. This enables:\n+\n+1. **Independent Deployment**: MFEs can be deployed separately from the host application\n+2. **Vendor Extensibility**: Third parties can create extensions without modifying host code, using ANY UI framework (Vue 3, Angular, Svelte, etc.)\n+3. **Complete Runtime Isolation**: Each MFE maintains its own isolated runtime (state, TypeSystemPlugin, schema registry) with controlled communication ONLY through the contract\n+4. **Type-Safe Contracts**: Each runtime has its own TypeSystemPlugin instance - MFEs cannot discover host or other MFE schemas\n+5. **Framework Agnostic**: Host uses React, but MFEs can use any framework - no React/ReactDOM dependency for MFEs\n+\n+## What Changes\n+\n+### Core Architecture\n+\n+Each MFE and host has its **own FULLY ISOLATED runtime**:\n+- Own `@hai3/screensets` instance (NOT singleton)\n+- Own `TypeSystemPlugin` instance (NOT singleton) with isolated schema registry\n+- Own `@hai3/state` container\n+- Can use ANY UI framework (host uses React, MFEs can use Vue 3, Angular, Svelte, etc.)\n+\n+Communication happens ONLY through the explicit contract (MfeBridge interface):\n+- **Shared properties** (parent to child, read-only)\n+- **Actions chain** delivered by ActionsChainsMediator to targets\n+\n+Internal runtime coordination (between host and MFE runtimes) uses PRIVATE mechanisms not exposed to MFE code.\n+\n+### Architectural Decision: Type System Plugin Abstraction\n+\n+The @hai3/screensets package abstracts the Type System as a **pluggable dependency**:\n+\n+1. **Opaque Type IDs**: The screensets package treats type IDs as opaque strings\n+2. **Required Plugin**: A `TypeSystemPlugin` must be provided at initialization\n+3. **Default Implementation**: GTS (`@globaltypesystem/gts-ts`) ships as the default plugin\n+4. **Extensibility**: Other Type System implementations can be plugged in\n+\n+**Key Principle**: When metadata about a type ID is needed, call plugin methods (`parseTypeId`, `getAttribute`, etc.) directly.\n+\n+**Plugin Interface:**\n+```typescript\n+interface TypeSystemPlugin {\n+  // Type ID operations\n+  isValidTypeId(id: string): boolean;\n+  buildTypeId(options: Record<string, unknown>): string;\n+  parseTypeId(id: string): Record<string, unknown>;\n+\n+  // Schema registry\n+  registerSchema(typeId: string, schema: JSONSchema): void;\n+  validateInstance(typeId: string, instance: unknown): ValidationResult;\n+  getSchema(typeId: string): JSONSchema | undefined;\n+\n+  // Query\n+  query(pattern: string, limit?: number): string[];\n+\n+  // Compatibility (REQUIRED)\n+  checkCompatibility(oldTypeId: string, newTypeId: string): CompatibilityResult;\n+\n+  // Attribute access (REQUIRED for dynamic schema resolution)\n+  getAttribute(typeId: string, path: string): AttributeResult;\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### HAI3 Internal TypeScript Types\n+\n+The MFE system uses these internal TypeScript interfaces. Each type has an `id: string` field as its identifier:\n+\n+**Core Types (6 types):**\n+\n+| TypeScript Interface | Fields | Purpose |\n+|---------------------|--------|---------|\n+| `MfeEntry` | `id, requiredProperties[], optionalProperties?[], actions[], domainActions[]` | Pure contract type (Abstract Base) |\n+| `ExtensionDomain` | `id, sharedProperties[], actions[], extensionsActions[], extensionsUiMeta, defaultActionTimeout` | Extension point contract |\n+| `Extension` | `id, domain, entry, uiMeta` | Extension binding |\n+| `SharedProperty` | `id, value` | Shared property instance |\n+| `Action` | `type, target, payload?, timeout?` | Action with self-identifying type ID and optional timeout override |\n+| `ActionsChain` | `action: Action, next?: ActionsChain, fallback?: ActionsChain` | Action chain for mediation (contains instances, no id) |\n+\n+**MF-Specific Types (2 types):**\n+\n+| TypeScript Interface | Fields | Purpose |\n+|---------------------|--------|---------|\n+| `MfManifest` | `id, remoteEntry, remoteName, sharedDependencies?[], entries?` | Module Federation manifest (standalone) |\n+| `MfeEntryMF` | `(extends MfeEntry) manifest, exposedModule` | Module Federation entry (derived) |\n+\n+**Note on MfeEntry Design:** MfeEntry is a **pure contract** type (abstract base) that defines ONLY the communication interface (properties, actions). Derived types like `MfeEntryMF` add loader-specific fields. This separation ensures the same entry contract works with any loader and allows future loaders (ESM, Import Maps) to add their own derived types.\n+\n+### GTS Type ID Format\n+\n+The GTS type ID format is: `gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.v<MAJOR>[.<MINOR>]~`","path":"openspec/changes/add-microfrontend-support/proposal.md","commit_id":"76a6669f869deb5d52dc41a5008e35a122135c1d","original_commit_id":"0c146565c7ab92c566d5ef92723d97f1bb958ddc","user":{"login":"GeraBart","id":246844849,"node_id":"U_kgDODraNsQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/246844849?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart","html_url":"https://github.com/GeraBart","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Already referenced","created_at":"2026-02-04T03:18:07Z","updated_at":"2026-02-04T03:18:08Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/131#discussion_r2761973615","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/131","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2761973615"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/131#discussion_r2761973615"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/131"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2761973615/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":166,"original_line":90,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2676455504,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":90,"position":166,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2761975275","pull_request_review_id":3748721195,"id":2761975275,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86koGXr","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,254 @@\n+# Change: Add Microfrontend Support\n+\n+## Why\n+\n+HAI3 applications need to compose functionality from multiple independently deployed microfrontends (MFEs). Vendors can create MFE extensions that integrate into host applications through well-defined extension points. This enables:\n+\n+1. **Independent Deployment**: MFEs can be deployed separately from the host application\n+2. **Vendor Extensibility**: Third parties can create extensions without modifying host code, using ANY UI framework (Vue 3, Angular, Svelte, etc.)\n+3. **Complete Runtime Isolation**: Each MFE maintains its own isolated runtime (state, TypeSystemPlugin, schema registry) with controlled communication ONLY through the contract\n+4. **Type-Safe Contracts**: Each runtime has its own TypeSystemPlugin instance - MFEs cannot discover host or other MFE schemas\n+5. **Framework Agnostic**: Host uses React, but MFEs can use any framework - no React/ReactDOM dependency for MFEs\n+\n+## What Changes\n+\n+### Core Architecture\n+\n+Each MFE and host has its **own FULLY ISOLATED runtime**:\n+- Own `@hai3/screensets` instance (NOT singleton)\n+- Own `TypeSystemPlugin` instance (NOT singleton) with isolated schema registry\n+- Own `@hai3/state` container\n+- Can use ANY UI framework (host uses React, MFEs can use Vue 3, Angular, Svelte, etc.)\n+\n+Communication happens ONLY through the explicit contract (MfeBridge interface):\n+- **Shared properties** (parent to child, read-only)\n+- **Actions chain** delivered by ActionsChainsMediator to targets\n+\n+Internal runtime coordination (between host and MFE runtimes) uses PRIVATE mechanisms not exposed to MFE code.\n+\n+### Architectural Decision: Type System Plugin Abstraction\n+\n+The @hai3/screensets package abstracts the Type System as a **pluggable dependency**:\n+\n+1. **Opaque Type IDs**: The screensets package treats type IDs as opaque strings\n+2. **Required Plugin**: A `TypeSystemPlugin` must be provided at initialization\n+3. **Default Implementation**: GTS (`@globaltypesystem/gts-ts`) ships as the default plugin\n+4. **Extensibility**: Other Type System implementations can be plugged in\n+\n+**Key Principle**: When metadata about a type ID is needed, call plugin methods (`parseTypeId`, `getAttribute`, etc.) directly.\n+\n+**Plugin Interface:**\n+```typescript\n+interface TypeSystemPlugin {\n+  // Type ID operations\n+  isValidTypeId(id: string): boolean;\n+  buildTypeId(options: Record<string, unknown>): string;\n+  parseTypeId(id: string): Record<string, unknown>;\n+\n+  // Schema registry\n+  registerSchema(typeId: string, schema: JSONSchema): void;\n+  validateInstance(typeId: string, instance: unknown): ValidationResult;\n+  getSchema(typeId: string): JSONSchema | undefined;\n+\n+  // Query\n+  query(pattern: string, limit?: number): string[];\n+\n+  // Compatibility (REQUIRED)\n+  checkCompatibility(oldTypeId: string, newTypeId: string): CompatibilityResult;\n+\n+  // Attribute access (REQUIRED for dynamic schema resolution)\n+  getAttribute(typeId: string, path: string): AttributeResult;\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### HAI3 Internal TypeScript Types\n+\n+The MFE system uses these internal TypeScript interfaces. Each type has an `id: string` field as its identifier:\n+\n+**Core Types (6 types):**\n+\n+| TypeScript Interface | Fields | Purpose |\n+|---------------------|--------|---------|\n+| `MfeEntry` | `id, requiredProperties[], optionalProperties?[], actions[], domainActions[]` | Pure contract type (Abstract Base) |\n+| `ExtensionDomain` | `id, sharedProperties[], actions[], extensionsActions[], extensionsUiMeta, defaultActionTimeout` | Extension point contract |\n+| `Extension` | `id, domain, entry, uiMeta` | Extension binding |\n+| `SharedProperty` | `id, value` | Shared property instance |\n+| `Action` | `type, target, payload?, timeout?` | Action with self-identifying type ID and optional timeout override |\n+| `ActionsChain` | `action: Action, next?: ActionsChain, fallback?: ActionsChain` | Action chain for mediation (contains instances, no id) |\n+\n+**MF-Specific Types (2 types):**\n+\n+| TypeScript Interface | Fields | Purpose |\n+|---------------------|--------|---------|\n+| `MfManifest` | `id, remoteEntry, remoteName, sharedDependencies?[], entries?` | Module Federation manifest (standalone) |\n+| `MfeEntryMF` | `(extends MfeEntry) manifest, exposedModule` | Module Federation entry (derived) |\n+\n+**Note on MfeEntry Design:** MfeEntry is a **pure contract** type (abstract base) that defines ONLY the communication interface (properties, actions). Derived types like `MfeEntryMF` add loader-specific fields. This separation ensures the same entry contract works with any loader and allows future loaders (ESM, Import Maps) to add their own derived types.\n+\n+### GTS Type ID Format\n+\n+The GTS type ID format is: `gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.v<MAJOR>[.<MINOR>]~`\n+\n+### Type System Registration (via Plugin)\n+\n+When using the GTS plugin, the following types are registered with properly structured GTS type IDs:\n+\n+**Core Types (6 types):**\n+\n+| GTS Type ID | Purpose |\n+|-------------|---------|\n+| `gts.hai3.screensets.mfe.entry.v1~` | Pure contract type (Abstract Base) |\n+| `gts.hai3.screensets.ext.domain.v1~` | Extension point contract |","path":"openspec/changes/add-microfrontend-support/proposal.md","commit_id":"76a6669f869deb5d52dc41a5008e35a122135c1d","original_commit_id":"0c146565c7ab92c566d5ef92723d97f1bb958ddc","user":{"login":"GeraBart","id":246844849,"node_id":"U_kgDODraNsQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/246844849?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart","html_url":"https://github.com/GeraBart","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Because MFE is an application, and extension is a binding.","created_at":"2026-02-04T03:18:43Z","updated_at":"2026-02-04T03:18:43Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/131#discussion_r2761975275","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/131","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2761975275"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/131#discussion_r2761975275"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/131"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2761975275/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":177,"original_line":101,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2676459827,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":101,"position":177,"subject_type":"line"}],"source_reviews":[]},{"source_pr_number":130,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/130","source_state":"closed","source_author":"GuilleX7","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #130] fix: standalone project generation","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"fix/standalone-project","pr_head_sha":"5bff8ef871dd5d39f87ac4bf7d91c71123f08e47","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"GuilleX7","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/130","id":3158723644,"node_id":"PR_kwDOQBxSA868Rkw8","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/130","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/130.diff","patch_url":"https://github.