":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens","html_url":"https://github.com/dingoatemytokens","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-30T04:04:30Z","updated_at":"2025-12-30T04:04:30Z","body":"It looks like this fix is incorrect. `zod` is used by the demo screenset, so it needs to be installed at the project root. But screensets are excluded from `knip.json`, which means `knip` doesn’t see screenset dependencies and flags `zod` as unused. As a result, we end up with a contradiction: a screenset has its own dependency, but it isn’t accounted for at the project level because screensets are excluded","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/comments/3698250562/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/comments/3698287769","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/115#issuecomment-3698287769","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/115","id":3698287769,"node_id":"IC_kwDOQBxSA87cb2SZ","user":{"login":"GeraBart","id":246844849,"node_id":"U_kgDODraNsQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/246844849?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart","html_url":"https://github.com/GeraBart","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GeraBart/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-30T04:31:33Z","updated_at":"2025-12-30T04:31:33Z","body":"> It looks like this fix is incorrect. `zod` is used by the demo screenset, so it needs to be installed at the project root. But screensets are excluded from `knip.json`, which means `knip` doesn’t see screenset dependencies and flags `zod` as unused. As a result, we end up with a contradiction: a screenset has its own dependency, but it isn’t accounted for at the project level because screensets are excluded\r\n\r\nI think excluding screensets from knit.json can be reverted.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/comments/3698287769/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/comments/3704308753","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/115#issuecomment-3704308753","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/115","id":3704308753,"node_id":"IC_kwDOQBxSA87cy0QR","user":{"login":"dingoatemytokens","id":244849678,"node_id":"U_kgDODpgcDg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244849678?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens","html_url":"https://github.com/dingoatemytokens","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dingoatemytokens/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-02T01:33:52Z","updated_at":"2026-01-02T01:33:52Z","body":"> > It looks like this fix is incorrect. `zod` is used by the demo screenset, so it needs to be installed at the project root. But screensets are excluded from `knip.json`, which means `knip` doesn’t see screenset dependencies and flags `zod` as unused. As a result, we end up with a contradiction: a screenset has its own dependency, but it isn’t accounted for at the project level because screensets are excluded\r\n> \r\n> I think excluding screensets from knit.json can be reverted.\r\n\r\nI created [another PR](https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3/pull/119) that include screensets to knip coverage\r\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/issues/comments/3704308753/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"r