ent applications for SaaS multitenant and multi-user control panels.\n+\n+## 🎯 Project Vision\n+\n+The main **HAI3 UI-Core objective** is to achieve the **maximum possible efficiency** of application screens generation by **AI**, while maintaining the **code quality** and **code structure** for future application logic scale.\n+\n+1. **HAI3 UI-core**: Human-driven development, AI-assisted, well structured and polished.\n+2. **Application business screens**: AI-driven development with help of HAI3 UI-core, Human-assisted.\n+\n+## ✨ Features\n+\n+- **TypeScript-first**: Strict typing for better developer experience and code quality\n+- **Modern Stack**: React 18 + Vite + Redux Toolkit + Tailwind CSS\n+- **Modular Architecture**: Screensets as vertical slices, reusable UIKit components\n+- **Layout System**: Complete set of layout components (Header, Footer, Menu, Sidebar, Popup, Overlay)","path":"README.md","commit_id":"f38b8ea4ff21969992a181fe6c2a9b0d0c77b677","original_commit_id":"e4e04eabbc3c586ddacf287549928d48e62748ff","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I'm not sure it's Complete,... i'd use:\r\n\r\nconfigurable set of layout components (Header, Footer, Menu, Sidebar, Popup, Overlay)","created_at":"2025-10-21T20:07:16Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T21:06:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449577023","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449577023"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449577023"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449577023/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":22,"original_line":19,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":21,"position":24,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449579461","pull_request_review_id":3362524289,"id":2449579461,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86SAZ3F","diff_hunk":"@@ -1 +1,179 @@\n-# HAI3\n\\ No newline at end of file\n+# HAI3 UI-Core\n+\n+**Human-driven development, AI-assisted, well structured and polished framework for SaaS control panels**\n+\n+HAI3 UI-Core is a framework that merges AI-assisted UI generation with human craftsmanship, ensuring maintainable, scalable, and visually consistent applications for SaaS multitenant and multi-user control panels.\n+\n+## 🎯 Project Vision\n+\n+The main **HAI3 UI-Core objective** is to achieve the **maximum possible efficiency** of application screens generation by **AI**, while maintaining the **code quality** and **code structure** for future application logic scale.\n+\n+1. **HAI3 UI-core**: Human-driven development, AI-assisted, well structured and polished.\n+2. **Application business screens**: AI-driven development with help of HAI3 UI-core, Human-assisted.\n+\n+## ✨ Features\n+\n+- **TypeScript-first**: Strict typing for better developer experience and code quality\n+- **Modern Stack**: React 18 + Vite + Redux Toolkit + Tailwind CSS\n+- **Modular Architecture**: Screensets as vertical slices, reusable UIKit components\n+- **Layout System**: Complete set of layout components (Header, Footer, Menu, Sidebar, Popup, Overlay)\n+- **Theme Support**: Configurable themes with light/dark mode support\n+- **State Management**: Redux with Flux pattern for shared and private state\n+- **Microfrontend Ready**: Designed for plugin ecosystems and third-party integrations\n+\n+## 📁 Project Structure\n+\n+```\n+HAI3/\n+├── docs/                    # Project documentation\n+│   ├── MANIFEST.md         # Core philosophy and principles\n+│   ├── MODEL.md            # Layout and architecture model\n+│   └── GUIDELINES.md       # Development guidelines\n+├── src/\n+│   ├── core/               # UI Core implementation\n+│   │   ├── layout/         # Layout domain (vertical slice)\n+│   │   │   ├── domains/    # Layout sub-domains\n+│   │   │   │   ├── header/ # Header component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── footer/ # Footer component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── menu/   # Menu component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── sidebar/# Sidebar component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── screen/ # Screen component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── popup/  # Popup component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   └── overlay/# Overlay component + slice\n+│   │   │   ├── Layout.tsx  # Main layout orchestrator\n+│   │   │   └── layoutSlice.ts # Layout-level state\n+│   │   ├── hooks/          # Typed Redux hooks\n+│   │   ├── coreSlice.ts    # Global app state\n+│   │   ├── store.ts        # Redux store configuration\n+│   │   └── types.ts        # Shared type definitions\n+│   ├── uikit/              # Reusable UI components\n+│   │   └── layout/         # Layout components (presentational)\n+│   ├── screensets/         # Application screens (vertical slices)\n+│   │   └── drafts/         # Draft screenset\n+│   │       └── screens/    # Screenset screens (component + slice per screen)\n+│   ├── styles/             # Global styles and themes\n+│   │   └── themes/         # Theme configurations\n+│   └── lib/                # Utility functions\n+├── public/                 # Static assets\n+└── [config files]          # TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind configs\n+```\n+\n+## 🚀 Getting Started\n+\n+### Prerequisites\n+\n+- Node.js 18+ and npm 9+\n+- Git\n+\n+### Installation\n+\n+1. **Clone the repository**\n+   ```bash\n+   git clone <repository-url>","path":"README.md","commit_id":"f38b8ea4ff21969992a181fe6c2a9b0d0c77b677","original_commit_id":"e4e04eabbc3c586ddacf287549928d48e62748ff","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"git clone https://github.com/HAI3org/HAI3","created_at":"2025-10-21T20:08:32Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T21:06:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449579461","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449579461"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449579461"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449579461/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":76,"original_line":72,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":74,"position":78,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449581221","pull_request_review_id":3362524289,"id":2449581221,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86SAaSl","diff_hunk":"@@ -1 +1,179 @@\n-# HAI3\n\\ No newline at end of file\n+# HAI3 UI-Core\n+\n+**Human-driven development, AI-assisted, well structured and polished framework for SaaS control panels**\n+\n+HAI3 UI-Core is a framework that merges AI-assisted UI generation with human craftsmanship, ensuring maintainable, scalable, and visually consistent applications for SaaS multitenant and multi-user control panels.\n+\n+## 🎯 Project Vision\n+\n+The main **HAI3 UI-Core objective** is to achieve the **maximum possible efficiency** of application screens generation by **AI**, while maintaining the **code quality** and **code structure** for future application logic scale.\n+\n+1. **HAI3 UI-core**: Human-driven development, AI-assisted, well structured and polished.\n+2. **Application business screens**: AI-driven development with help of HAI3 UI-core, Human-assisted.\n+\n+## ✨ Features\n+\n+- **TypeScript-first**: Strict typing for better developer experience and code quality\n+- **Modern Stack**: React 18 + Vite + Redux Toolkit + Tailwind CSS\n+- **Modular Architecture**: Screensets as vertical slices, reusable UIKit components\n+- **Layout System**: Complete set of layout components (Header, Footer, Menu, Sidebar, Popup, Overlay)\n+- **Theme Support**: Configurable themes with light/dark mode support\n+- **State Management**: Redux with Flux pattern for shared and private state\n+- **Microfrontend Ready**: Designed for plugin ecosystems and third-party integrations\n+\n+## 📁 Project Structure\n+\n+```\n+HAI3/\n+├── docs/                    # Project documentation\n+│   ├── MANIFEST.md         # Core philosophy and principles\n+│   ├── MODEL.md            # Layout and architecture model\n+│   └── GUIDELINES.md       # Development guidelines\n+├── src/\n+│   ├── core/               # UI Core implementation\n+│   │   ├── layout/         # Layout domain (vertical slice)\n+│   │   │   ├── domains/    # Layout sub-domains\n+│   │   │   │   ├── header/ # Header component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── footer/ # Footer component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── menu/   # Menu component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── sidebar/# Sidebar component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── screen/ # Screen component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── popup/  # Popup component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   └── overlay/# Overlay component + slice\n+│   │   │   ├── Layout.tsx  # Main layout orchestrator\n+│   │   │   └── layoutSlice.ts # Layout-level state\n+│   │   ├── hooks/          # Typed Redux hooks\n+│   │   ├── coreSlice.ts    # Global app state\n+│   │   ├── store.ts        # Redux store configuration\n+│   │   └── types.ts        # Shared type definitions\n+│   ├── uikit/              # Reusable UI components\n+│   │   └── layout/         # Layout components (presentational)\n+│   ├── screensets/         # Application screens (vertical slices)\n+│   │   └── drafts/         # Draft screenset\n+│   │       └── screens/    # Screenset screens (component + slice per screen)\n+│   ├── styles/             # Global styles and themes\n+│   │   └── themes/         # Theme configurations\n+│   └── lib/                # Utility functions\n+├── public/                 # Static assets\n+└── [config files]          # TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind configs\n+```\n+\n+## 🚀 Getting Started\n+\n+### Prerequisites\n+\n+- Node.js 18+ and npm 9+\n+- Git\n+\n+### Installation\n+\n+1. **Clone the repository**\n+   ```bash\n+   git clone <repository-url>\n+   cd HAI3\n+   ```\n+\n+2. **Install dependencies**\n+   ```bash\n+   npm install\n+   ```\n+\n+3. **Start the development server**\n+   ```bash\n+   npm run dev\n+   ```\n+\n+4. **Open your browser**\n+   Navigate to `http://localhost:5173`\n+\n+### Available Scripts\n+\n+- `npm run dev` - Start development server\n+- `npm run build` - Build for production\n+- `npm run preview` - Preview production build\n+- `npm run lint` - Run ESLint\n+- `npm run type-check` - Run TypeScript type checking\n+\n+## 🎨 Layout Components\n+\n+HAI3 provides a complete set of layout components:","path":"README.md","commit_id":"f38b8ea4ff21969992a181fe6c2a9b0d0c77b677","original_commit_id":"e4e04eabbc3c586ddacf287549928d48e62748ff","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"a complete set -> configurable predefined set","created_at":"2025-10-21T20:09:27Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T21:06:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449581221","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449581221"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449581221"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449581221/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":103,"original_line":99,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":101,"position":105,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449585172","pull_request_review_id":3362524289,"id":2449585172,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86SAbQU","diff_hunk":"@@ -1 +1,179 @@\n-# HAI3\n\\ No newline at end of file\n+# HAI3 UI-Core\n+\n+**Human-driven development, AI-assisted, well structured and polished framework for SaaS control panels**\n+\n+HAI3 UI-Core is a framework that merges AI-assisted UI generation with human craftsmanship, ensuring maintainable, scalable, and visually consistent applications for SaaS multitenant and multi-user control panels.\n+\n+## 🎯 Project Vision\n+\n+The main **HAI3 UI-Core objective** is to achieve the **maximum possible efficiency** of application screens generation by **AI**, while maintaining the **code quality** and **code structure** for future application logic scale.\n+\n+1. **HAI3 UI-core**: Human-driven development, AI-assisted, well structured and polished.\n+2. **Application business screens**: AI-driven development with help of HAI3 UI-core, Human-assisted.\n+\n+## ✨ Features\n+\n+- **TypeScript-first**: Strict typing for better developer experience and code quality\n+- **Modern Stack**: React 18 + Vite + Redux Toolkit + Tailwind CSS\n+- **Modular Architecture**: Screensets as vertical slices, reusable UIKit components\n+- **Layout System**: Complete set of layout components (Header, Footer, Menu, Sidebar, Popup, Overlay)\n+- **Theme Support**: Configurable themes with light/dark mode support\n+- **State Management**: Redux with Flux pattern for shared and private state\n+- **Microfrontend Ready**: Designed for plugin ecosystems and third-party integrations\n+\n+## 📁 Project Structure\n+\n+```\n+HAI3/\n+├── docs/                    # Project documentation\n+│   ├── MANIFEST.md         # Core philosophy and principles\n+│   ├── MODEL.md            # Layout and architecture model\n+│   └── GUIDELINES.md       # Development guidelines\n+├── src/\n+│   ├── core/               # UI Core implementation\n+│   │   ├── layout/         # Layout domain (vertical slice)\n+│   │   │   ├── domains/    # Layout sub-domains\n+│   │   │   │   ├── header/ # Header component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── footer/ # Footer component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── menu/   # Menu component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── sidebar/# Sidebar component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── screen/ # Screen component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── popup/  # Popup component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   └── overlay/# Overlay component + slice\n+│   │   │   ├── Layout.tsx  # Main layout orchestrator\n+│   │   │   └── layoutSlice.ts # Layout-level state\n+│   │   ├── hooks/          # Typed Redux hooks\n+│   │   ├── coreSlice.ts    # Global app state\n+│   │   ├── store.ts        # Redux store configuration\n+│   │   └── types.ts        # Shared type definitions\n+│   ├── uikit/              # Reusable UI components\n+│   │   └── layout/         # Layout components (presentational)\n+│   ├── screensets/         # Application screens (vertical slices)\n+│   │   └── drafts/         # Draft screenset\n+│   │       └── screens/    # Screenset screens (component + slice per screen)\n+│   ├── styles/             # Global styles and themes\n+│   │   └── themes/         # Theme configurations\n+│   └── lib/                # Utility functions\n+├── public/                 # Static assets\n+└── [config files]          # TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind configs\n+```\n+\n+## 🚀 Getting Started\n+\n+### Prerequisites\n+\n+- Node.js 18+ and npm 9+\n+- Git\n+\n+### Installation\n+\n+1. **Clone the repository**\n+   ```bash\n+   git clone <repository-url>\n+   cd HAI3\n+   ```\n+\n+2. **Install dependencies**\n+   ```bash\n+   npm install\n+   ```\n+\n+3. **Start the development server**\n+   ```bash\n+   npm run dev\n+   ```\n+\n+4. **Open your browser**\n+   Navigate to `http://localhost:5173`\n+\n+### Available Scripts\n+\n+- `npm run dev` - Start development server\n+- `npm run build` - Build for production\n+- `npm run preview` - Preview production build\n+- `npm run lint` - Run ESLint\n+- `npm run type-check` - Run TypeScript type checking\n+\n+## 🎨 Layout Components\n+\n+HAI3 provides a complete set of layout components:\n+\n+- **Header**: Top navigation bar with logo and actions\n+- **Footer**: Bottom bar with copyright and links\n+- **Menu**: Collapsible navigation menu with nested items\n+- **Sidebar**: Contextual side panels (left or right)\n+- **Popup**: Modal/dialog system with backdrop\n+- **Overlay**: Backdrop for popups and loading states\n+\n+All components are fully typed, themeable, and follow accessibility best practices.\n+\n+## 🏗️ Core Architecture\n+\n+### Redux Store Structure\n+\n+```typescript\n+{\n+  core: {\n+    user: User | null,\n+    tenant: Tenant | null,\n+    loading: boolean,\n+    error: string | null\n+  },\n+  layout: {\n+    menuCollapsed: boolean,\n+    sidebarCollapsed: boolean,\n+    sidebarPosition: 'left' | 'right',\n+    theme: 'light' | 'dark',\n+    popupStack: PopupState[],\n+    overlayVisible: boolean\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Screensets\n+\n+Screensets are vertical slices of your application. Each screenset:","path":"README.md","commit_id":"f38b8ea4ff21969992a181fe6c2a9b0d0c77b677","original_commit_id":"e4e04eabbc3c586ddacf287549928d48e62748ff","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"We'll need to add a description of why screensets are needed in general - the concept was described well in the original HAI3-org/HAI3-poc","created_at":"2025-10-21T20:11:28Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T21:06:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449585172","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449585172"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449585172"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449585172/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":139,"original_line":135,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":137,"position":141,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449586407","pull_request_review_id":3362524289,"id":2449586407,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86SAbjn","diff_hunk":"@@ -1 +1,179 @@\n-# HAI3\n\\ No newline at end of file\n+# HAI3 UI-Core\n+\n+**Human-driven development, AI-assisted, well structured and polished framework for SaaS control panels**\n+\n+HAI3 UI-Core is a framework that merges AI-assisted UI generation with human craftsmanship, ensuring maintainable, scalable, and visually consistent applications for SaaS multitenant and multi-user control panels.\n+\n+## 🎯 Project Vision\n+\n+The main **HAI3 UI-Core objective** is to achieve the **maximum possible efficiency** of application screens generation by **AI**, while maintaining the **code quality** and **code structure** for future application logic scale.\n+\n+1. **HAI3 UI-core**: Human-driven development, AI-assisted, well structured and polished.\n+2. **Application business screens**: AI-driven development with help of HAI3 UI-core, Human-assisted.\n+\n+## ✨ Features\n+\n+- **TypeScript-first**: Strict typing for better developer experience and code quality\n+- **Modern Stack**: React 18 + Vite + Redux Toolkit + Tailwind CSS\n+- **Modular Architecture**: Screensets as vertical slices, reusable UIKit components\n+- **Layout System**: Complete set of layout components (Header, Footer, Menu, Sidebar, Popup, Overlay)\n+- **Theme Support**: Configurable themes with light/dark mode support\n+- **State Management**: Redux with Flux pattern for shared and private state\n+- **Microfrontend Ready**: Designed for plugin ecosystems and third-party integrations\n+\n+## 📁 Project Structure\n+\n+```\n+HAI3/\n+├── docs/                    # Project documentation\n+│   ├── MANIFEST.md         # Core philosophy and principles\n+│   ├── MODEL.md            # Layout and architecture model\n+│   └── GUIDELINES.md       # Development guidelines\n+├── src/\n+│   ├── core/               # UI Core implementation\n+│   │   ├── layout/         # Layout domain (vertical slice)\n+│   │   │   ├── domains/    # Layout sub-domains\n+│   │   │   │   ├── header/ # Header component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── footer/ # Footer component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── menu/   # Menu component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── sidebar/# Sidebar component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── screen/ # Screen component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── popup/  # Popup component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   └── overlay/# Overlay component + slice\n+│   │   │   ├── Layout.tsx  # Main layout orchestrator\n+│   │   │   └── layoutSlice.ts # Layout-level state\n+│   │   ├── hooks/          # Typed Redux hooks\n+│   │   ├── coreSlice.ts    # Global app state\n+│   │   ├── store.ts        # Redux store configuration\n+│   │   └── types.ts        # Shared type definitions\n+│   ├── uikit/              # Reusable UI components\n+│   │   └── layout/         # Layout components (presentational)\n+│   ├── screensets/         # Application screens (vertical slices)\n+│   │   └── drafts/         # Draft screenset\n+│   │       └── screens/    # Screenset screens (component + slice per screen)\n+│   ├── styles/             # Global styles and themes\n+│   │   └── themes/         # Theme configurations\n+│   └── lib/                # Utility functions\n+├── public/                 # Static assets\n+└── [config files]          # TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind configs\n+```\n+\n+## 🚀 Getting Started\n+\n+### Prerequisites\n+\n+- Node.js 18+ and npm 9+\n+- Git\n+\n+### Installation\n+\n+1. **Clone the repository**\n+   ```bash\n+   git clone <repository-url>\n+   cd HAI3\n+   ```\n+\n+2. **Install dependencies**\n+   ```bash\n+   npm install\n+   ```\n+\n+3. **Start the development server**\n+   ```bash\n+   npm run dev\n+   ```\n+\n+4. **Open your browser**\n+   Navigate to `http://localhost:5173`\n+\n+### Available Scripts\n+\n+- `npm run dev` - Start development server\n+- `npm run build` - Build for production\n+- `npm run preview` - Preview production build\n+- `npm run lint` - Run ESLint\n+- `npm run type-check` - Run TypeScript type checking\n+\n+## 🎨 Layout Components\n+\n+HAI3 provides a complete set of layout components:\n+\n+- **Header**: Top navigation bar with logo and actions\n+- **Footer**: Bottom bar with copyright and links\n+- **Menu**: Collapsible navigation menu with nested items\n+- **Sidebar**: Contextual side panels (left or right)\n+- **Popup**: Modal/dialog system with backdrop\n+- **Overlay**: Backdrop for popups and loading states\n+\n+All components are fully typed, themeable, and follow accessibility best practices.\n+\n+## 🏗️ Core Architecture\n+\n+### Redux Store Structure\n+\n+```typescript\n+{\n+  core: {\n+    user: User | null,\n+    tenant: Tenant | null,\n+    loading: boolean,\n+    error: string | null\n+  },\n+  layout: {\n+    menuCollapsed: boolean,\n+    sidebarCollapsed: boolean,\n+    sidebarPosition: 'left' | 'right',\n+    theme: 'light' | 'dark',\n+    popupStack: PopupState[],\n+    overlayVisible: boolean\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Screensets\n+\n+Screensets are vertical slices of your application. Each screenset:\n+- Has its own components and business logic\n+- Can have its own Redux slice\n+- Uses UIKit components for consistency\n+- Is isolated from other screensets\n+\n+## 📖 Development Guidelines\n+\n+Please refer to [docs/GUIDELINES.md](./docs/GUIDELINES.md) for detailed development guidelines including:\n+\n+- TypeScript best practices\n+- Project structure conventions\n+- Component development patterns\n+- State management guidelines\n+- Screenset architecture\n+\n+## 🤝 Contributing\n+\n+Please read [CONTRIBUTING.md](./CONTRIBUTING.md) for details on our code of conduct and the process for submitting pull requests.\n+\n+## 📄 License\n+\n+This project is licensed under the MIT License - see the [LICENSE](./LICENSE) file for details.","path":"README.md","commit_id":"f38b8ea4ff21969992a181fe6c2a9b0d0c77b677","original_commit_id":"e4e04eabbc3c586ddacf287549928d48e62748ff","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Not MIT, Apache 2.0 (!)","created_at":"2025-10-21T20:12:05Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T21:06:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449586407","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449586407"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449586407"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449586407/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":161,"original_line":157,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":159,"position":163,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449587484","pull_request_review_id":3362524289,"id":2449587484,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86SAb0c","diff_hunk":"@@ -1 +1,179 @@\n-# HAI3\n\\ No newline at end of file\n+# HAI3 UI-Core\n+\n+**Human-driven development, AI-assisted, well structured and polished framework for SaaS control panels**\n+\n+HAI3 UI-Core is a framework that merges AI-assisted UI generation with human craftsmanship, ensuring maintainable, scalable, and visually consistent applications for SaaS multitenant and multi-user control panels.\n+\n+## 🎯 Project Vision\n+\n+The main **HAI3 UI-Core objective** is to achieve the **maximum possible efficiency** of application screens generation by **AI**, while maintaining the **code quality** and **code structure** for future application logic scale.\n+\n+1. **HAI3 UI-core**: Human-driven development, AI-assisted, well structured and polished.\n+2. **Application business screens**: AI-driven development with help of HAI3 UI-core, Human-assisted.\n+\n+## ✨ Features\n+\n+- **TypeScript-first**: Strict typing for better developer experience and code quality\n+- **Modern Stack**: React 18 + Vite + Redux Toolkit + Tailwind CSS\n+- **Modular Architecture**: Screensets as vertical slices, reusable UIKit components\n+- **Layout System**: Complete set of layout components (Header, Footer, Menu, Sidebar, Popup, Overlay)\n+- **Theme Support**: Configurable themes with light/dark mode support\n+- **State Management**: Redux with Flux pattern for shared and private state\n+- **Microfrontend Ready**: Designed for plugin ecosystems and third-party integrations\n+\n+## 📁 Project Structure\n+\n+```\n+HAI3/\n+├── docs/                    # Project documentation\n+│   ├── MANIFEST.md         # Core philosophy and principles\n+│   ├── MODEL.md            # Layout and architecture model\n+│   └── GUIDELINES.md       # Development guidelines\n+├── src/\n+│   ├── core/               # UI Core implementation\n+│   │   ├── layout/         # Layout domain (vertical slice)\n+│   │   │   ├── domains/    # Layout sub-domains\n+│   │   │   │   ├── header/ # Header component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── footer/ # Footer component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── menu/   # Menu component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── sidebar/# Sidebar component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── screen/ # Screen component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── popup/  # Popup component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   └── overlay/# Overlay component + slice\n+│   │   │   ├── Layout.tsx  # Main layout orchestrator\n+│   │   │   └── layoutSlice.ts # Layout-level state\n+│   │   ├── hooks/          # Typed Redux hooks\n+│   │   ├── coreSlice.ts    # Global app state\n+│   │   ├── store.ts        # Redux store configuration\n+│   │   └── types.ts        # Shared type definitions\n+│   ├── uikit/              # Reusable UI components\n+│   │   └── layout/         # Layout components (presentational)\n+│   ├── screensets/         # Application screens (vertical slices)\n+│   │   └── drafts/         # Draft screenset\n+│   │       └── screens/    # Screenset screens (component + slice per screen)\n+│   ├── styles/             # Global styles and themes\n+│   │   └── themes/         # Theme configurations\n+│   └── lib/                # Utility functions\n+├── public/                 # Static assets\n+└── [config files]          # TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind configs\n+```\n+\n+## 🚀 Getting Started\n+\n+### Prerequisites\n+\n+- Node.js 18+ and npm 9+\n+- Git\n+\n+### Installation\n+\n+1. **Clone the repository**\n+   ```bash\n+   git clone <repository-url>\n+   cd HAI3\n+   ```\n+\n+2. **Install dependencies**\n+   ```bash\n+   npm install\n+   ```\n+\n+3. **Start the development server**\n+   ```bash\n+   npm run dev\n+   ```\n+\n+4. **Open your browser**\n+   Navigate to `http://localhost:5173`\n+\n+### Available Scripts\n+\n+- `npm run dev` - Start development server\n+- `npm run build` - Build for production\n+- `npm run preview` - Preview production build\n+- `npm run lint` - Run ESLint\n+- `npm run type-check` - Run TypeScript type checking\n+\n+## 🎨 Layout Components\n+\n+HAI3 provides a complete set of layout components:\n+\n+- **Header**: Top navigation bar with logo and actions\n+- **Footer**: Bottom bar with copyright and links\n+- **Menu**: Collapsible navigation menu with nested items\n+- **Sidebar**: Contextual side panels (left or right)\n+- **Popup**: Modal/dialog system with backdrop\n+- **Overlay**: Backdrop for popups and loading states\n+\n+All components are fully typed, themeable, and follow accessibility best practices.\n+\n+## 🏗️ Core Architecture\n+\n+### Redux Store Structure\n+\n+```typescript\n+{\n+  core: {\n+    user: User | null,\n+    tenant: Tenant | null,\n+    loading: boolean,\n+    error: string | null\n+  },\n+  layout: {\n+    menuCollapsed: boolean,\n+    sidebarCollapsed: boolean,\n+    sidebarPosition: 'left' | 'right',\n+    theme: 'light' | 'dark',\n+    popupStack: PopupState[],\n+    overlayVisible: boolean\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Screensets\n+\n+Screensets are vertical slices of your application. Each screenset:\n+- Has its own components and business logic\n+- Can have its own Redux slice\n+- Uses UIKit components for consistency\n+- Is isolated from other screensets\n+\n+## 📖 Development Guidelines\n+\n+Please refer to [docs/GUIDELINES.md](./docs/GUIDELINES.md) for detailed development guidelines including:\n+\n+- TypeScript best practices\n+- Project structure conventions\n+- Component development patterns\n+- State management guidelines\n+- Screenset architecture\n+\n+## 🤝 Contributing\n+\n+Please read [CONTRIBUTING.md](./CONTRIBUTING.md) for details on our code of conduct and the process for submitting pull requests.\n+\n+## 📄 License\n+\n+This project is licensed under the MIT License - see the [LICENSE](./LICENSE) file for details.\n+\n+## 🎯 Roadmap","path":"README.md","commit_id":"d4edce7bdd80e8870b6b23a45fd9476b5472bd67","original_commit_id":"e4e04eabbc3c586ddacf287549928d48e62748ff","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I'd suggest to move Roadmap to docs/ROADMAP.md because it can be large eventually","created_at":"2025-10-21T20:12:37Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T21:06:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449587484","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449587484"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449587484"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449587484/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":159,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":161,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449588128","pull_request_review_id":3362524289,"id":2449588128,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86SAb-g","diff_hunk":"@@ -1 +1,179 @@\n-# HAI3\n\\ No newline at end of file\n+# HAI3 UI-Core\n+\n+**Human-driven development, AI-assisted, well structured and polished framework for SaaS control panels**\n+\n+HAI3 UI-Core is a framework that merges AI-assisted UI generation with human craftsmanship, ensuring maintainable, scalable, and visually consistent applications for SaaS multitenant and multi-user control panels.\n+\n+## 🎯 Project Vision\n+\n+The main **HAI3 UI-Core objective** is to achieve the **maximum possible efficiency** of application screens generation by **AI**, while maintaining the **code quality** and **code structure** for future application logic scale.\n+\n+1. **HAI3 UI-core**: Human-driven development, AI-assisted, well structured and polished.\n+2. **Application business screens**: AI-driven development with help of HAI3 UI-core, Human-assisted.\n+\n+## ✨ Features\n+\n+- **TypeScript-first**: Strict typing for better developer experience and code quality\n+- **Modern Stack**: React 18 + Vite + Redux Toolkit + Tailwind CSS\n+- **Modular Architecture**: Screensets as vertical slices, reusable UIKit components\n+- **Layout System**: Complete set of layout components (Header, Footer, Menu, Sidebar, Popup, Overlay)\n+- **Theme Support**: Configurable themes with light/dark mode support\n+- **State Management**: Redux with Flux pattern for shared and private state\n+- **Microfrontend Ready**: Designed for plugin ecosystems and third-party integrations\n+\n+## 📁 Project Structure\n+\n+```\n+HAI3/\n+├── docs/                    # Project documentation\n+│   ├── MANIFEST.md         # Core philosophy and principles\n+│   ├── MODEL.md            # Layout and architecture model\n+│   └── GUIDELINES.md       # Development guidelines\n+├── src/\n+│   ├── core/               # UI Core implementation\n+│   │   ├── layout/         # Layout domain (vertical slice)\n+│   │   │   ├── domains/    # Layout sub-domains\n+│   │   │   │   ├── header/ # Header component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── footer/ # Footer component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── menu/   # Menu component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── sidebar/# Sidebar component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── screen/ # Screen component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   ├── popup/  # Popup component + slice\n+│   │   │   │   └── overlay/# Overlay component + slice\n+│   │   │   ├── Layout.tsx  # Main layout orchestrator\n+│   │   │   └── layoutSlice.ts # Layout-level state\n+│   │   ├── hooks/          # Typed Redux hooks\n+│   │   ├── coreSlice.ts    # Global app state\n+│   │   ├── store.ts        # Redux store configuration\n+│   │   └── types.ts        # Shared type definitions\n+│   ├── uikit/              # Reusable UI components\n+│   │   └── layout/         # Layout components (presentational)\n+│   ├── screensets/         # Application screens (vertical slices)\n+│   │   └── drafts/         # Draft screenset\n+│   │       └── screens/    # Screenset screens (component + slice per screen)\n+│   ├── styles/             # Global styles and themes\n+│   │   └── themes/         # Theme configurations\n+│   └── lib/                # Utility functions\n+├── public/                 # Static assets\n+└── [config files]          # TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind configs\n+```\n+\n+## 🚀 Getting Started\n+\n+### Prerequisites\n+\n+- Node.js 18+ and npm 9+\n+- Git\n+\n+### Installation\n+\n+1. **Clone the repository**\n+   ```bash\n+   git clone <repository-url>\n+   cd HAI3\n+   ```\n+\n+2. **Install dependencies**\n+   ```bash\n+   npm install\n+   ```\n+\n+3. **Start the development server**\n+   ```bash\n+   npm run dev\n+   ```\n+\n+4. **Open your browser**\n+   Navigate to `http://localhost:5173`\n+\n+### Available Scripts\n+\n+- `npm run dev` - Start development server\n+- `npm run build` - Build for production\n+- `npm run preview` - Preview production build\n+- `npm run lint` - Run ESLint\n+- `npm run type-check` - Run TypeScript type checking\n+\n+## 🎨 Layout Components\n+\n+HAI3 provides a complete set of layout components:\n+\n+- **Header**: Top navigation bar with logo and actions\n+- **Footer**: Bottom bar with copyright and links\n+- **Menu**: Collapsible navigation menu with nested items\n+- **Sidebar**: Contextual side panels (left or right)\n+- **Popup**: Modal/dialog system with backdrop\n+- **Overlay**: Backdrop for popups and loading states\n+\n+All components are fully typed, themeable, and follow accessibility best practices.\n+\n+## 🏗️ Core Architecture\n+\n+### Redux Store Structure\n+\n+```typescript\n+{\n+  core: {\n+    user: User | null,\n+    tenant: Tenant | null,\n+    loading: boolean,\n+    error: string | null\n+  },\n+  layout: {\n+    menuCollapsed: boolean,\n+    sidebarCollapsed: boolean,\n+    sidebarPosition: 'left' | 'right',\n+    theme: 'light' | 'dark',\n+    popupStack: PopupState[],\n+    overlayVisible: boolean\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Screensets\n+\n+Screensets are vertical slices of your application. Each screenset:\n+- Has its own components and business logic\n+- Can have its own Redux slice\n+- Uses UIKit components for consistency\n+- Is isolated from other screensets\n+\n+## 📖 Development Guidelines\n+\n+Please refer to [docs/GUIDELINES.md](./docs/GUIDELINES.md) for detailed development guidelines including:\n+\n+- TypeScript best practices\n+- Project structure conventions\n+- Component development patterns\n+- State management guidelines\n+- Screenset architecture\n+\n+## 🤝 Contributing\n+\n+Please read [CONTRIBUTING.md](./CONTRIBUTING.md) for details on our code of conduct and the process for submitting pull requests.\n+\n+## 📄 License\n+\n+This project is licensed under the MIT License - see the [LICENSE](./LICENSE) file for details.\n+\n+## 🎯 Roadmap\n+\n+- [ ] Add more UIKit components (Button, Input, Card, etc.)\n+- [ ] Implement API layer with typed contracts\n+- [ ] Add authentication and RBAC\n+- [ ] Create theme builder and customization tools\n+- [ ] Implement microfrontend plugin system\n+- [ ] Add i18n/l10n support\n+- [ ] Create testing framework and examples\n+- [ ] Build documentation site\n+- [ ] Add CLI for scaffolding screens and components\n+\n+## 📚 Learn More\n+\n+- [Project Manifest](./docs/MANIFEST.md) - Core philosophy and principles\n+- [Architecture Model](./docs/MODEL.md) - Layout and design model\n+- [Development Guidelines](./docs/GUIDELINES.md) - How to build with HAI3","path":"README.md","commit_id":"c422e99e656d2b74f8412a1fce9e332f566680f8","original_commit_id":"e4e04eabbc3c586ddacf287549928d48e62748ff","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"add docs/ROADMAP.md here","created_at":"2025-10-21T20:12:57Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T21:06:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449588128","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449588128"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449588128"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449588128/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":175,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":177,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449596151","pull_request_review_id":3362524289,"id":2449596151,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86SAd73","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,151 @@\n+# Programming\n+- TypeScript is used as the programming language\n+- Always provide explicit types everywhere and use as strict typing as possible\n+- Use explicit generics when possible\n+- Follow the SOLID and DRY principles\n+\n+# Frameworks\n+- React is used as the framework\n+- shadcn/ui is used for UI components\n+- Tailwind CSS is used for styling\n+\n+# Code structure\n+- **src/** - Source code\n+  - **src/uikit/** - UI Kit: reusable business-logic-free components\n+  - **src/core/** - UI Core: foundational layout, state management, and hooks\n+    - **src/core/layout/** - Layout domain (vertical slice)\n+      - **src/core/layout/domains/[name]/** - Layout domain folders (header, footer, menu, sidebar, screen, popup, overlay)\n+        - **Component.tsx** - Domain component\n+        - **domainSlice.ts** - Domain Redux slice\n+        - **index.ts** - Public API\n+      - **src/core/layout/Layout.tsx** - Main layout orchestrator\n+      - **src/core/layout/layoutSlice.ts** - Layout-level state\n+    - **src/core/coreSlice.ts** - Global app state (user, tenant, loading, error)\n+    - **src/core/store.ts** - Redux store configuration\n+    - **src/core/types.ts** - Shared type definitions\n+    - **src/core/hooks/** - Typed Redux hooks\n+  - **src/screensets/** - UI screensets, each is a vertical slice of the application\n+    - **src/screensets/[name]/screens/[screen]/** - Screenset screen folders\n+      - **ScreenComponent.tsx** - Screen component\n+      - **screenSlice.ts** - Screen Redux slice\n+      - **index.ts** - Public API\n+    - **src/screensets/[name]/data.ts** - Simulated data for the screenset\n+    - **src/screensets/[name]/api.ts** - API simulation layer\n+    - **src/screensets/[name]/store.ts** - Screenset store configuration (optional)\n+  - **src/styles/** - Global styles and theme configurations\n+    - **src/styles/themes/** - Theme definitions\n+    - **src/styles/globals.css** - Global CSS with Tailwind directives\n+  - **src/lib/** - Utility functions\n+  - **src/App.tsx** - Root application component\n+  - **src/main.tsx** - Application entry point\n+\n+# UI Kit\n+- UI Kit is located in the src/uikit folder and is a collection of reusable business-logic-free components\n+- Always build UI screens using the components from UI Kit\n+- If there is no suitable component in UI Kit, then create a new component in UI Kit and use it","path":".ai/GUIDELINES.md","commit_id":"f38b8ea4ff21969992a181fe6c2a9b0d0c77b677","original_commit_id":"e4e04eabbc3c586ddacf287549928d48e62748ff","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This is a bit tricky ... the desired flow must be:\n- if there is no suitable component in UI Kit, then create a new component in the local screenset\n- if this component approved later, it will be moved (as folder move) to the src/uikit","created_at":"2025-10-21T20:16:56Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T21:06:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449596151","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449596151"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449596151"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449596151/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":45,"original_line":45,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":45,"position":45,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449599862","pull_request_review_id":3362524289,"id":2449599862,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86SAe12","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,151 @@\n+# Programming\n+- TypeScript is used as the programming language\n+- Always provide explicit types everywhere and use as strict typing as possible\n+- Use explicit generics when possible\n+- Follow the SOLID and DRY principles\n+\n+# Frameworks\n+- React is used as the framework\n+- shadcn/ui is used for UI components\n+- Tailwind CSS is used for styling\n+\n+# Code structure\n+- **src/** - Source code\n+  - **src/uikit/** - UI Kit: reusable business-logic-free components\n+  - **src/core/** - UI Core: foundational layout, state management, and hooks\n+    - **src/core/layout/** - Layout domain (vertical slice)\n+      - **src/core/layout/domains/[name]/** - Layout domain folders (header, footer, menu, sidebar, screen, popup, overlay)\n+        - **Component.tsx** - Domain component\n+        - **domainSlice.ts** - Domain Redux slice\n+        - **index.ts** - Public API\n+      - **src/core/layout/Layout.tsx** - Main layout orchestrator\n+      - **src/core/layout/layoutSlice.ts** - Layout-level state\n+    - **src/core/coreSlice.ts** - Global app state (user, tenant, loading, error)\n+    - **src/core/store.ts** - Redux store configuration\n+    - **src/core/types.ts** - Shared type definitions\n+    - **src/core/hooks/** - Typed Redux hooks\n+  - **src/screensets/** - UI screensets, each is a vertical slice of the application\n+    - **src/screensets/[name]/screens/[screen]/** - Screenset screen folders\n+      - **ScreenComponent.tsx** - Screen component\n+      - **screenSlice.ts** - Screen Redux slice\n+      - **index.ts** - Public API\n+    - **src/screensets/[name]/data.ts** - Simulated data for the screenset\n+    - **src/screensets/[name]/api.ts** - API simulation layer\n+    - **src/screensets/[name]/store.ts** - Screenset store configuration (optional)\n+  - **src/styles/** - Global styles and theme configurations\n+    - **src/styles/themes/** - Theme definitions\n+    - **src/styles/globals.css** - Global CSS with Tailwind directives\n+  - **src/lib/** - Utility functions\n+  - **src/App.tsx** - Root application component\n+  - **src/main.tsx** - Application entry point\n+\n+# UI Kit\n+- UI Kit is located in the src/uikit folder and is a collection of reusable business-logic-free components\n+- Always build UI screens using the components from UI Kit\n+- If there is no suitable component in UI Kit, then create a new component in UI Kit and use it\n+\n+# UI Core\n+\n+## STRICT RULES\n+1. NO prop drilling - config via Redux only\n+2. Domains are self-contained - own component + slice + config\n+3. Orchestrators accept ONLY `children` - no domain props\n+4. Core domains wrap UI Kit components\n+5. Domains self-hide via `visible` boolean in slice\n+\n+## Domain Pattern\n+```\n+domains/[name]/\n+├── Component.tsx    # useAppSelector(state => state.domainName), if (!visible) return null\n+├── domainSlice.ts   # export types, state interface, actions\n+└── index.ts         # export component, actions, reducer, types\n+```\n+\n+**Type Location:**\n+- Domain types → export from `[domain]Slice.ts`\n+- Global types → `src/core/types.ts`\n+\n+## Required Slice Structure\n+```typescript\n+interface DomainState {\n+  visible: boolean;  // REQUIRED\n+  // config + state\n+}\n+// REQUIRED actions: setDomainConfig, setDomainVisible\n+```\n+\n+## Init Pattern\n+```typescript\n+useEffect(() => dispatch(setDomainConfig({ ...config, visible: true })), []);\n+```\n+\n+## Files\n+- `coreSlice.ts` = global (user, tenant, loading, error)\n+- `store.ts` = combine reducers\n+- `types.ts` = shared types\n+\n+## ❌ FORBIDDEN → ✅ REQUIRED\n+```typescript\n+❌ <Layout headerLogo={x} menuItems={y} />\n+✅ <Layout>{children}</Layout>\n+\n+❌ {showMenu && <Menu />}\n+✅ <Menu /> // self-hides\n+\n+❌ <Menu items={x} collapsed={y} />\n+✅ <Menu /> // reads state.menu\n+\n+❌ const [open, setOpen] = useState(false)\n+✅ dispatch(setMenuConfig({visible: true}))\n+```\n+\n+# UI Screensets\n+- Independent variants in `src/screensets/[name]`\n+- Develop in screenset, not global (unless specified)\n+- Vertical slices = components + logic + data\n+- Build from UI Kit + UI Core","path":".ai/GUIDELINES.md","commit_id":"f38b8ea4ff21969992a181fe6c2a9b0d0c77b677","original_commit_id":"e4e04eabbc3c586ddacf287549928d48e62748ff","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Build from global UI Kit + UI Core, use screenset specific UI Kit draft when required","created_at":"2025-10-21T20:18:50Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T21:06:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449599862","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449599862"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449599862"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449599862/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":106,"original_line":106,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":106,"position":106,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449626296","pull_request_review_id":3362604301,"id":2449626296,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86SAlS4","diff_hunk":"","path":".cursorrules","commit_id":"c422e99e656d2b74f8412a1fce9e332f566680f8","original_commit_id":"e4e04eabbc3c586ddacf287549928d48e62748ff","user":{"login":"xiboliaren","id":192490142,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3kqng","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192490142?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiboliaren","html_url":"https://github.com/xiboliaren","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiboliaren/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiboliaren/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiboliaren/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiboliaren/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiboliaren/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiboliaren/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiboliaren/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiboliaren/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiboliaren/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Why the rules are partially duplicated with docs/GUIDELINES.md? Shouldn't it just refer to docs/GUIDELINES.md?","created_at":"2025-10-21T20:31:05Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T20:40:13Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449626296","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449626296"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449626296"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449626296/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":1,"original_line":1,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":1,"position":1,"subject_type":"file"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449639446","pull_request_review_id":3362604301,"id":2449639446,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86SAogW","diff_hunk":"","path":"tailwind.config.ts","commit_id":"f38b8ea4ff21969992a181fe6c2a9b0d0c77b677","original_commit_id":"e4e04eabbc3c586ddacf287549928d48e62748ff","user":{"login":"xiboliaren","id":192490142,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3kqng","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192490142?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiboliaren","html_url":"https://github.com/xiboliaren","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiboliaren/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiboliaren/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiboliaren/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiboliaren/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiboliaren/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiboliaren/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiboliaren/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiboliaren/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xiboliaren/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Why tailwind.config.js but not tailwind.config..ts is required here? Shouldn't it be just renamed?","created_at":"2025-10-21T20:37:23Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T20:40:13Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449639446","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449639446"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449639446"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449639446/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":1,"original_line":1,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":1,"position":1,"subject_type":"file"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449642280","pull_request_review_id":3362524289,"id":2449642280,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86SApMo","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,151 @@\n+# Programming\n+- TypeScript is used as the programming language\n+- Always provide explicit types everywhere and use as strict typing as possible\n+- Use explicit generics when possible\n+- Follow the SOLID and DRY principles\n+\n+# Frameworks\n+- React is used as the framework\n+- shadcn/ui is used for UI components\n+- Tailwind CSS is used for styling\n+\n+# Code structure\n+- **src/** - Source code\n+  - **src/uikit/** - UI Kit: reusable business-logic-free components\n+  - **src/core/** - UI Core: foundational layout, state management, and hooks\n+    - **src/core/layout/** - Layout domain (vertical slice)\n+      - **src/core/layout/domains/[name]/** - Layout domain folders (header, footer, menu, sidebar, screen, popup, overlay)\n+        - **Component.tsx** - Domain component\n+        - **domainSlice.ts** - Domain Redux slice\n+        - **index.ts** - Public API\n+      - **src/core/layout/Layout.tsx** - Main layout orchestrator\n+      - **src/core/layout/layoutSlice.ts** - Layout-level state\n+    - **src/core/coreSlice.ts** - Global app state (user, tenant, loading, error)\n+    - **src/core/store.ts** - Redux store configuration\n+    - **src/core/types.ts** - Shared type definitions\n+    - **src/core/hooks/** - Typed Redux hooks\n+  - **src/screensets/** - UI screensets, each is a vertical slice of the application\n+    - **src/screensets/[name]/screens/[screen]/** - Screenset screen folders\n+      - **ScreenComponent.tsx** - Screen component\n+      - **screenSlice.ts** - Screen Redux slice\n+      - **index.ts** - Public API\n+    - **src/screensets/[name]/data.ts** - Simulated data for the screenset\n+    - **src/screensets/[name]/api.ts** - API simulation layer\n+    - **src/screensets/[name]/store.ts** - Screenset store configuration (optional)\n+  - **src/styles/** - Global styles and theme configurations\n+    - **src/styles/themes/** - Theme definitions\n+    - **src/styles/globals.css** - Global CSS with Tailwind directives\n+  - **src/lib/** - Utility functions\n+  - **src/App.tsx** - Root application component\n+  - **src/main.tsx** - Application entry point\n+\n+# UI Kit\n+- UI Kit is located in the src/uikit folder and is a collection of reusable business-logic-free components\n+- Always build UI screens using the components from UI Kit\n+- If there is no suitable component in UI Kit, then create a new component in UI Kit and use it\n+\n+# UI Core\n+\n+## STRICT RULES\n+1. NO prop drilling - config via Redux only\n+2. Domains are self-contained - own component + slice + config\n+3. Orchestrators accept ONLY `children` - no domain props\n+4. Core domains wrap UI Kit components\n+5. Domains self-hide via `visible` boolean in slice\n+\n+## Domain Pattern\n+```\n+domains/[name]/\n+├── Component.tsx    # useAppSelector(state => state.domainName), if (!visible) return null\n+├── domainSlice.ts   # export types, state interface, actions\n+└── index.ts         # export component, actions, reducer, types\n+```\n+\n+**Type Location:**\n+- Domain types → export from `[domain]Slice.ts`\n+- Global types → `src/core/types.ts`\n+\n+## Required Slice Structure\n+```typescript\n+interface DomainState {\n+  visible: boolean;  // REQUIRED\n+  // config + state\n+}\n+// REQUIRED actions: setDomainConfig, setDomainVisible\n+```\n+\n+## Init Pattern\n+```typescript\n+useEffect(() => dispatch(setDomainConfig({ ...config, visible: true })), []);\n+```\n+\n+## Files\n+- `coreSlice.ts` = global (user, tenant, loading, error)\n+- `store.ts` = combine reducers\n+- `types.ts` = shared types\n+\n+## ❌ FORBIDDEN → ✅ REQUIRED\n+```typescript\n+❌ <Layout headerLogo={x} menuItems={y} />\n+✅ <Layout>{children}</Layout>\n+\n+❌ {showMenu && <Menu />}\n+✅ <Menu /> // self-hides\n+\n+❌ <Menu items={x} collapsed={y} />\n+✅ <Menu /> // reads state.menu\n+\n+❌ const [open, setOpen] = useState(false)\n+✅ dispatch(setMenuConfig({visible: true}))\n+```\n+\n+# UI Screensets\n+- Independent variants in `src/screensets/[name]`\n+- Develop in screenset, not global (unless specified)\n+- Vertical slices = components + logic + data\n+- Build from UI Kit + UI Core\n+\n+## Screenset Pattern\n+```\n+screensets/[name]/screens/[screen]/\n+├── ScreenComponent.tsx\n+├── screenSlice.ts\n+└── index.ts\n+data.ts     # simulated data\n+api.ts      # API simulation layer\n+store.ts    # optional: combine reducers\n+```\n+\n+## Screenset Rules\n+- Export slices with \"Slice\" suffix\n+- Screensets READ core state, cannot MODIFY\n+- No data sharing between screensets\n+- Can use global actions/data\n+\n+# Rules\n+\n+## Styles\n+- Support themes in `/src/styles/themes`\n+- Use existing styles first\n+- Add to ALL themes if new style needed\n+\n+## Screens\n+- NO hardcoded screenset names\n+- NO `if screenset ==` in shared logic\n+\n+## TypeScript\n+- Types for ALL variables, params, returns\n+- Export types with component\n+- `type` for objects, `interface` for props\n+- NEVER `any`, use `unknown`\n+- Use enums for string constants - NO hardcoded strings\n+  - Define in slice file (vertical slice approach)\n+  - ❌ `theme: 'light' | 'dark'` → ✅ `theme: Theme` (from layoutSlice)\n+  - ❌ `name: 'menu'` → ✅ `name: LayoutDomains.Menu` (from layoutSlice)\n+  - Domain enums → export from `[domain]Slice.ts`\n+\n+# Draft Screenset (`src/screensets/drafts`)\n+- Mockups = wireframes, not pixel-perfect","path":".ai/GUIDELINES.md","commit_id":"f38b8ea4ff21969992a181fe6c2a9b0d0c77b677","original_commit_id":"e4e04eabbc3c586ddacf287549928d48e62748ff","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"It's better to distinguish terms - Draft screens vs Mockups. They are different, see HAPI-poc/README.md\n\nactually no, should pretty pixel perfect, just not final\nThe idea of dratf screens is to get the first draft versions quickly, including the layout and visualization ideas, such as colors/fonts/icons/paddings/sizes/ etc","created_at":"2025-10-21T20:38:49Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T21:06:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449642280","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449642280"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449642280"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449642280/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":148,"original_line":148,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":148,"position":148,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449645240","pull_request_review_id":3362524289,"id":2449645240,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86SAp64","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,151 @@\n+# Programming\n+- TypeScript is used as the programming language\n+- Always provide explicit types everywhere and use as strict typing as possible\n+- Use explicit generics when possible\n+- Follow the SOLID and DRY principles\n+\n+# Frameworks\n+- React is used as the framework\n+- shadcn/ui is used for UI components\n+- Tailwind CSS is used for styling\n+\n+# Code structure\n+- **src/** - Source code\n+  - **src/uikit/** - UI Kit: reusable business-logic-free components\n+  - **src/core/** - UI Core: foundational layout, state management, and hooks\n+    - **src/core/layout/** - Layout domain (vertical slice)\n+      - **src/core/layout/domains/[name]/** - Layout domain folders (header, footer, menu, sidebar, screen, popup, overlay)\n+        - **Component.tsx** - Domain component\n+        - **domainSlice.ts** - Domain Redux slice\n+        - **index.ts** - Public API\n+      - **src/core/layout/Layout.tsx** - Main layout orchestrator\n+      - **src/core/layout/layoutSlice.ts** - Layout-level state\n+    - **src/core/coreSlice.ts** - Global app state (user, tenant, loading, error)\n+    - **src/core/store.ts** - Redux store configuration\n+    - **src/core/types.ts** - Shared type definitions\n+    - **src/core/hooks/** - Typed Redux hooks\n+  - **src/screensets/** - UI screensets, each is a vertical slice of the application\n+    - **src/screensets/[name]/screens/[screen]/** - Screenset screen folders\n+      - **ScreenComponent.tsx** - Screen component\n+      - **screenSlice.ts** - Screen Redux slice\n+      - **index.ts** - Public API\n+    - **src/screensets/[name]/data.ts** - Simulated data for the screenset\n+    - **src/screensets/[name]/api.ts** - API simulation layer\n+    - **src/screensets/[name]/store.ts** - Screenset store configuration (optional)\n+  - **src/styles/** - Global styles and theme configurations\n+    - **src/styles/themes/** - Theme definitions\n+    - **src/styles/globals.css** - Global CSS with Tailwind directives\n+  - **src/lib/** - Utility functions\n+  - **src/App.tsx** - Root application component\n+  - **src/main.tsx** - Application entry point\n+\n+# UI Kit\n+- UI Kit is located in the src/uikit folder and is a collection of reusable business-logic-free components\n+- Always build UI screens using the components from UI Kit\n+- If there is no suitable component in UI Kit, then create a new component in UI Kit and use it\n+\n+# UI Core\n+\n+## STRICT RULES\n+1. NO prop drilling - config via Redux only\n+2. Domains are self-contained - own component + slice + config\n+3. Orchestrators accept ONLY `children` - no domain props\n+4. Core domains wrap UI Kit components\n+5. Domains self-hide via `visible` boolean in slice\n+\n+## Domain Pattern\n+```\n+domains/[name]/\n+├── Component.tsx    # useAppSelector(state => state.domainName), if (!visible) return null\n+├── domainSlice.ts   # export types, state interface, actions\n+└── index.ts         # export component, actions, reducer, types\n+```\n+\n+**Type Location:**\n+- Domain types → export from `[domain]Slice.ts`\n+- Global types → `src/core/types.ts`\n+\n+## Required Slice Structure\n+```typescript\n+interface DomainState {\n+  visible: boolean;  // REQUIRED\n+  // config + state\n+}\n+// REQUIRED actions: setDomainConfig, setDomainVisible\n+```\n+\n+## Init Pattern\n+```typescript\n+useEffect(() => dispatch(setDomainConfig({ ...config, visible: true })), []);\n+```\n+\n+## Files\n+- `coreSlice.ts` = global (user, tenant, loading, error)\n+- `store.ts` = combine reducers\n+- `types.ts` = shared types\n+\n+## ❌ FORBIDDEN → ✅ REQUIRED\n+```typescript\n+❌ <Layout headerLogo={x} menuItems={y} />\n+✅ <Layout>{children}</Layout>\n+\n+❌ {showMenu && <Menu />}\n+✅ <Menu /> // self-hides\n+\n+❌ <Menu items={x} collapsed={y} />\n+✅ <Menu /> // reads state.menu\n+\n+❌ const [open, setOpen] = useState(false)\n+✅ dispatch(setMenuConfig({visible: true}))\n+```\n+\n+# UI Screensets\n+- Independent variants in `src/screensets/[name]`\n+- Develop in screenset, not global (unless specified)\n+- Vertical slices = components + logic + data\n+- Build from UI Kit + UI Core\n+\n+## Screenset Pattern\n+```\n+screensets/[name]/screens/[screen]/\n+├── ScreenComponent.tsx\n+├── screenSlice.ts\n+└── index.ts\n+data.ts     # simulated data\n+api.ts      # API simulation layer\n+store.ts    # optional: combine reducers\n+```\n+\n+## Screenset Rules\n+- Export slices with \"Slice\" suffix\n+- Screensets READ core state, cannot MODIFY\n+- No data sharing between screensets\n+- Can use global actions/data\n+\n+# Rules\n+\n+## Styles\n+- Support themes in `/src/styles/themes`\n+- Use existing styles first\n+- Add to ALL themes if new style needed\n+\n+## Screens\n+- NO hardcoded screenset names\n+- NO `if screenset ==` in shared logic\n+\n+## TypeScript\n+- Types for ALL variables, params, returns\n+- Export types with component\n+- `type` for objects, `interface` for props\n+- NEVER `any`, use `unknown`\n+- Use enums for string constants - NO hardcoded strings\n+  - Define in slice file (vertical slice approach)\n+  - ❌ `theme: 'light' | 'dark'` → ✅ `theme: Theme` (from layoutSlice)\n+  - ❌ `name: 'menu'` → ✅ `name: LayoutDomains.Menu` (from layoutSlice)\n+  - Domain enums → export from `[domain]Slice.ts`\n+\n+# Draft Screenset (`src/screensets/drafts`)\n+- Mockups = wireframes, not pixel-perfect\n+- Stickers: GREEN=behavior, YELLOW=hints, ORANGE=add functionality\n+- Multiple mockups = different states","path":".ai/GUIDELINES.md","commit_id":"f38b8ea4ff21969992a181fe6c2a9b0d0c77b677","original_commit_id":"e4e04eabbc3c586ddacf287549928d48e62748ff","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Multiple drafts = different states","created_at":"2025-10-21T20:40:03Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T21:06:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449645240","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449645240"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449645240"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449645240/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":150,"original_line":150,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":150,"position":150,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449648829","pull_request_review_id":3362524289,"id":2449648829,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86SAqy9","diff_hunk":"@@ -1 +1,179 @@\n-# HAI3\n\\ No newline at end of file\n+# HAI3 UI-Core\n+\n+**Human-driven development, AI-assisted, well structured and polished framework for SaaS control panels**\n+\n+HAI3 UI-Core is a framework that merges AI-assisted UI generation with human craftsmanship, ensuring maintainable, scalable, and visually consistent applications for SaaS multitenant and multi-user control panels.","path":"README.md","commit_id":"f38b8ea4ff21969992a181fe6c2a9b0d0c77b677","original_commit_id":"e4e04eabbc3c586ddacf287549928d48e62748ff","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"There was more text and definitions, including the embedded diagram... I will add it later","created_at":"2025-10-21T20:41:36Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T21:06:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449648829","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449648829"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449648829"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449648829/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":8,"original_line":5,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":7,"position":10,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449650178","pull_request_review_id":3362524289,"id":2449650178,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86SArIC","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,312 @@\n+# HAI3 UI-Core Quick Start Guide\n+\n+This guide will help you get started with HAI3 UI-Core development.\n+\n+## Installation\n+\n+1. **Install dependencies**\n+   ```bash\n+   npm install\n+   ```\n+\n+2. **Start development server**\n+   ```bash\n+   npm run dev\n+   ```\n+\n+3. **Open browser**\n+   Navigate to `http://localhost:5173`\n+\n+## Project Structure Overview\n+\n+```\n+src/\n+├── core/               # Core UI implementation\n+│   ├── layout/         # CoreLayout component\n+│   ├── store/          # Redux store (global state)\n+│   └── hooks/          # Typed Redux hooks\n+├── uikit/              # Reusable UI components\n+│   └── layout/         # Layout components (Header, Footer, Menu, etc.)\n+├── screensets/         # Application screens\n+│   └── drafts/         # Draft screens for development","path":"QUICK_START.md","commit_id":"f38b8ea4ff21969992a181fe6c2a9b0d0c77b677","original_commit_id":"e4e04eabbc3c586ddacf287549928d48e62748ff","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"|-- mockups/\n|-- production/\n","created_at":"2025-10-21T20:42:18Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T21:06:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449650178","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449650178"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449650178"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449650178/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":34,"original_line":31,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":31,"position":34,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449655264","pull_request_review_id":3362524289,"id":2449655264,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86SAsXg","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,312 @@\n+# HAI3 UI-Core Quick Start Guide\n+\n+This guide will help you get started with HAI3 UI-Core development.\n+\n+## Installation\n+\n+1. **Install dependencies**\n+   ```bash\n+   npm install\n+   ```\n+\n+2. **Start development server**\n+   ```bash\n+   npm run dev\n+   ```\n+\n+3. **Open browser**\n+   Navigate to `http://localhost:5173`\n+\n+## Project Structure Overview\n+\n+```\n+src/\n+├── core/               # Core UI implementation\n+│   ├── layout/         # CoreLayout component\n+│   ├── store/          # Redux store (global state)\n+│   └── hooks/          # Typed Redux hooks\n+├── uikit/              # Reusable UI components\n+│   └── layout/         # Layout components (Header, Footer, Menu, etc.)\n+├── screensets/         # Application screens\n+│   └── drafts/         # Draft screens for development\n+├── styles/             # Global styles and themes\n+└── lib/                # Utility functions\n+```\n+\n+## Creating Your First Screen\n+\n+1. **Create a new screen file**\n+   ```bash\n+   # Create in src/screensets/drafts/\n+   touch src/screensets/drafts/MyScreen.tsx\n+   ```\n+\n+2. **Write your screen component**\n+   ```typescript\n+   import React from 'react';\n+\n+   export const MyScreen: React.FC = () => {\n+     return (\n+       <div className=\"p-6\">\n+         <h1 className=\"text-2xl font-bold\">My Screen</h1>\n+         <p>Content goes here</p>\n+       </div>\n+     );\n+   };\n+   ```\n+\n+3. **Use it in App.tsx**\n+   ```typescript\n+   import { MyScreen } from '@/screensets/drafts/MyScreen';\n+\n+   // In your CoreLayout children\n+   <MyScreen />\n+   ```\n+\n+## Using Layout Components\n+\n+### Header\n+```typescript\n+<Header \n+  logo={<Logo />}\n+  actions={<UserMenu />}\n+/>\n+```\n+\n+### Menu\n+```typescript\n+const menuItems: MenuItem[] = [\n+  {\n+    id: 'home',\n+    label: 'Home',\n+    icon: <HomeIcon />,\n+  },\n+];\n+\n+<Menu items={menuItems} collapsed={false} />\n+```\n+\n+### Sidebar\n+```typescript\n+<Sidebar \n+  position=\"left\"\n+  title=\"Sidebar Title\"\n+  collapsed={false}\n+>\n+  <div>Sidebar content</div>\n+</Sidebar>\n+```\n+\n+### Popup\n+```typescript\n+const [open, setOpen] = useState(false);\n+\n+<Popup\n+  open={open}\n+  onClose={() => setOpen(false)}\n+  title=\"My Popup\"\n+>\n+  <div>Popup content</div>\n+</Popup>\n+```\n+\n+## Using Redux State\n+\n+### Read state\n+```typescript\n+import { useAppSelector } from '@/core/hooks/useRedux';\n+\n+const MyComponent = () => {\n+  const layout = useAppSelector(state => state.layout);\n+  const user = useAppSelector(state => state.core.user);\n+  \n+  return <div>Menu collapsed: {layout.menuCollapsed}</div>;\n+};\n+```\n+\n+### Dispatch actions\n+```typescript\n+import { useAppDispatch } from '@/core/hooks/useRedux';\n+import { toggleMenu, setUser } from '@/core/store';\n+\n+const MyComponent = () => {\n+  const dispatch = useAppDispatch();\n+  \n+  const handleToggle = () => {\n+    dispatch(toggleMenu());\n+  };\n+  \n+  return <button onClick={handleToggle}>Toggle Menu</button>;\n+};\n+```\n+\n+## Styling with Tailwind\n+\n+HAI3 uses Tailwind CSS with custom theme tokens:\n+\n+```typescript\n+<div className=\"bg-background text-foreground\">\n+  <h1 className=\"text-2xl font-bold text-primary\">Title</h1>\n+  <p className=\"text-muted-foreground\">Description</p>\n+</div>\n+```\n+\n+### Available Theme Colors\n+- `background` - Main background\n+- `foreground` - Main text color\n+- `primary` - Primary brand color\n+- `secondary` - Secondary color\n+- `accent` - Accent color\n+- `muted` - Muted color\n+- `border` - Border color","path":"QUICK_START.md","commit_id":"f38b8ea4ff21969992a181fe6c2a9b0d0c77b677","original_commit_id":"e4e04eabbc3c586ddacf287549928d48e62748ff","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Need more for backgrounds and borders I believe...\nso better to use:\n\nbg-***\ntext-***\nborder-***\n...\n\nneed to check what is the ideomatic way","created_at":"2025-10-21T20:44:46Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T21:06:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449655264","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449655264"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449655264"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449655264/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":164,"original_line":161,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":161,"position":164,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449659424","pull_request_review_id":3362524289,"id":2449659424,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86SAtYg","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,312 @@\n+# HAI3 UI-Core Quick Start Guide\n+\n+This guide will help you get started with HAI3 UI-Core development.\n+\n+## Installation\n+\n+1. **Install dependencies**\n+   ```bash\n+   npm install\n+   ```\n+\n+2. **Start development server**\n+   ```bash\n+   npm run dev\n+   ```\n+\n+3. **Open browser**\n+   Navigate to `http://localhost:5173`\n+\n+## Project Structure Overview\n+\n+```\n+src/\n+├── core/               # Core UI implementation\n+│   ├── layout/         # CoreLayout component\n+│   ├── store/          # Redux store (global state)\n+│   └── hooks/          # Typed Redux hooks\n+├── uikit/              # Reusable UI components\n+│   └── layout/         # Layout components (Header, Footer, Menu, etc.)\n+├── screensets/         # Application screens\n+│   └── drafts/         # Draft screens for development\n+├── styles/             # Global styles and themes\n+└── lib/                # Utility functions\n+```\n+\n+## Creating Your First Screen\n+\n+1. **Create a new screen file**\n+   ```bash\n+   # Create in src/screensets/drafts/\n+   touch src/screensets/drafts/MyScreen.tsx\n+   ```\n+\n+2. **Write your screen component**\n+   ```typescript\n+   import React from 'react';\n+\n+   export const MyScreen: React.FC = () => {\n+     return (\n+       <div className=\"p-6\">\n+         <h1 className=\"text-2xl font-bold\">My Screen</h1>\n+         <p>Content goes here</p>\n+       </div>\n+     );\n+   };\n+   ```\n+\n+3. **Use it in App.tsx**\n+   ```typescript\n+   import { MyScreen } from '@/screensets/drafts/MyScreen';\n+\n+   // In your CoreLayout children\n+   <MyScreen />\n+   ```\n+\n+## Using Layout Components\n+\n+### Header\n+```typescript\n+<Header \n+  logo={<Logo />}\n+  actions={<UserMenu />}\n+/>\n+```\n+\n+### Menu\n+```typescript\n+const menuItems: MenuItem[] = [\n+  {\n+    id: 'home',\n+    label: 'Home',\n+    icon: <HomeIcon />,\n+  },\n+];\n+\n+<Menu items={menuItems} collapsed={false} />\n+```","path":"QUICK_START.md","commit_id":"f38b8ea4ff21969992a181fe6c2a9b0d0c77b677","original_commit_id":"e4e04eabbc3c586ddacf287549928d48e62748ff","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I didn't get how to link a screen to a menu item","created_at":"2025-10-21T20:46:42Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T21:06:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449659424","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449659424"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449659424"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449659424/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":90,"original_line":87,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":87,"position":90,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449680718","pull_request_review_id":3362524289,"id":2449680718,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86SAylO","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,151 @@\n+# Programming\n+- TypeScript is used as the programming language\n+- Always provide explicit types everywhere and use as strict typing as possible\n+- Use explicit generics when possible\n+- Follow the SOLID and DRY principles\n+\n+# Frameworks\n+- React is used as the framework\n+- shadcn/ui is used for UI components\n+- Tailwind CSS is used for styling\n+\n+# Code structure\n+- **src/** - Source code\n+  - **src/uikit/** - UI Kit: reusable business-logic-free components\n+  - **src/core/** - UI Core: foundational layout, state management, and hooks\n+    - **src/core/layout/** - Layout domain (vertical slice)\n+      - **src/core/layout/domains/[name]/** - Layout domain folders (header, footer, menu, sidebar, screen, popup, overlay)\n+        - **Component.tsx** - Domain component\n+        - **domainSlice.ts** - Domain Redux slice\n+        - **index.ts** - Public API\n+      - **src/core/layout/Layout.tsx** - Main layout orchestrator\n+      - **src/core/layout/layoutSlice.ts** - Layout-level state\n+    - **src/core/coreSlice.ts** - Global app state (user, tenant, loading, error)\n+    - **src/core/store.ts** - Redux store configuration\n+    - **src/core/types.ts** - Shared type definitions\n+    - **src/core/hooks/** - Typed Redux hooks\n+  - **src/screensets/** - UI screensets, each is a vertical slice of the application\n+    - **src/screensets/[name]/screens/[screen]/** - Screenset screen folders\n+      - **ScreenComponent.tsx** - Screen component\n+      - **screenSlice.ts** - Screen Redux slice\n+      - **index.ts** - Public API\n+    - **src/screensets/[name]/data.ts** - Simulated data for the screenset\n+    - **src/screensets/[name]/api.ts** - API simulation layer\n+    - **src/screensets/[name]/store.ts** - Screenset store configuration (optional)\n+  - **src/styles/** - Global styles and theme configurations\n+    - **src/styles/themes/** - Theme definitions\n+    - **src/styles/globals.css** - Global CSS with Tailwind directives\n+  - **src/lib/** - Utility functions\n+  - **src/App.tsx** - Root application component\n+  - **src/main.tsx** - Application entry point\n+\n+# UI Kit\n+- UI Kit is located in the src/uikit folder and is a collection of reusable business-logic-free components\n+- Always build UI screens using the components from UI Kit\n+- If there is no suitable component in UI Kit, then create a new component in UI Kit and use it\n+\n+# UI Core\n+\n+## STRICT RULES\n+1. NO prop drilling - config via Redux only\n+2. Domains are self-contained - own component + slice + config\n+3. Orchestrators accept ONLY `children` - no domain props\n+4. Core domains wrap UI Kit components\n+5. Domains self-hide via `visible` boolean in slice\n+\n+## Domain Pattern\n+```\n+domains/[name]/\n+├── Component.tsx    # useAppSelector(state => state.domainName), if (!visible) return null\n+├── domainSlice.ts   # export types, state interface, actions\n+└── index.ts         # export component, actions, reducer, types\n+```\n+\n+**Type Location:**\n+- Domain types → export from `[domain]Slice.ts`\n+- Global types → `src/core/types.ts`\n+\n+## Required Slice Structure\n+```typescript\n+interface DomainState {\n+  visible: boolean;  // REQUIRED\n+  // config + state\n+}\n+// REQUIRED actions: setDomainConfig, setDomainVisible\n+```\n+\n+## Init Pattern\n+```typescript\n+useEffect(() => dispatch(setDomainConfig({ ...config, visible: true })), []);\n+```\n+\n+## Files\n+- `coreSlice.ts` = global (user, tenant, loading, error)\n+- `store.ts` = combine reducers\n+- `types.ts` = shared types\n+\n+## ❌ FORBIDDEN → ✅ REQUIRED\n+```typescript\n+❌ <Layout headerLogo={x} menuItems={y} />\n+✅ <Layout>{children}</Layout>\n+\n+❌ {showMenu && <Menu />}\n+✅ <Menu /> // self-hides\n+\n+❌ <Menu items={x} collapsed={y} />\n+✅ <Menu /> // reads state.menu\n+\n+❌ const [open, setOpen] = useState(false)\n+✅ dispatch(setMenuConfig({visible: true}))\n+```\n+\n+# UI Screensets\n+- Independent variants in `src/screensets/[name]`\n+- Develop in screenset, not global (unless specified)\n+- Vertical slices = components + logic + data\n+- Build from UI Kit + UI Core\n+\n+## Screenset Pattern\n+```\n+screensets/[name]/screens/[screen]/\n+├── ScreenComponent.tsx\n+├── screenSlice.ts\n+└── index.ts\n+data.ts     # simulated data\n+api.ts      # API simulation layer\n+store.ts    # optional: combine reducers\n+```\n+\n+## Screenset Rules\n+- Export slices with \"Slice\" suffix\n+- Screensets READ core state, cannot MODIFY\n+- No data sharing between screensets\n+- Can use global actions/data\n+\n+# Rules\n+\n+## Styles\n+- Support themes in `/src/styles/themes`\n+- Use existing styles first\n+- Add to ALL themes if new style needed","path":".ai/GUIDELINES.md","commit_id":"f38b8ea4ff21969992a181fe6c2a9b0d0c77b677","original_commit_id":"e4e04eabbc3c586ddacf287549928d48e62748ff","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I'd some notes about the tailwind rules in a separate file, e.g.:\n\n-----\n\n# Tailwind CSS Rules for Consistency\n\n## Design Tokens\n- Always use values defined in `tailwind.config.{js,ts}`.\n- Colors must use theme tokens (`text-primary`, `bg-secondary`, `border-muted`), never raw hex codes.\n- Font sizes should come from the theme scale (`text-sm`, `text-base`, `text-lg`), avoid arbitrary pixel sizes.\n- Spacing should only use Tailwind spacing units (`p-4`, `m-2`, `gap-6`), not `px-[7px]` unless approved.\n\n## Layout & Responsiveness\n- Default layout orientation is mobile-first.\n- Always structure responsive classes incrementally (`sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`).\n- Never apply more than one width definition without breakpoints (e.g. avoid both `w-1/2` and `w-full` on the same element).\n\n## Reusable Components\n- Extract repeated class groups into `@layer components` and apply `@apply` for cleanliness:\n```\n@layer components {\n    .btn-primary {\n        @apply bg-blue-500 text-white px-4 py-2 rounded-md hover:bg-blue-600;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n- When generating new components, prefer reusing design tokens over custom colors or measurements.\n\n## Accessibility & State Variants\n- Interactive elements must have hover and focus states:\n```\n<button class=\"bg-primary hover:bg-primary/90 focus:ring-2 focus:ring-primary/40\">Save</button>\n```\n- Disabled states use `opacity-50` and `cursor-not-allowed`.\n\n## Shadows, Borders & Radii\n- Use Tailwind’s predefined tokens (`shadow-sm`, `rounded-md`, `border-gray-200`), not arbitrary values.\n- Never mix multiple radius classes on one component.\n\n## Flex & Grid Structure\n- Use consistent layout utilities:\n- For flex: `flex items-center justify-between gap-2`\n- For grid: `grid gap-4 grid-cols-[1fr_2fr]`\n- Preserve alignment principles — always pair layout utilities (e.g. `flex` with `items-center`).\n\n## Animations & Transitions\n- Use standardized animations and durations (`transition-colors duration-300`).\n- Custom animations must live inside `@keyframes` in `tailwind.config` or theme extension.\n\n## Avoid\n- Raw inline styles (`style=` attributes).\n- Arbitrary non-token values (`text-[#123456]`).\n- Overloaded class strings beyond 12 utilities per element.\n\n---\n# AI Behavior Notes\n- When generating new UI elements, infer design semantics from tokens (e.g. `primary`, `secondary`).\n- Default button = `.btn-primary`; secondary variant = `.btn-secondary`.\n- Prefer structural hierarchy over inline display utilities.","created_at":"2025-10-21T20:56:38Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T21:06:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449680718","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449680718"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449680718"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449680718/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":130,"original_line":130,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":130,"position":130,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449688033","pull_request_review_id":3362524289,"id":2449688033,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86SA0Xh","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@\n+# Model\n+\n+## Glossary\n+\n+- Screen-set","path":"docs/MODEL.md","commit_id":"f38b8ea4ff21969992a181fe6c2a9b0d0c77b677","original_commit_id":"e4e04eabbc3c586ddacf287549928d48e62748ff","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"- Draft screen-set - a screenset primarily generated by LLM after prompts, used to see the options, can be any code\n- Mockup screen-set - a screenset polished by designers, not perfect code inside, matches the key visual guidelines (layout/tailwind/ui-kit)\n- Production screen-set - a screenset polished by developers, fully matches visual guidelines (layout/tailwind/ui-kit) AND development guidelines\n","created_at":"2025-10-21T20:59:25Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T21:06:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449688033","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449688033"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449688033"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449688033/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":8,"original_line":5,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":5,"position":8,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449719860","pull_request_review_id":3362729502,"id":2449719860,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86SA8I0","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,159 @@\n+import React, { useEffect } from 'react';\n+import { Layout } from '@/core/layout';\n+import { DemoScreen } from '@/screensets/drafts/DemoScreen';\n+import { useAppDispatch } from '@/core/hooks/useRedux';\n+import {\n+  setHeaderConfig,\n+  setFooterConfig,\n+  setMenuConfig,\n+  type MenuItem,\n+} from '@/core/store';\n+\n+/**\n+ * Main HAI3 Application Component\n+ * Initializes layout domain configurations via Redux\n+ */\n+\n+const menuItems: MenuItem[] = [\n+  {\n+    id: 'home',\n+    label: 'Home',\n+    icon: (\n+      <svg\n+        width=\"20\"\n+        height=\"20\"\n+        viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"\n+        fill=\"none\"\n+        stroke=\"currentColor\"\n+        strokeWidth=\"2\"\n+        strokeLinecap=\"round\"\n+        strokeLinejoin=\"round\"\n+      >\n+        <path d=\"m3 9 9-7 9 7v11a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2z\" />\n+        <polyline points=\"9 22 9 12 15 12 15 22\" />\n+      </svg>\n+    ),\n+  },\n+  {\n+    id: 'screens',","path":"src/App.tsx","commit_id":"f38b8ea4ff21969992a181fe6c2a9b0d0c77b677","original_commit_id":"e4e04eabbc3c586ddacf287549928d48e62748ff","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The screen-set switcher must not be in the menu, because every screenset populates menu separately, so that every screenset can have very different menu items\n\nin the HAI3-poc it was in the right top corner (check the version)","created_at":"2025-10-21T21:14:22Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T21:14:27Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449719860","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449719860"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pull/1#discussion_r2449719860"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/1"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449719860/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":38,"original_line":38,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":38,"position":38,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-frontx/pulls/comments/2449821692","pull_request_review_id":3362878523,"id":2449821692,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQBxSA86SBU_8","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,159 @@\n+import React, { useEffect } from 'react';\n+import { Layout } from '@/core/layout';\n+import { DemoScreen } from '@/screensets/drafts/DemoScreen';\n+import { useAppDispatch } from '@/core/hooks/useRedux';\n+import {\n+  setHeaderConfig,\n+  setFooterConfig,\n+  setMenuConfig,\n+  type MenuItem,\n+} from '@/core/store';\n+\n+/**\n+ * Main HAI3 Application Component\n+ * Initializes layout domain configurations via Redux\n+ */\n+\n+const menuItems: MenuItem[] = [\n+  {\n+    id: 'home',\n+    label: 'Home',\n+    icon: (\n+      <svg\n+        width=\"20\"\n+        height=\"20\"\n+        viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"\n+        fill=\"none\"\n+        stroke=\"currentColor\"\n+        strokeWidth=\"2\"\n+        strokeLinecap=\"round\"\n+        strokeLinejoin=\"round\"\n+      >\n+        <path d=\"m3 9 9-7 9 7v11a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2z\" />\n+        <polyline points=\"9 22 9 12 15 12 15 22\" />\n+      </svg>\n+    ),\n+  },\n+  {\n+    id: 'screens',\n+    label: 'Screens',\n+    icon: (\n+      <svg\n+        width=\"20\"\n+        height=\"20\"\n+        viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"\n+        fill=\"none\"\n+        stroke=\"currentColor\"\n+        strokeWidth=\"2\"\n+        strokeLinecap=\"round\"\n+        strokeLinejoin=\"round\"\n+      >\n+        <rect width=\"18\" height=\"18\" x=\"3\" y=\"3\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\" />\n+        <line x1=\"9\" x2=\"9\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"21\" />\n+      </svg>\n+    ),\n+    children: [\n+      { id: 'drafts', label: 'Drafts' },\n+      { id: 'mockups', label: 'Mockups' },\n+      { id: 'production', label: 'Production' },\n+    ],\n+  },\n+  {\n+    id: 'components',\n+    label: 'Components',\n+    icon: (\n+      <svg\n+        width=\"20\"\n+        height=\"20\"\n+        viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"\n+        fill=\"none\"\n+        stroke=\"currentColor\"\n+        strokeWidth=\"2\"\n+        strokeLinecap=\"round\"\n+        strokeLinejoin=\"round\"\n+      >\n+        <path d=\"M12 2v20M2 12h20\" />\n+      </svg>\n+    ),\n+  },\n+  {\n+    id: 'settings',\n+    label: 'Settings',\n+    icon: (\n+      <svg\n+        width=\"20\"\n+        height=\"20\"\n+        viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"\n+        fill=\"none\"\n+        stroke=\"currentColor\"\n+        strokeWidth=\"2\"\n+        strokeLinecap=\"round\"\n+        strokeLinejoin=\"round\"\n+      >\n+        <path d=\"M12.22 2h-.44a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v.18a2 2 0 0 1-1 1.73l-.43.25a2 2 0 0 1-2 0l-.15-.08a2 2 0 0 0-2.73.73l-.22.38a2 2 0 0 0 .73 2.73l.15.1a2 2 0 0 1 1 1.72v.51a2 2 0 0 1-1 1.74l-.15.09a2 2 0 0 0-.73 2.73l.22.38a2 2 0 0 0 2.73.73l.15-.08a2 2 0 0 1 2 0l.43.25a2 2 0 0 1 1 1.73V20a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h.44a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-.18a2 2 0 0 1 1-1.73l.43-.25a2 2 0 0 1 2 0l.15.08a2 2 0 0 0 2.73-.73l.22-.39a2 2 0 0 0-.73-2.73l-.15-.08a2 2 0 0 1-1-1.74v-.5a2 2 0 0 1 1-1.74l.15-.09a2 2 0 0 0 .73-2.73l-.22-.38a2 2 0 0 0-2.73-.73l-.15.08a2 2 0 0 1-2 0l-.43-.25a2 2 0 0 1